 earlier reply references riffing on Bloodborne.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T17:32:10-07:00","id":1443957,"title":"","content":"It wasn\u2019t supposed to be like the Morpheans, I just really like Bloodborne and physically astral projection back into the real world is a big part. [legion] and Morphean are a common fail state of the legacy I would expect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T17:47:17-07:00","id":1443959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1443956#post1443956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/114668-ask-a-simple-question-awakened-edition?p=1443298#post1443298\">Simple Question thread</a>, preceding this thread's creation, which is why my earlier reply references riffing on Bloodborne.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, looks like I know what books to read next now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T17:56:26-07:00","id":1443961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1443959#post1443959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, looks like I know what books to read next now...</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m assuming you mean the Bloodborne books, they were kinda weird, but the game was amazing, and the lore was awesome. If you can get the game, ( it\u2019s PlayStation exclusive) it is worth every cent and second and then some. The books were mostly concerned with references to the game rather than building on it. Maybe some of the later ones were better, I didn\u2019t try them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T18:21:30-07:00","id":1443963,"title":"","content":"No, actually I was talking about the CofD books (Dark Eras 2, etc). I didn\u2019t even know Bloodborne had a book form!<br /> <br /> Anyways, I haven\u2019t played Bloodborne yet (though my father probably will...), I\u2019ve read the lore stuff on the net. Especially the spoiler-y stuff. It seems there\u2019s a discrepancy between what the Korean fanwiki thinks of a certain entity\u2019s identity and what the English fandom thinks,<br /> <br /> ... but I digress. If we\u2019re talking about Bloodborne in Mage, it feels like the Hunters could be some weird variant of Proximi. If DnD 5E, then anything goes, right? Oh, and I hear Scion\u2019s new edition is getting a Cthulu Mythos in its supplements - when that comes out, you might want to check it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T18:38:37-07:00","id":1443965,"title":"","content":"I personally would use a variant of deviant for Bloodborne, but hunter would work too. I probably need to check scion anyways, but now I\u2019m out of book money. *looks at Satchel*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T12:13:47-07:00","id":1444049,"title":"","content":"I am musing over some potential names, does a different name for the guardian version and the free council version seem like a good idea? The guardian potential name would be the \u201cdisciples of Mauma\u201d. That\u2019s the same monster that inspired the Inguma beast family. I think the guardian legacy should be related to that type of beast for theme and general logical sense. Looks like the French name for it would be \u201cadeptes d\u2019lnguma\u201d? I\u2019m not sure if I\u2019m comfortable with using anyone\u2019s mythology, even if Wikipedia says nobody practices it anymore.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I\u2019m going to be busy the next few days, but I should be able to finish on Sunday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-15-2021, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T21:11:30-07:00","id":1444130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1444049#post1444049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am musing over some potential names, does a different name for the guardian version and the free council version seem like a good idea? The guardian potential name would be the \u201cdisciples of Mauma\u201d. That\u2019s the same monster that inspired the Inguma beast family. I think the guardian legacy should be related to that type of beast for theme and general logical sense. Looks like the French name for it would be \u201cadeptes d\u2019lnguma\u201d? I\u2019m not sure if I\u2019m comfortable with using anyone\u2019s mythology, even if Wikipedia says nobody practices it anymore.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I\u2019m going to be busy the next few days, but I should be able to finish on Sunday.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A sleep paralysis demon? Sounds good for emulating Bloodborne and/or exploring dreams and the Astral and/or factoring in Beast, but sounds a bit off for the &quot;liberate the self&quot; aspect. That could also be the in-universe reason why Libertine members want to change the name... But at the same time, Libertines are also big on drawing from human culture, so maybe they aren't fussy about it after all.<br /> <br /> For mythological names, well, we already have the Fangs of Mara (a Legacy) apparently not knowing whether their name is from the Buddhist arch-demon or the Germanic nightmare spirits, and not particularly caring about it (since both makes sense for them), so a little liberty with names it should be okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T22:01:40-07:00","id":1444132,"title":"","content":"The idea was that it was kinda a dream demon thing, referencing the main point of the legacy. I somehow didn\u2019t realize the sleep paralysis connection. I like the name less now. I guess I\u2019m trying to find a doppelg\u00e4nger like being to reference, or anything about living dreams. Actually the faceless ghosts yokai, may make more sense. Or maybe I\u2019m going in another weird direction. I don\u2019t know, it\u2019s late and I\u2019m probably too picky about names.<br /> <br /> edit: had a idea for the free council name, something about the pool of Narcissus. The idea is the free council see the reflection as the dream self, or something. It\u2019s really late, and I\u2019ll work on it tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-16-2021, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T19:30:43-07:00","id":1444587,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm almost done with it. These things are a massive amount of work. I really respect anyone who does this a lot. Thanks everyone for all the advice.<br /> <br /> edit: I\u2019m done for the day and nearly finished. As always comments and concerns are welcome.<br /> I\u2019m probably going to start working on my next legacy, but no commitments to when that will be. The idea is a Prime legacy devoted to the idea of insight and power at the cost of the mages health, granted by the Aeon of Prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-19-2021, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-11T08:10:34-07:00","id":1448217,"title":"","content":"Well, I\u2019m back, mostly. I still have a heavy workload, but I can fit in some legacy creation in my schedule now. I have five legacies I plan to make, and I would like some help deciding which I should do first. These are all in various states of completion in my head, so your mileage may vary.<br /> The options are:<br /> Prime focused legacy that turns the mental addiction to mystery into a literal one in return for power and knowledge. No name yet, please say something if you have a idea for one. Edit: (Something to do with the hanged man tarot or Odin\u2019s sacrifice of a eye? Sacrifice for knowledge is a key theme)<br /> The Singers in Silence redone for 2e, Death/Fate.<br /> The Tamers of Roots, a Thyrsus Matter/Life legacy focused on potions and supernatural chemical knowledge.<br /> The Estatic Circle, the decedents of the Tamers of Roots focused on the insights their altered perceptions bring.<br /> The Gunslingers, (again please suggest a better name) a legacy focused on the duel and stand off mechanics in dark eras 2. Time/Prime, probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-11-2021, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T13:33:44-07:00","id":1448614,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay, some unexpected things came up, along with some things I totally forgot about, but should have remembered. Anyway, I'm starting with the Singers in Silence, because they are somewhat easy to convert to 2e. I'm about a third of the way done, but I ran out of time today, and wanted something done by today, so here we are. Edit: and I ran out of time again.. I will work on it later today. Edit the second: nearly done, now needs refinement. Final edits!<br /> <br /> Thank you everyone that helped me with this, especially proindrakenzol who suggested many of the final attainments, and provided some nice flavor text. the parts in quotes is their writing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Singers in Silence</b></span><br /> <br /> She always had a smile for every occasion, and could halt the world with the beauty in her songs. Now that smile is long gone, but she can still bring tears to your eyes when she sings. She sings now for the funeral service, and all who hear it seem to find some measure of comfort there.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">A Song for The Dead</span></b><br /> <br /> In ancient times, people died. They were mourned through tears and wails, thorough story and song. Over time, the role fell to fairy women who came to mourn the passing of lives. Some families even came to have their own bean s\u03afdhe, or banshee, to presage their own death. The Singers in Silence were born of that grief and loss, to know the truths of the passage of those we hold dear.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Arcanthus, Mysterium<br /> <b>Background</b>: The Banshees come from no single background. Most experience a great tragedy just before they enter the legacy.<br /> <b>Appearances</b>: Those that take on this legacy grow skeletally thin, as if eaten away by hunger. Their features become sunken, their bodies bony, and many grow deathly pale.<br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Banshee<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Death 2, Fate 1, Empathy 2<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: After a tragic loss, a initiate must spend a day fasting. Upon the final hour they must find their way to a place of death and silence, and must listen with mage sight. If they are open, they will start to hear the melodies that will haunt them until the end of their days.<br /> <b>Organization</b>: Really intense Master student chains.<br /> <b>Theory</b>: Death comes for everyone, eventually. The Singers in Silence sing songs of mourning, so we all can let go.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>: Death<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: (In a place of Death (graveyard, funeral home, etc) +1); (On someone Fated to die within the next 24 day +2); (Succeed on a expression roll related to the spell+2); (With a corpse +1, performing a funeral service +2 )<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: Singing; Creating Laments ; Preparing a Body for a Funeral ; Ritual Prayers for the Departed; Performing Euthanasia<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">First: The Knowing</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation.<br /> The Banshee sees the Dead and the Doomed. She may see and speak with the dead, even in Twilight. The Banshee can focus on a single ghost and reveal the number of Anchors the ghost has, along with Rank of the ghost. Furthermore, the Banshee knows if any within her perceptions are fated or cursed to die within the next day. The knowledge comes unbidden, it cannot be wished away or easily ignored. This perception is distracting, if there are more ghosts or doomed individuals within the Banshee\u2019s senses than the Banshee\u2019s Gnosis + Composure, she takes a -2 penalty to any extended action rolls . The Storyteller may rule that a particular ghost is being more or less distracting, raising or lowing the effective amount ghosts present in the area.<br /> <br /> Permanent Speak with the Dead, with a side of Doom seeing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Second: The Seeing</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Death 2, Expression 2, Empathy 3<br /> The songs of death and doom flow into the Banshee\u2019s soul. When touching a corpse, a Banshee may activate this attainment to see<br /> the circumstances behind a persons doom, even knowledge of what the doomed person saw and felt in their final moments. This knowledge takes the form of a keening song, a story of fated demise. If the Banshee wishes, she may gain a positive condition related towards singing the death song of the departed soul.<br /> <br /> Forensic Gaze, reach towards instant and seeing through the dead\u2019s eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Fate 2.<br /> The Banshee being associated with ill omen, can insulate herself from false Fate.<br /> <br /> Warding Gesture, with reach towards advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Third: The Calling</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Death 3, Empathy 3, Expression 3<br /> &quot;The Singer's song calls to the dead, and draws them to her; ghosts, zombies, vampires, and other restless dead that can hear the Singer's haunting melody and have Rank or Composure lower than the Singer's dots in Death are compelled to travel towards the Singer by the fastest safe route possible, whether the affected undead is willingly or forcefully drawn to the Singer their impression level starts one higher than normal.&quot; &quot;In addition, those in mourning that hear the song have the sharpness of their pain blunted, allowing fond memories of the deceased to come to the fore and for the bereaved to come to terms with their loss more quickly.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ghost Lure with reach towards first impression and advanced scale: area<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Fate 3<br /> A Singer\u2019s song may provide a measure of Fortune. Those that accept the Singer\u2019s blessings are insulated from their dooms, with a clash of wills from the Singer for Fate to see their Fate triggers.<br /> <br /> Fabricate Fortune, with reach toward instant cast, and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Fourth: The Releasing</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Death 4, Empathy 4.<br /> &quot;Some ghosts are reticent to move on to the afterlife and they cling desperately to the material world by possessing people, places, or objects that they should not. The Singer's song can bring such ghosts back from madness and allow them to move on to the Underworld. After a scene of performing the Singer strips away a number of Manifestation Conditions from a ghost or its host equal to the Singer's dots in Death, this is Withstood by the ghost's Rank. The ghost cannot reestablish these Manifestation Conditions while the Singer continues singing, but the Singer must make a Stamina + Expression roll for each minute they sing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Exorcism with the reach to not allow the ghost to reestablish manifestation conditions<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Fate 4<br /> The Singer's songs may carry a bitter tone, and ill fortune befalls any that invoke the Banshee's rancor. This melody of ill tidings causes the Dooms of all who hear it to trigger, and individuals cursed have their Curses trigger. Even those insignificant to Fate find their accidents harder to overcome, taking the Singers\u2019 Death? extra damage, or intensifying their negative conditions and counting as doomed to Fate effects, including the Singer\u2019s Knowing. This lasts while the Singer continues to sing, but the Singer must make a Stamina + Expression roll for each minute they sing. Those with a Composure equal to the Singer\u2019s dots in Death are immune as are those under the Singer\u2019s third attainment effects.<br /> <br /> Grave Misfortune with a reach towards advanced scale and a reach to trigger the dooms<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Fifth: The Keening</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Death 5, Expression 4<br /> Although ghosts truly do not belong in this world, the Singers know the dead must sometimes linger in this world to complete important tasks. A Singer may use this Attainment to sing or cry out a wordless lament, marking those of her choice that hear her voice. Those that bear this mark linger as ghosts when they die. Singer's are informed of the marked ones doom as if they were always within sensory range of the first attainment. She may also use this attainment on the recently dead, either at the physical remains or the location that they died at, to raise a ghost as if they had been marked. These ghosts are not under the mages control, but start with a higher awareness of their situation than normal ghosts of their rank. The ghosts are here to fulfill any remaining business, and have the minimum anchors appropriate for such.<br /> <br /> Linger with reach toward advanced scale: targets, sensory range, instant cast, and advanced duration<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Fate 5<br /> The Singers are masters of dooms, with a heart felt song of sorrow, they may free bound ephemeral entities, or souls, change the effects of active hexes, modify or negate an oath or other supernatural agreement reinforced by fate, change or dispel a conditional trigger, or modify a subjects Doom.<br /> <br /> When the subject is a ghost, one more option appears. With the ghost's cooperation, the Singer may let a Ghost Move On, regardless of the remaining requirements a ghost may have before they can do so. This allows ghosts, who by chance or fate couldn't finish their business, the chance to properly move on. The Attainment truly lifts all fetters that could stop the ghost from truly moving on, whatever they fate may now be. Many Singers believe that the dead unerringly find their rest in the Supernal Realms, but none can say for sure.<br /> <br /> Sever Oaths with reach towards lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-17-2021, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T15:26:41-07:00","id":1448628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448614#post1448614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">First: The Knowing</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation.<br /> The Banshee <b>Permanently </b>has Death Active Mage Sight activated, with no cost. This combines with The Eyes of the Dead Death 2 Attainment to mean the Banshee sees ghosts and souls in Twilight. She may speak with the dead, even in Twilight. Furthermore, the Banshee knows if any within her perceptions are fated or cursed to die within the next day. The knowledge comes unbidden, it cannot be wished away or easily ignored.<br /> <br /> This is in my opinion the best way to replicate their iconic power. I\u2019m leaving out the distraction penalty, storytellers can determine that for themselves. Semi replicates speak with the dead, but doesn\u2019t show rank or allow speaking with ghosts that don\u2019t speak your language.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Speak With Dead</i> without the reach option also doesn't allow speaking with ghosts that don't speak your language.<br /> <br /> Always on Active Mage Sight has significant drawbacks: -2 to <i>all</i> rolls unrelated to perceiving or using magic (much harsher than the distraction of the 1e version, which only penalizes things requiring &quot;significant concentration) and it leaves you perpetually susceptible to Nimbus Tilts.<br /> <br /> <i>Speak With Dead</i> with reach for Advanced Duration (thus requiring a scene of prep time to activate), the knowledge of whether any in her perception are fated or cursed to die within 24 hours, and a -2 penalty to Extended Actions while in the presence of more Ghosts and/or doomed individuals than their Composure + Gnosis rating more closely aligns with the 1e version of the power.<br /> <br /> There's no real reason to restrict the ability to see the Rank of a Ghost.<br /> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Second: The Calling</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Death 2, Expression 2<br /> When she wills it, the Singer\u2019s voice conveys haunting power. The Banshee sings a song that resonates with the dead. When activating the Attainment while singing, all Ghosts who can hear her voice are beckoned to approach as if by Lure/Repel. The Ghosts that do treat the Banshee as having Good first impression for Social maneuvering, and must stay until the end of the song.<br /> <br /> Ghost Lure with reach towards first impression. </div> </div> </div>As written this requires a scene of Activation, lasts for only a few turns, only works on weak ghosts, and has almost no range at all. You're also trying to replicate <i>Ghost Summons</i> (a Perfecting spell) with <i>Lure and Repel</i> (a Ruling spell).<br /> <br /> <i>Forensic Gaze</i> with Instant cast and the ability to witness the final moments might be good here; <i>Ghost Shield</i> could also be a good choice to protect from dangerous ghosts you might encounter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Optional</b>: Fate 2.<br /> The Banshee may raise both her Death and Fate mage armor at the same time, and gains her Fate dots in General Armor when she does so.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a bit ambivalent about the fate optional, the extra Fate armor is from the original version, but I\u2019m not sure it\u2019s in theme. </div> </div> </div>All the Arcana defensive spells provided Armor rating in 1e, in 2e they work differently. While allowing both Death and Fate Mage Armor to be up at the same time is... fine? I think <i>Warding Gesture</i> with Advanced Duration makes more sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third Attainment </div> </div> </div><i>Lure</i> would work well here, I would do Advanced Scale: Area and good first impression, lasting for as long as the Singer sings:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Singer's song calls to the dead, and draws them to her; ghosts, zombies, vampires, and other restless dead that can hear the Singer's haunting melody and have Rank or Composure lower than the Singer's dots in Death are compelled to travel towards the Singer by the fastest safe route possible, whether the affected undead is willingly or forcefully drawn to the Singer their impression level starts one higher than normal.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third alt </div> </div> </div><i>Fabricate Fortune</i> with Instant cast and Advanced Duration probably works best here, allowing the Singer to hide a target from the conditions that will cause their Death or misfortune.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fourth Attainment </div> </div> </div><i>Ghosts Summons </i>with Instant cast, Open Condition, and a modification so that its duration is for as long as the Singer is singing (basically concentration, if they're disrupted the effect ends).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fourth alt </div> </div> </div><i>Grave Misfortune</i> with Instant cast and Advanced area with the same &quot;while they hear the Singer singing&quot; caveat as above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fifth Attainment </div> </div> </div>A Death Patterning spell with Sensory Range and Advanced Duration that makes it so that if the target is capable of leaving a ghost behind when they die they do so as long as they die within the Mage's Death dots on the Advanced Duration chart.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fifth alt </div> </div> </div><i>Sever Oaths</i> with reach for Lasting, maybe? Since it can modify rather than simply remove.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-15-2021, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T21:34:30-07:00","id":1448652,"title":"","content":"Well I'm back from work early with a sinus headache, so hopefully I won't be super tired when writing this. Much later: yeah, I got too tired to continue . I'm going to post this now, and clear up any problems tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Speak With Dead</i> without the reach option also doesn't allow speaking with ghosts that don't speak your language.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, for some reason, felt like I should mention that it wasn't using that reach, I see that was a mistake. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Always on Active Mage Sight has significant drawbacks: -2 to <i>all</i> rolls unrelated to perceiving or using magic (much harsher than the distraction of the 1e version, which only penalizes things requiring &quot;significant concentration) and it leaves you perpetually susceptible to Nimbus Tilts.</div> </div> </div> </div> Completely forgot about Nimbus Tilts, and and the penalty to everything. So much for being clever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Speak With Dead</i> with reach for Advanced Duration (thus requiring a scene of prep time to activate), the knowledge of whether any in her perception are fated or cursed to die within 24 hours, and a -2 penalty to Extended Actions while in the presence of more Ghosts and/or doomed individuals than their Composure + Gnosis rating more closely aligns with the 1e version of the power.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that would work better, except I feel this should be always on. That's why I tried to finagle something out of Death Mage Sight, I feel the only acceptable version of the Singers needs the always on version to fit the themes of the legacy. I feel like it would not be appropriate to have the first attainment be always on if it is a spell. Messing with Mage sight seems well within the bounds of strange attainments. If it absolutely will not fit in the first attainment, I will put it in the second attainment, even though that will irk me almost as bad as it not being always active.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no real reason to restrict the ability to see the Rank of a Ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>.Again, that was me noting the differences. Why I thought that necessary is beyond me now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As written this requires a scene of Activation, lasts for only a few turns, only works on weak ghosts, and has almost no range at all. You're also trying to replicate <i>Ghost Summons</i> (a Perfecting spell) with <i>Lure and Repel</i> (a Ruling spell).</div> </div> </div> </div> I was not trying to replicate Ghost Summons, somewhat. The legacy is thematically made to treat the dead with a gentler hand then most other Death legacies. I wanted the ability to set down a beacon for lack of a better word, not yank every ghost around into seeing seeing the mage. The point is that there is a Choice involved. I am certainly moving this to third attainment, as you pointed out, the spell is weak right here.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Forensic Gaze</i> with Instant cast and the ability to witness the final moments might be good here; <i>Ghost Shield</i> could also be a good choice to protect from dangerous ghosts you might encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would go with Forensic Gaze, but as you mention, both would work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the Arcana defensive spells provided Armor rating in 1e, in 2e they work differently. While allowing both Death and Fate Mage Armor to be up at the same time is... fine? I think <i>Warding Gesture</i> with Advanced Duration makes more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will admit a lack of experience with Fate, and 1e. How does warding gesture work? I'm unclear what warrants a change in fate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Lure</i> would work well here, I would do Advanced Scale: Area and good first impression, lasting for as long as the Singer sings:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Singer's song calls to the dead, and draws them to her; ghosts, zombies, vampires, and other restless dead that can hear the Singer's haunting melody and have Rank or Composure lower than the Singer's dots in Death are compelled to travel towards the Singer by the fastest safe route possible, whether the affected undead is willingly or forcefully drawn to the Singer their impression level starts one higher than normal.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, that is good. Can the conditional duration Fate 2 Attainment be added to this, to extend duration to the length of the song?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Fabricate Fortune</i> with Instant cast and Advanced Duration probably works best here, allowing the Singer to hide a target from the conditions that will cause their Death or misfortune.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wait, does Fabricate Fortune do anything besides hide someone's Fate? I'm not seeing the point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Ghosts Summons </i>with Instant cast, Open Condition, and a modification so that its duration is for as long as the Singer is singing (basically concentration, if they're disrupted the effect ends).</div> </div> </div> </div> I think Lure does everything the legacy needs in the ghost department. I would put something related to helping people grieve here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Grave Misfortune</i> with Instant cast and Advanced area with the same &quot;while they hear the Singer singing&quot; caveat as above.</div> </div> </div> </div> Seems good, since their song sometimes bring bad luck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Death Patterning spell with Sensory Range and Advanced Duration that makes it so that if the target is capable of leaving a ghost behind when they die they do so as long as they die within the Mage's Death dots on the Advanced Duration chart.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wouldn't that be Ruling? People (and things) leaves ghosts when they die, under certain circumstances. Surely Ruling could make the person produce a ghost despite not having the right conditions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448628#post1448628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Sever Oaths</i> with reach for Lasting, maybe? Since it can modify rather than simply remove.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what a final attainment should be.<br /> <br /> Things I want from the legacy:<br /> have attainments making them the unhappy constant medium, it informed so much about the legacy.<br /> have attainments related to their role as grief counselor/ helping people let go and grieve. <br /> have attainments that deal with the dead in gentle fashion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-15T23:51:01-07:00","id":1448660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448652#post1448652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I'm back from work early with a sinus headache, so hopefully I won't be super tired when writing this. Much later: yeah, I got too tired to continue . I'm going to post this now, and clear up any problems tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Yeah, for some reason, felt like I should mention that it wasn't using that reach, I see that was a mistake.<br /> <br /> Completely forgot about Nimbus Tilts, and and the penalty to everything. So much for being clever.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that would work better, except I feel this should be always on. That's why I tried to finagle something out of Death Mage Sight, I feel the only acceptable version of the Singers needs the always on version to fit the themes of the legacy. I feel like it would not be appropriate to have the first attainment be always on if it is a spell. Messing with Mage sight seems well within the bounds of strange attainments. If it absolutely will not fit in the first attainment, I will put it in the second attainment, even though that will irk me almost as bad as it not being always active.<br /> <br /> <br /> .Again, that was me noting the differences. Why I thought that necessary is beyond me now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would just make it always on with the drawback from the 1e version of the Legacy. For all practical purposes, self-buff Legacy Attainments with Advanced Duration and primary factor Duration are &quot;always on,&quot; making it always active isn't really a buff, and the distraction penalty can be genuine drawback that is also quite flavorful. Knowing the Ghost's rank should probably be left in, it doesn't really affect anything one way or the other and there's already a drawback (though not a punishing one).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was not trying to replicate Ghost Summons, somewhat. The legacy is thematically made to treat the dead with a gentler hand then most other Death legacies. I wanted the ability to set down a beacon for lack of a better word, not yank every ghost around into seeing seeing the mage. The point is that there is a Choice involved. I am certainly moving this to third attainment, as you pointed out, the spell is weak right here.<br /> I would go with Forensic Gaze, but as you mention, both would work. </div> </div> </div>I'd tie the <i>Forensic Gaze</i> to something thematic, like when the Singer touches the corpse and activates this power they sing the death song (how they died, what they saw, &amp;c) of the corpse for all to hear. It's cool, it's creepy, and it's in theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will admit a lack of experience with Fate, and 1e. How does warding gesture work? I'm unclear what warrants a change in fate. </div> </div> </div>Mucking with your Destiny (including forcing one on you), trying to bind you to an Oath unwillingly, any form of mind control, and any Hex would provoke a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yep, that is good. Can the conditional duration Fate 2 Attainment be added to this, to extend duration to the length of the song? </div> </div> </div>It would require a Mana and would add three levels to the Duration (&quot;stop singing&quot; is a common condition); personally I would just allow the effect to last for as long as the Singer sings without having to worry about anything else, it's not a huge power bump and is very in line with the Singer's theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait, does Fabricate Fortune do anything besides hide someone's Fate? I'm not seeing the point. </div> </div> </div>It can also &quot;trick&quot; Fate based triggers. If someone were, say, cursed to die if they crossed paths with a black cat, this would allow you to make it so that for the duration of the Legacy Attainment if the subject crossed paths with a black cat there would be a Clash of Wills to &quot;hide&quot; the subject from the trigger.<br /> <br /> The Singer sings a song that hides the subject from Doom and Destiny, basically.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think Lure does everything the legacy needs in the ghost department. I would put something related to helping people grieve here. </div> </div> </div>I would tack the following onto the Third Attainment: &quot;In addition, those in mourning that hear the song have the sharpness of their pain blunted, allowing fond memories of the deceased to come to the fore and for the bereaved to come to terms with their loss more quickly.&quot;<br /> <br /> For the Fourth, maybe <i>Exorcism</i> with the +1 Reach option and duration of while singing?<br /> <br /> &quot;Some ghosts are reticent to move on to the afterlife and they cling desperately to the material world by possessing people, places, or objects that they should not. The Singer's song can bring such ghosts back from madness and allow them to move on to the Underworld. After a scene of performing the Singer strips away a number of Manifestation Conditions from a ghost or its host equal to the Singer's dots in Death, this is Withstood by the ghost's Rank. The ghost cannot reestablish these Manifestation Conditions while the Singer continues singing, but the Singer must make a Stamina + Expression roll for each minute they sing.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seems good, since their song sometimes bring bad luck. </div> </div> </div>I tried to go with something more flavorful than just the straight bashing damage from 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wouldn't that be Ruling? People (and things) leaves ghosts when they die, under certain circumstances. Surely Ruling could make the person produce a ghost despite not having the right conditions. </div> </div> </div>I feel like it's Patterning, but if the consensus is that it's Ruling I'd tack on Advanced Scale: Targets and Instant cast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure what a final attainment should be. </div> </div> </div><i>Sever Oaths</i> can also free bound entities and change someone's Doom, I think it's appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Things I want from the legacy:<br /> have attainments making them the unhappy constant medium, it informed so much about the legacy.<br /> have attainments related to their role as grief counselor/ helping people let go and grieve.<br /> have attainments that deal with the dead in gentle fashion. </div> </div> </div>I think I hit all those points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T07:17:57-07:00","id":1448683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would just make it always on with the drawback from the 1e version of the Legacy. For all practical purposes, self-buff Legacy Attainments with Advanced Duration and primary factor Duration are &quot;always on,&quot; making it always active isn't really a buff, and the distraction penalty can be genuine drawback that is also quite flavorful. Knowing the Ghost's rank should probably be left in, it doesn't really affect anything one way or the other and there's already a drawback (though not a punishing one).</div> </div> </div> </div> Alright, I will do that. My only issue with it then is penalty from 1e was a little strange, being both non scaling, and having a resistance of Gnosis + Composure. I would like if the dead are being quite today, or one ghost is sobbing loudly right next to the Singer having different values for the resistance. The intrusive thoughts style, doomed individual knowledge is fine having a value of one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd tie the <i>Forensic Gaze</i> to something thematic, like when the Singer touches the corpse and activates this power they sing the death song (how they died, what they saw, &amp;c) of the corpse for all to hear. It's cool, it's creepy, and it's in theme.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, it really is. Could the Singer gain Inspiration or a positive condition related to singing their funeral song? I think it would be a nice touch. Either that or start the helping people cope with there loss here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mucking with your Destiny (including forcing one on you), trying to bind you to an Oath unwillingly, any form of mind control, and any Hex would provoke a Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm, that\u2019s actually neat. How common is ones Fate being manipulated though? Later thought: if even half of the superstitions about things causing bad luck are true, then this could be very useful indeed. Fate Mage Armor really coves this angle, but I\u2019m probably still going to keep this here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would require a Mana and would add three levels to the Duration (&quot;stop singing&quot; is a common condition); personally I would just allow the effect to last for as long as the Singer sings without having to worry about anything else, it's not a huge power bump and is very in line with the Singer's theme.</div> </div> </div> </div> Perfect then, I won\u2019t need to mess with that. I really like the Stamina + Expression rolls you mentioned later, I will probably put that a side note in every power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can also &quot;trick&quot; Fate based triggers. If someone were, say, cursed to die if they crossed paths with a black cat, this would allow you to make it so that for the duration of the Legacy Attainment if the subject crossed paths with a black cat there would be a Clash of Wills to &quot;hide&quot; the subject from the trigger.<br /> <br /> The Singer sings a song that hides the subject from Doom and Destiny, basically.</div> </div> </div> </div> That\u2019s neat. What\u2019s the difference besides practice between Warding Gesture and Fabricate Fortune?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would tack the following onto the Third Attainment: &quot;In addition, those in mourning that hear the song have the sharpness of their pain blunted, allowing fond memories of the deceased to come to the fore and for the bereaved to come to terms with their loss more quickly.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Agreed. Any converted version of the Singers needs this line somewhere. Third attainment is a good spot for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Fourth, maybe <i>Exorcism</i> with the +1 Reach option and duration of while singing?<br /> <br /> &quot;Some ghosts are reticent to move on to the afterlife and they cling desperately to the material world by possessing people, places, or objects that they should not. The Singer's song can bring such ghosts back from madness and allow them to move on to the Underworld. After a scene of performing the Singer strips away a number of Manifestation Conditions from a ghost or its host equal to the Singer's dots in Death, this is Withstood by the ghost's Rank. The ghost cannot reestablish these Manifestation Conditions while the Singer continues singing, but the Singer must make a Stamina + Expression roll for each minute they sing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, this works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to go with something more flavorful than just the straight bashing damage from 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well it absolutely is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it's Patterning, but if the consensus is that it's Ruling I'd tack on Advanced Scale: Targets and Instant cast.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it would be Patterning if you assumed giving it a conditional thing makes one step down from making. The thing is, that you might as well draw ghosts from shadows with Patterning. In my opinion, Ruling is the only way that waits for the target to die.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Sever Oaths</i> can also free bound entities and change someone's Doom, I think it's appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hey... can Sever Oaths free ghosts from the whole must resolve ones anchors, and then spend time in the underworld, and move the ghost straight to passing on to the bottom of the Ocean of Fragments, Starry Anu, the Supernal or whenever they go when they are done? I was toying with the idea of a final attainment that just lets the ghost pass on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448660#post1448660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I hit all those points.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I would be content to just copy and paste your version and call it a day, but I\u2019m going to try my best to improve what I can so this becomes the best I can make it, with your help as you will.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T13:36:36-07:00","id":1448713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448683#post1448683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Alright, I will do that. My only issue with it then is penalty from 1e was a little strange, being both non scaling, and having a resistance of Gnosis + Composure. I would like if the dead are being quite today, or one ghost is sobbing loudly right next to the Singer having different values for the resistance. The intrusive thoughts style, doomed individual knowledge is fine having a value of one.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could take inspiration from the Medium Merit, give a condition related to being pestered by the ghosts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, it really is. Could the Singer gain Inspiration or a positive condition related to singing their funeral song? I think it would be a nice touch. Either that or start the helping people cope with there loss here. </div> </div> </div>Informed (Death of the Person) would certainly be appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm, that\u2019s actually neat. How common is ones Fate being manipulated though? Later thought: if even half of the superstitions about things causing bad luck are true, then this could be very useful indeed. Fate Mage Armor really coves this angle, but I\u2019m probably still going to keep this here. </div> </div> </div>Depends on how often you deal with Mages, Mummies, and Fae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perfect then, I won\u2019t need to mess with that. I really like the Stamina + Expression rolls you mentioned later, I will probably put that a side note in every power. </div> </div> </div>I'd keep it as a roll per minute, though, making it shorter than that is too punishing, I think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That\u2019s neat. What\u2019s the difference besides practice between Warding Gesture and Fabricate Fortune? </div> </div> </div><i>Warding Gesture</i> protects against new manipulations, <i>Fabricate Fortune</i> can trick existing ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Agreed. Any converted version of the Singers needs this line somewhere. Third attainment is a good spot for it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, this works.<br /> <br /> Well it absolutely is.<br /> <br /> I think it would be Patterning if you assumed giving it a conditional thing makes one step down from making. The thing is, that you might as well draw ghosts from shadows with Patterning. In my opinion, Ruling is the only way that waits for the target to die.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hey... can Sever Oaths free ghosts from the whole must resolve ones anchors, and then spend time in the underworld, and move the ghost straight to passing on to the bottom of the Ocean of Fragments, Starry Anu, the Supernal or whenever they go when they are done? I was toying with the idea of a final attainment that just lets the ghost pass on. </div> </div> </div>Even if <i>Sever Oaths </i>can't, <i>Sever Oaths</i> with guaranteed Death 5 certainly should be able to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I would be content to just copy and paste your version and call it a day, but I\u2019m going to try my best to improve what I can so this becomes the best I can make it, with your help as you will. </div> </div> </div>:thumbsup:<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T09:43:14-07:00","id":1448784,"title":"","content":"Well, I definitely tried to think of anything else that might fit in the legacy, with the only thing coming to mind is possibly shifting to twilight for a little bit to pass through walls. This would make the legacy a little more ghostly. I think it would be neat if they could still sing through twilight. I think fourth attainment would be the only spot for it...but that would replace Exorcism. Maybe it's just something the legacy members commonly do? I think that's everything, I might edit it for wording and grammar, but the legacy is officially done. I will leave the quotes in and credit proindrakenzol for their great help. Thank you, proindrakenzol, you were of great assistance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T10:40:15-07:00","id":1448878,"title":"","content":"Alright, so I'm moving on to the Tamers of Roots. This is a mess right now, and I am not sure where to put certain attainments. I also have no idea about what the later attainments should be. Edit: I think I might be sticking too hard to one idea about what the legacy should be. The Singers in Silence had maybe two attainments related towards each of their roles, but each worked in a harmony to make the whole picture.<br /> This legacy comes from a desire for more high fantasy alchemy, and from the realization that Matter can enhance the effects a substance has on a body.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Tamers of Roots</b></span><br /> <br /> description<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Better Living Through Chemistry</span> </b><br /> <br /> There have always been those that seek knowledge of root and stem. Dirt and Stone have ecologies of their own, with ore vein root and flowers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Thyrsus, Free Council, Nameless, Seers<br /> <b>Background</b>: Many come from medical backgrounds,<br /> <b>Appearances</b>: Many are warped and twisted by the strange chemicals running in their veins, with signs of their preferred method of delivery.<br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Blights, Alchemists<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Matter 2, Life 2, Medicine 2, Science 2, Occult or Crafting 1<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Consumption and survival without magic of an extremely toxic mix of nightshade and Aperion<br /> <b>Organization</b>: Pre-Great Refusal: A council overseen by the strongest legacy member. After Great Refusal: Master Student chains<br /> <b>Theory</b>: Certain Materials when consumed or with exposure, effect the body and mind. The Tamers of Roots brew potions that elevate these effects to a wonderous degree.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>: Matter<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: (+1); (+2); (+2); (consumption of a prepared draught+1, a draught congaing supernatural materials +2)<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: tending to a garden; studying chemical formula; self-experimentation;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">First: The Formula</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation.<br /> The Tamers must know the properties of their materials before anything else. The Tamer may take a instant action to study a non-living object and learn it\u2019s properties and use in recipes. The Tamer gains the informed (material use) condition. This includes any supernatural properties a material may have.<br /> Discern Composition with advanced duration.<br /> This may not be a properly built attainment and I\u2019m open to suggestions. I was going to do craftsman\u2019s eye, but I don\u2019t have the reach to learn the uses, so this is me comprise. I want them to just know how to use their chemicals and herbs after just looking at them as the first attainment<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 1<br /> When using the first attainment, the tamer may scan still living creatures to see what properties their body parts may have, both while still living and when they turn into matter.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Second: The Immunity</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Matter 2, Life 2, Medicine 3<br /> The Tamers consume and use toxic materials on a daily basis, immunity to the negative effects of their draughts. The tamer is immune to negative conditions caused by their creations, in addition they are immune to bashing damage caused by handling toxic materials, and reduce lethal damage by their Matter dots. The mage also adds Matter dots to stamina rolls to resist the effects<br /> Alchemist's Touch and Cleanse the Body with advanced duration<br /> <br /> The Tamers of Roots handle toxic materials regularly, they need inbuilt protection.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Third: The Elixir</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Matter 3, Science 3, Crafts 2 or Occult 2<br /> The Tamer can create a potion, a blank state material that can absorb up the Tamers Matter dots in sacrificed materials to absorb a property of a sacrificed non-living material. This includes any supernatural properties a material may have. The potion can last up to matter years before expiring, or for a additional mana may be indefinite.<br /> <br /> <br /> Spell Potion and Wonderful Machine with advanced duration. The extra mana comes from the matter 2 attainment.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if this should be third or fourth attainment.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 3<br /> .The tamer may use living materials, like perfected blood or flesh, or vampire blood, in their potions.<br /> <br /> Maybe I drop this and allow the weaving of certain properties into the body when consumed?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fourth: The Refinement</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Matter 4, Medicine 4.<br /> The tamer may enhance the effects of a given substance, adding matter dots to the chosen effect. If the substance is used in The Elixir attainment, the enhanced properties remain if selected.<br /> Matter Perfecting with advanced duration<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 4<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fifth: Clever name</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Matter 5, two dots in a third Skill among the optional prerequisite Skills<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-18-2021, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T10:59:55-07:00","id":1448880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448878#post1448878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so I'm moving on to the Tamers of Roots. This is a mess right now, and I am not sure where to put certain attainments. I also have no idea about what the later attainments should be.<br /> This legacy comes from a desire for more high fantasy alchemy, and from the realization that Matter can enhance the effects a substance has on a body.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd recommend making this a Moros Life/Matter Legacy, rather than a Thyrsus Matter/Life Legacy for two reason:<br /> <br /> The first is flavor: Moroi are heavily steeped in the &quot;alchemy&quot; symbolism and already have the nickname &quot;Alchemists.&quot;<br /> <br /> The second is overlap: there's already a Matter/Life Thyrsus Tamer Legacy, the Tamers of Rivers.<br /> <br /> I would look at the DE2 Legacy &quot;Kitchen Alchemists&quot; for a solid starting point on what a Matter/Life Alchemy Legacy could and should do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T11:13:12-07:00","id":1448881,"title":"","content":"That was fast.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448880#post1448880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd recommend making this a Moros Life/Matter Legacy, rather than a Thyrsus Matter/Life Legacy for two reason:<br /> <br /> The first is flavor: Moroi are heavily steeped in the &quot;alchemy&quot; symbolism and already have the nickname &quot;Alchemists.&quot;<br /> <br /> The second is overlap: there's already a Matter/Life Thyrsus Tamer Legacy, the Tamers of Rivers.<br /> <br /> I would look at the DE2 Legacy &quot;Kitchen Alchemists&quot; for a solid starting point on what a Matter/Life Alchemy Legacy could and should do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm expecting some rewrites of this one. I've had one person argue for a Thyrsus Matter legacy before, I figured the difference in theme should be enough from the Tamers of Rivers, but I can redo this as a Moros version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T12:07:16-07:00","id":1448887,"title":"","content":"how is this?<br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Tamers of Roots</b></span><br /> <br /> description<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Better Living Through Chemistry</span></b><br /> <br /> There have always been those that seek knowledge of root and stem. Dirt and Stone have ecologies of their own, with ore vein root and flowers.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Moros, Free Council, Nameless, Seers<br /> <b>Background</b>: Many come from medical backgrounds, Drug Producers, and Herbalists<br /> <b>Appearances</b>: Many are warped and twisted by the strange chemicals running in their veins, with signs of their preferred method of delivery.<br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Blights, Herbalist<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 2, Matter 2, Medicine 2, Science 2, Occult or Crafting 1<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Consumption and survival without magic of an extremely toxic mix of nightshade and Aperion<br /> <b>Organization</b>: Pre-Great Refusal: A council overseen by the strongest legacy member. After Great Refusal: Master Student chains<br /> <b>Theory</b>: Certain Materials when consumed or with exposure, effect the body and mind. The Tamers of Roots brew potions that elevate these effects to a wonderous degree.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>: Life<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: (+1); (+2); (+2); (consumption of a prepared draught+1, a draught congaing supernatural materials +2)<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: tending to a garden; studying chemical formula; self-experimentation;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">First: </span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation.<br /> The Herbalist is resistant to drug and disease, adding their Life dots to resistance rolls. The herbalist makes the roll immediately.<br /> Cleanse body with 1 reach effect<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Matter 1<br /> The Herbalist may make a concoction that imparts the effects of the above to the next person who drinks it.<br /> Same as the above, but with advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Second: </span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 2, Medicine 3<br /> Heightened Senses Taste and Smell maybe?<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Matter 2<br /> Body Control Spell Potion with advanced duration. Mage choses the effects.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Third: </span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 3, Science 3, Crafts 2 or Occult 2<br /> Transform Life? or Honing the Form?<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Matter 3<br /> Wonderful Machine spell potion to add material properties into living subject. You could also make permanent jewel or perfected material flowers with the matter two attainment, so that's nice.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fourth: </span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 4, Medicine 4.<br /> Mend with reach into aggravated?<br /> <b>Optional</b>: Matter 4<br /> Weave Life Properties into Matter? Edit: here is where we would put Matter Perfecting to enhance the properties of materials on living things.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fifth: </span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 5, two dots in a third Skill among the optional prerequisite Skills<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Matter 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-18-2021, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T12:21:54-07:00","id":1448889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448881#post1448881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was fast.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm expecting some rewrites of this one. I've had one person argue for a Thyrsus Matter legacy before, I figured the difference in theme should be enough from the Tamers of Rivers, but I can redo this as a Moros version.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main reason I'd say Moros is less about the Tamers of Rivers (though that is a small consideration), and more the heavy &quot;Alchemist&quot; theming to the Moros.<br /> <br /> Assuming you swap this to Moros:<br /> <br /> For the first Attainment, I'd just make it a combined attainment of Life and Matter that reveals what would happen if the substance were ingested or otherwise used in an alchemical concoction, basically looking at something would give you a list of its properties a la Elder Scrolls. Advanced Duration, requires an Instant Action to study the object.<br /> <br /> Second is fine as it is, protection is always a good idea, the bonus to rolls should be Life, though, not Matter.<br /> <br /> Third: Life side I'd go with <i>Body Control</i> with the +2 Reach option for halving Lethal healing time <i>and</i> Advanced Duration from the Matter 2 Attainment Permanence since this would be tied to an alchemical potion, however it would only work on the Mage, instead acting as a toxin with strength equal to the effect's potency of (1 + lower of Life or Matter dots)/2 and a duration based on the Mage's Life dots on the Advanced Duration chart, roll every Lethal healing interval.<br /> For the Matter Attainment I'd go with the ability to spend a scene to create a potion that, when ingested, causes the effects of <i>Transform Life</i> on the imbiber with the effects of <i>Shrink and Grow</i> as one of the potential options (each potency allocated to <i>Shrink and Grow</i> would be a potency not allocated to a different <i>Transform Life</i> effect). This Attainment would cost a Mana (Permanence Attainment), the transformation would last a scene, and it would spend its reach on Advanced Scale: Size. The Mage would have to choose which effects took place in what order in case the imbiber decides to Withstand. The potion itself retains its potency for the Mage's Matter dots on the Advanced Duration chart.<br /> <br /> Fourth: Life side: <i>Honing the Form</i> with Advanced Duration (Permanence), the ability to split between two attributes, and the ability to boost an attribute above the normal maximum rating, costs 1 Mana. Same negative effects on anyone other than the Mage consuming it as the Third Attainment, consuming another concoction changes the Attribute bonuses. Takes a scene to prepare a concoction, but a whole bunch can be made if the Mage wants to constantly flip-flop their Attributes.<br /> Matter side: can create a more potent potion with a shorter duration that can be consumed by anyone. <i>Honing the Form</i> with reach to change the primary factor to Potency, Advanced Duration from Permanence, and the ability to boost attribute above the normal maximum rating, boosts a single Attribute of the imbiber by the Mage's Life dots for a Scene (attribute chosen during potion creation). Costs a Mana. The potion itself retains its potency for the Mage's Matter dots on the Advanced Duration chart. If the Mage drinks their own potion the boost <i>stacks</i> with the boost from the primary portion of the Attainment, rather than overwriting or giving only a transient boost.<br /> <br /> Fifth: I'd put <i>Hone the Perfected Form</i> here with the +2 reach option and Life conjunctional to work on a living person, Advanced Duration from Permanence, and Indefinite for the final reach. This would only work on the Mage in question, killing anyone else that consumed the potion, what the effects of being Perfected would be on the Mage is something I'll have to think about, but it seems cool, so...<br /> <br /> I'd also make all of the above require special ingredients to keep with the theme.<br /> <br /> <br /> [edit] Sorry, didn't see your post until after I posted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-18-2021, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T13:02:09-07:00","id":1448891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448889#post1448889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The main reason I'd say Moros is less about the Tamers of Rivers (though that is a small consideration), and more the heavy &quot;Alchemist&quot; theming to the Moros.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this started in my head as a Moros Matter Legacy, then when asking about some of the ideas I had about how to do it I was informed Thyrsus might work better, and then it was now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448889#post1448889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the first Attainment, I'd just make it a combined attainment of Life and Matter that reveals what would happen if the substance were ingested or otherwise used in an alchemical concoction, basically looking at something would give you a list of its properties a la Elder Scrolls. Advanced Duration, requires an Instant Action to study the object.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is pretty much what i was thinking of when I started this, I tried Heightened Senses as a stand by for the Moros version, my Thyrsus version was a bit closer to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448889#post1448889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second is fine as it is, protection is always a good idea, the bonus to rolls should be Life, though, not Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually did it as a combined spell of Alchemists Touch and Cleanse the Body in my Thyrsus version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448889#post1448889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third: Life side I'd go with <i>Body Control</i> with the +2 Reach option for halving Lethal healing time <i>and</i> Advanced Duration from the Matter 2 Attainment Permanence since this would be tied to an alchemical potion, however it would only work on the Mage, instead acting as a toxin with strength equal to the effect's potency of (1 + lower of Life or Matter dots)/2 and a duration based on the Mage's Life dots on the Advanced Duration chart, roll every Lethal healing interval.<br /> For the Matter Attainment I'd go with the ability to spend a scene to create a potion that, when ingested, causes the effects of <i>Transform Life</i> on the imbiber with the effects of <i>Shrink and Grow</i> as one of the potential options (each potency allocated to <i>Shrink and Grow</i> would be a potency not allocated to a different <i>Transform Life</i> effect). This Attainment would cost a Mana (Permanence Attainment), the transformation would last a scene, and it would spend its reach on Advanced Scale: Size. The Mage would have to choose which effects took place in what order in case the imbiber decides to Withstand. The potion itself retains its potency for the Mage's Matter dots on the Advanced Duration chart.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like the Potion/Poison based on who uses it. Both effects are good. The use of the Permanence Attainment is nice, along with the priority of effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448889#post1448889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth: Life side: <i>Honing the Form</i> with Advanced Duration (Permanence), the ability to split between two attributes, and the ability to boost an attribute above the normal maximum rating, costs 1 Mana. Same negative effects on anyone other than the Mage consuming it as the Third Attainment, consuming another concoction changes the Attribute bonuses. Takes a scene to prepare a concoction, but a whole bunch can be made if the Mage wants to constantly flip-flop their Attainments.<br /> Matter side: can create a more potent potion with a shorter duration that can be consumed by anyone. <i>Honing the Form</i> with reach to change the primary factor to Potency, Advanced Duration from Permanence, and the ability to boost attribute above the normal maximum rating, boosts a single Attribute of the imbiber by the Mage's Life dots for a Scene (attribute chosen during potion creation). Costs a Mana. The potion itself retains its potency for the Mage's Matter dots on the Advanced Duration chart. If the Mage drinks their own potion the boost <i>stacks</i> with the boost from the primary portion of the Attainment, rather than overwriting or giving only a transient boost.</div> </div> </div> </div> Looks good. What are the rules on legacy attainments and spell control? If you make multiple potions, does it take up a separate spell control?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448889#post1448889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fifth: I'd put <i>Hone the Perfected Form</i> here with the +2 reach option and Life conjunctional to work on a living person, Advanced Duration from Permanence, and Indefinite for the final reach. This would only work on the Mage in question, killing anyone else that consumed the potion, what the effects of being Perfected would be on the Mage is something I'll have to think about, but it seems cool, so...</div> </div> </div> </div> Shiny. Keeping for any future versions. I was thinking about the big ultimate transformation style final Attainment, but I couldn't figure out how to do it. Perfecting yourself is awesome. I would say it depends on the shadow name, nimbus.. etc. The Blight from Dead by Daylight might be good example of this, he inspired this legacy after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448889#post1448889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also make all of the above require special ingredients to keep with the theme.</div> </div> </div> </div> Of course, I need my Formula: Elixir Zeboim and my Blisterwort and Wheat potions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448889#post1448889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[edit] Sorry, didn't see your post until after I posted.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I thought this was amusing. I like your version better than mine for the most part. Let's see, healing potion is covered, fallout buff-out is covered, (edit: whoops, forgot to finish), the long duration body control effects are covered, that's pretty much everything I wanted. Only thing missing is the immortality pursuit trope, and frankly I don't think they need it. Maybe, if they wanted, they could weave perfected gold's never rust or spoil property into themselves, like the philosophers stone was supposed to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-18-2021, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T13:16:04-07:00","id":1448892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448891#post1448891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks good. What are the rules on legacy attainments and spell control? If you make multiple potions, does it take up a separate spell control?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Legacy Attainments do not use spell control at all.<br /> <br /> Another thought I had if you decide to keep the resistance/immunity to poison effect for the second attainment is you could open this Legacy up to making Ascending Ones style potions, as well, treating the lower of the Mage's Life or Matter dots as their &quot;dots&quot; in the Elixir Endowment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T13:36:03-07:00","id":1448895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448892#post1448892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacy Attainments do not use spell control at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Then my first idea of buffed drugs would get out of hand really fast.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448892#post1448892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thought I had if you decide to keep the resistance/immunity to poison effect for the second attainment is you could open this Legacy up to making Ascending Ones style potions, as well, treating the lower of the Mage's Life or Matter dots as their &quot;dots&quot; in the Elixir Endowment.</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the Ascending Ones, I was told I would need the proper Arcanum to replicate their effects. I switched to mage specific things I could do, and thought that it would be possible, for example, to make bloodborne healing blood vials from vampire blood, or goblin fruit, or some werewolf gland or some else crazy. The Ascending Ones rely on mundane materials combined with internal alchemy. A mage version of them would have access to tons of extra supernatural materials, potentially replicating some of their effects. That's what I was going for is the Thyrsus version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T13:48:21-07:00","id":1448896,"title":"","content":"Taking a break from mechanics for a bit, I had some ideas for the history of the legacy. The basic idea is that it actually forms it's own small nameless order through out most of history, and fights heavily in the Nameless war. When it became clear the rest of what would become the Free Council would side with the Diamond Orders, the Legacy had schism, with the head of the legacy being unable or unwilling to ever remotely ally with the Diamond. Legacy Sympathetic Connections being what they are, the argument broke out into a fight that caught the Legacy headquarters on Perfected Fire... or so the only known surviving member says. In truth, something is blocking Time magic from seeing what REALLY went on that Fateful day... and the Seers of the Throne have had access to the Legacy ever since.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T14:09:27-07:00","id":1448897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448895#post1448895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Then my first idea of buffed drugs would get out of hand really fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, not really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Ascending Ones, I was told I would need the proper Arcanum to replicate their effects. I switched to mage specific things I could do, and thought that it would be possible, for example, to make bloodborne healing blood vials from vampire blood, or goblin fruit, or some werewolf gland or some else crazy. The Ascending Ones rely on mundane materials combined with internal alchemy. A mage version of them would have access to tons of extra supernatural materials, potentially replicating some of their effects. That's what I was going for is the Thyrsus version. </div> </div> </div>Allowing the replication of the Endowment wouldn't be outside the bounds of a Legacy Attainment, and it's a lot easier to use the rules provided in the HtV2e Kickstarter for making new potions than to try and come up with a bunch on your own. Even if you decide the system isn't exactly the same in-universe, from an out of universe standpoint leveraging the Ascending Ones or Promethean Alchemist rules is just so much easier than trying to put together a new system to accomplish the same effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T14:17:15-07:00","id":1448898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448896#post1448896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking a break from mechanics for a bit, I had some ideas for the history of the legacy. The basic idea is that it actually forms it's own small nameless order through out most of history, and fights heavily in the Nameless war. When it became clear the rest of what would become the Free Council would side with the Diamond Orders, the Legacy had schism, with the head of the legacy being unable or unwilling to ever remotely ally with the Diamond. Legacy Sympathetic Connections being what they are, the argument broke out into a fight that caught the Legacy headquarters on Perfected Fire... or so the only known surviving member says. In truth, something is blocking Time magic from seeing what REALLY went on that Fateful day... and the Seers of the Throne have had access to the Legacy ever since.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good transition to the modern day. Does the Legacy trace its roots to any particular region or group of alchemists? The Herbalists have mechanical parallels with the Ascending Ones, even if you don't want to allow the use of their potions. Maybe they formed around studying a Promethean and its brand of alchemy, or are an outgrowth of the alchemists commissioned by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qin_Shi_Huang\" target=\"_blank\">Qin Shi Huang</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T15:22:50-07:00","id":1448902,"title":"","content":"Back from getting food.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448898#post1448898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good transition to the modern day. Does the Legacy trace its roots to any particular region or group of alchemists? The Herbalists have mechanical parallels with the Ascending Ones, even if you don't want to allow the use of their potions. Maybe they formed around studying a Promethean and its brand of alchemy, or are an outgrowth of the alchemists commissioned by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qin_Shi_Huang\" target=\"_blank\">Qin Shi Huang</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I hadn\u2019t planning on giving a direct link to any particular group, my history education is extremely lacking. I feel like I wouldn\u2019t do it justice by skimming Wikipedia articles to pick. I do know I planned on the Master of the legacy having taken part in the awakened portion of the Opium Wars, and being embittered by the Diamond\u2019s actions during that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T17:03:35-07:00","id":1448915,"title":"","content":"So... are the Tamers of Roots part of the Elemental Masteries as their name suggests?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T17:22:07-07:00","id":1448917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448915#post1448915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... are the Tamers of Roots part of the Elemental Masteries as their name suggests?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes? It wasn\u2019t originally intended to be , but that was the only name that kinda fit that I could come up with. (I\u2019m terrible at names) I got the idea when I thought about ore veins looking like roots of a plant, and roots among other things are used in herbalism. If you have a better name, I will happily change it. Also wood has some basis as a element in Taoism... and Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T18:27:59-07:00","id":1448920,"title":"","content":"If so, then the Life part of their Attainments could directly manipulate plant matter. That seems to be a thing for the Tamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T20:11:50-07:00","id":1448930,"title":"","content":"Try three, all future changes will come from edits of this post. Keeping as a Moros. I have not backed the hunter 2e, so no access to the manuscripts without piracy, which I won't do moral reasons. If someone would be so generous, a brief summery of the mechanics of the 2e Ascending Ones and the Alchemists from Promethean as I have access to neither. One day I can afford to buy everything I'm missing, but today is not that day... maybe next month.<br /> <br /> edit: New name is Seekers of the Lotus, because the lotus is used in traditional medicine, and it\u2019s edible. Think I'm going to try for a Ascending Ones type name. Thanks for all the help!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Z\u00e9te\u00f3 Theriaca</b></span><br /> <br /> He was talented chemist, worked for the East India Trading Company even. But as I hear it, he came back a few months ago, and has locked himself in the family estate, only coming out to order rare ingredients.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Better Living Through Chemistry</span></b><br /> <br /> There have always been those that seek knowledge of root and stem. In time, one group rose to prominence in a ancient land and traveled to others who plied similar trades. Eventually a number of nameless Herbalists arose from these and put their trust in a great library in Alexandria. From the ashes, the nascent order took it upon themselves to carry their legacy and declared themselves apart from the others. They shunned both the servants of tyrant gods and those who sought control them. Eventually they found allies in other outcasts and began to expand, drawing knowledge from anywhere they could to expand their arts. Eventually, members of the legacy were caught up into the Nameless War, and when it became clear that their allies would side with the Diamond, those same Members refused to follow. This rift eventually resulted in first word, then fist, and finally fire. For the second time, Fire robbed the legacy of it's home, and of it's strength. the few that remained fully threw their support into the Free Council, knowing full well that to do otherwise would invite destruction. And yet, the servants of the lie have learned the legacy's secrets, far more detailed than the mere theft of a soul stone would allow... And something blocks that Fateful day from Time, so none may see the Truth, whatever that may be.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Moros, Free Council, Nameless, Seers<br /> <b>Background</b>: Z\u00e9te\u00f3 Theriaca primarily pull their members from those with backgrounds in pharmaceutical chemistry, herbalism, and mortal alchemy.<br /> <b>Appearances</b>: Many are warped and twisted by the strange chemicals running in their veins, with signs of their preferred method of delivery.<br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Blights, Herbalist<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 2, Matter 2, Medicine 2, Science 2, Occult or Crafting 1<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Consumption and survival without magic of a mix of nightshade, lotus root, and Lunargent.<br /> <b>Organization</b>: Pre-Great Refusal: A council overseen by the strongest legacy member. After Great Refusal: Master Student chains<br /> <b>Theory</b>: Certain Materials when consumed or with exposure, effect the body and mind. The Tamers of Roots brew potions that elevate these effects to a wonderous degree.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>: Life<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: mundane chemical or alchemical ingredients +1; supernatural alchemical ingredients +2; consumption of a prepared draught +1 (+2 if made with supernatural ingredients)<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: tending to a garden; studying chemical formula; self-experimentation; spending at least a hour preparing a concoction<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">First: Taste the Root</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation.<br /> The Herbalist can spend a scene to prepare a concoction to open up their inner eye to the secrets of the alchemical universe, after which the Herbalist can determine the alchemical properties of plant and mineral with naught but a simple examination. The effects of the concoction last for the lower of the Herbalist's Life or Matter dots on the Advanced Duration chart, and the examination requires an instant action and tasting or otherwise handling the examined substance.<br /> This insight allows the Herbalist to replicate the feats of Mortal Alchemists, the Herbalist treats the lower of their Life or Matter dots as dots in any specialized form of Alchemy available to Mortals such as the Ascending One's Elixir Endowment or the Magnitude trait of the Alchemists described in Promethean: the Created 2e. If the Herbalist already has such a Merit, use the Merit's value if higher and refund the experience per Sanctity of Merits if lower.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Second: Internal Alchemy</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 2, Matter 2, Medicine 3<br /> <br /> The Herbalists consume and use toxic materials on a daily basis, immunity to the negative effects of their draughts. The Herbalist is immune and this Attainment grants the Herbalist resistance to the negative conditions caused by their creations: they are immune to bashing damage caused by handling or consuming caustic or toxic materials, and reduce lethal damage by their Matter dots. The Herbalist can also attempt to immediately flush their system of toxins, spending an Instant action to roll immediately to resist the toxin's effects, they add their Life dots to rolls to resist the effects this roll.<br /> This Attainment negates any backlash or physiological drawback to consuming a potion derived from Mortal Alchemy, but not any mystical backlash or drawback.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Third: The Bitter Draught</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 3, Science 3, Crafts 2 or Occult 2<br /> The Herbalist may spend a scene preparing a concoction, The herbalist chooses a number of effects from the below list equal to their dots in Life to affect the potion's imbiber, the imbiber may Withstand the transformation with Stamina if they are unwilling:<ul><li>Breathing: Each rank slows down the subject\u2019s breathing, halving Halves the amount of oxygen she the Herbalist needs to function normally.</li> <li>Heartbeat: By slowing down Slows the subject\u2019s Herbalist's heartbeat, she can double doubling the interval at which a toxin affects her.</li> <li>Metabolism: Regulating the subject\u2019s Regulates the Herbalist's metabolism allowing her to subsist on half as much food, and doubling the amount of time between checks for deprivation or fatigue.</li> <li>Reflexes: Add +1 to the Herbalist\u2019s Initiative.</li> <li>Scent: The mage Herbalist can change the subject\u2019s her scent to any that her body could naturally produce, eliminating (or increasing) body odors, controlling pheromone release.</li> <li>Healing: Halve the healing time for bashing and lethal damage.</li> </ul>The effects of this potion last for an amount of time equal to the Herbalist's Life dots on the Advanced Duration chart.<br /> <br /> If the potion consumed by anyone other than the Herbalist that created it, it instead acts as a deadly poison, with strength equal to the effect's potency of (1 + lower of Life or Matter dots)/2 and a duration based on the Mage's Life dots on the Advanced Duration chart, rolling every Lethal healing interval.<br /> <br /> This attainment functions as the spell Body Control with the Permanence Attainment and 2 reach towards lethal healing.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Matter 3<br /> The Herbalist may spend scene and a point of Mana to prepare a concoction capable of transforming whoever drinks it. This potion may be exist for Life steps on the advanced duration chart before losing it's potency. Once taken the transformation begins in the subject gains Life ranks in which to gain effects. These effects are:<ul><li>Claws: The subject gains savage claws, granting her a +1 weapon bonus.</li> <li>Environmental Adaptation: Like creatures adapted for life deep underwater or inhospitable deserts, the subject gains the ability to survive pressure, extreme heat or cold (up to level 4 environments), and arid or moisture-heavy environments. This effect may be chosen multiple times, each time choose a different environment.</li> <li>Gills/Lungs: The subject may breathe underwater (or in air, if normally aquatic) freely.</li> <li>Immunities: The subject gains resistance to toxins or poisonous materials, like a rat\u2019s ability to devour even rotten food unharmed or herbivores\u2019 ability to fully digest plant matter. This effect may be chosen multiple times, each time choose a different immunity.</li> <li>Leaping: Gaining powerful legs like a frog\u2019s or kangaroo\u2019s, the target gains a bonus to jumping rolls, increasing the distance leaped by each success on the Athletics roll.</li> <li>Prehensile Tail: Gain a bonus to rolls related to balance or climbing equal to Potency.</li> <li>Scaly Armor/Thick Hide: The subject gains 2/1 armor (must be at least Size 2).</li> <li>Senses: The subject gains a new sense, such as echolocation, primitive infravision, or a keen sense for vibrations, granting a bonus to Perception rolls and the ability to perceive phenomena outside the human senses. This effect may be chosen multiple times, each time choose a different sense.</li> <li>Size: Each level of ranks either adds or subtracts one from the subject\u2019s Size. If reduced to Size 0, subject can be made roughly the size of a dime. The subject can grow to a size of up to 1 + (the lower of the Herbalist's Life or Matter dots)/2 on the Advanced Scale chart.</li> <li>Tentacles: The subject may make grappling attempts against targets up to her Size in feet away.</li> <li>Venom: The subject gains fangs or small stingers (damage bonus 0) capable of injecting venom with a Toxicity equal to the Herbalists Life dots. Must grapple first unless a second level of adaptation is taken. If taken with Tentacles, the Venom may be delivered automatically by any successful move during a grapple.</li> <li>Wall-Crawling: The subject (which can be no larger than Size 7) gains the ability to climb on surfaces without equipment</li> <li>or even handholds, provided the surface can bear her weight.</li> </ul>This transformation last a scene. The potion, if unconsumed, retains its efficacy for the Herbalist's Matter dots on the Advanced Duration chart.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fourth: The Putrid Serum</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 4, Medicine 4.<br /> The Herbalist may spends a scene and a point of Mana to prepare a concoction that enhances the Herbalist's physical attributes. When creating the concoction the Herbalist assigns 1 + Life dots/2 potency to up to two physical Attributes, drinking this concoction increases the Herbalist's Attributes by the chose potency for an amount of time equal to the Herbalist's Life dots on the Advanced Duration chart and can increase the Attributes above the Herbalist's normal limit. Drinking a second concoction ends the effects of the first and applies the new Attribute bonuses, however the duration of the effect is measured from the creation of the concoction, not its consumption.<br /> If the potion is consumed by anyone other than the Herbalist that created it, it instead acts as a deadly poison, with strength equal to the effect's potency of (1 + lower of Life or Matter dots)/2 and a duration based on the Mage's Life dots on the Advanced Duration chart, rolling every Lethal healing interval.<br /> This Attainment replicates the effects of Honing the Form with the Permanence Attainment, the ability to boost attributes above the normal maximum, and the ability to increase two attributes.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Matter 4<br /> The Herbalist can spend a scene and a point of Mana to creates a similar, but more potent and shorter lasting, concoction than the above. Rather than a long lasting, but small, boost to their own Attributes, the Herbalist can instead make a potion that increases a single physical Attribute of the imbiber by the Herbalist's Life dots for a single scene, this effect can take the imbiber above their normal Attribute maximum. The potion, if unconsumed, retains its efficacy for the Herbalist's Matter dots on the Advanced Duration chart. If the Herbalist imbibes the potion the effect fully stacks with the Attribute bonus from the primary Attainment, rather than overwriting it or stacking transiently. A subject can only safely drink one such potion, each additional potion counts as a toxin with toxicity equal to potency and an interval of 1 minute.<br /> This Attainment replicates the effects of Honing the Form with the Permanence Attainment and reach to change the primary factor to potency and the ability to boost attributes above the normal maximum.<br /> <br /> Honing the Form with reach to change the primary factor to Potency, Advanced Duration from Permanence, and the ability to boost attribute above the normal maximum rating<br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fifth: The Final Transmutation</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 5, Matter 5, Science 4. Crafts or Occult 3<br /> The Herbalist makes one final potion, their Magnum Opus. This potion kills any without the Strongest Internal Alchemy and only work once, the Herbalist cannot benefit from further applications of this potion, even from other Masters. If anyone other than the Herbalist that brewed it consumes this potion they die immediately. After consuming the potion the Master Herbalist becomes something more than they once were, and possibly something less: they are a Perfected living being. The Herbalist gains the rote action quality on any non-spellcasting action whose unmodified dice pool is 8 or greater. However, for any action whose base dice pool is 3 or less their failures are automatically dramatic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hone the Perfected Form here with the +2 reach option and Life conjunctional to work on a living person, Advanced Duration from Permanence, and Indefinite for the final reach.<br /> Edit: this is from the Prime Beast ability, turns you into a semi-ascended Ochemata","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-19-2021, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T20:14:01-07:00","id":1448931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448920#post1448920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, then the Life part of their Attainments could directly manipulate plant matter. That seems to be a thing for the Tamers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I should rename this Legacy, and then make the real Tamers of Roots. I want the plants from plants vs zombies, or growing Supernal plants in the fallen world now.<br /> <br /> Edit: yeah, I\u2019m doing this next or second next. Arcanthus Life/Time season plant magic? Or maybe flowers that change the resonance of a area? Or maybe messing with fruits of knowledge? Life/Prime Orbimos. I still want my jewel plants I mentioned earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-18-2021, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T21:25:48-07:00","id":1448935,"title":"","content":"The Roses of Eden are an Acanthus Legacy with Life primary, introduced in Keys to the Supernal Tarot. They were mostly about denouncing the Atlantis paradigm hegemony of Awakened society... which, under the 2E framework of how \u201cAtlantis\u201d is treated, comes off a bit unfit. I think they had some plant-magic going on, so maybe you could do them a facelift for that magical botanist Legacy?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, for this magical herbalist Legacy I\u2019ll need to look deeper... but at a glance I think you\u2019re doing fine?<br /> (Tbh I\u2019m still busy doing the Nighthawks, and a college class assignment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-18T21:37:45-07:00","id":1448936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448935#post1448935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Roses of Eden are an Acanthus Legacy with Life primary, introduced in Keys to the Supernal Tarot. They were mostly about denouncing the Atlantis paradigm hegemony of Awakened society... which, under the 2E framework of how \u201cAtlantis\u201d is treated, comes off a bit unfit. I think they had some plant-magic going on, so maybe you could do them a facelift for that magical botanist Legacy?</div> </div> </div> </div> I will have to read about them, but I started planning stuff about sacred groves and and nimbuses growing like plants, an plants that have their own nimbus. If I like them I might just make both, because I have some free time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448935#post1448935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, for this magical herbalist Legacy I\u2019ll need to look deeper... but at a glance I think you\u2019re doing fine?<br /> (Tbh I\u2019m still busy doing the Nighthawks, and a college class assignment <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks to <b>proindrakenzol, </b>they really helped focus my ideas while staying within the themes I wanted. <br /> Good luck on your assignment!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T07:42:22-07:00","id":1448986,"title":"","content":"Read the Roses of Eden, not sure I am a fan. They are pretty different than what I was going for, building a nameless order for some reasons that are less relevant in 2e. Their attainments are practically life only, with only one attainment actually using prime. I do like their symbolic metaphor, that they become thornless roses. If I did bring them to 2e I would have to radically retool them to taste, and at that point I might as well make a whole new legacy. Also why is it a Arcanthus legacy if it\u2019s life and prime, don\u2019t Orbimos usually get the religious metaphors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T08:29:40-07:00","id":1448989,"title":"","content":"Let\u2019s see, tamer legacies usually have attainments manipulating their element, things symbolic of their element, and metaphorically become their element. Interesting, the Roses of Eden do indeed fit the mold, in the symbolically becoming their element: thornless roses. They become pretty, they become peaceful and caring, and they sprout new plants healing plants, they finally as the final expression of their legacy become a hive mind?... umm I guess that\u2019s supposed to make them into a garden? I\u2019m not sure it does the metaphor right. If I was making a legacy based on gardens, I focus on resonance and nodes, as those are similar to gardens, deep roots that the average person can\u2019t see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T08:41:58-07:00","id":1448992,"title":"","content":"TempleBuilder, do you mind if I clean up the Legacy write-up a bit? Fixing grammar and syntax, clarifying mechanics, things like that?<br /> <br /> re: a Tamer Legacy around gardens, I think your idea about resonance and nodes is good, a Prime/Life Thyrsus Legacy seems like a solid fit for gardeners.<br /> <br /> re: 1e Legacies: a lot of them are very messy and while many have cool themes, the mechanics are often broken or nonsensical even by 1e standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T08:52:28-07:00","id":1448993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448992#post1448992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TempleBuilder, do you mind if I clean up the Legacy write-up a bit? Fixing grammar and syntax, clarifying mechanics, things like that?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure, no problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448992#post1448992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">re: a Tamer Legacy around gardens, I think your idea about resonance and nodes is good, a Prime/Life Thyrsus Legacy seems like a solid fit for gardeners.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay, that\u2019s next on list then. Need to finish the previous legacies <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1448992#post1448992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">re: 1e Legacies: a lot of them are very messy and while many have cool themes, the mechanics are often broken or nonsensical even by 1e standards.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, that is a very good point. I do like the theme they are trying to present with the Roses of Eden, I just think the mechanics are wacky. Maybe I could make something with them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T10:52:38-07:00","id":1449011,"title":"","content":"Changes in <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">red</span>, comments in <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">blue</span>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Seekers of the Lotus (until I think of a better name)</b></span> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">how &quot;ancient&quot; you want the Legacy to be is going to influence the name, personally I like the idea of a Legacy like this tracing its roots back to either the Fangshi of China or being tied to the Ascending Ones of pre-Arab Egypt.</span><br /> <br /> description<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Better Living Through Chemistry</span></b><br /> <br /> There have always been those that seek knowledge of root and stem. Over time,<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Moros, Free Council, Nameless, Seers <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">unless you have a specific Nameless Order in mind I would remove &quot;Nameless&quot; from the parentage, it's too broad</span><br /> <b>Background</b>: <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The Seekers of the Lotus primarily pull their members from those with backgrounds in pharmaceutical chemistry, herbalism, and mortal alchemy.</span><br /> <b>Appearances</b>: Many are warped and twisted by the strange chemicals running in their veins, with signs of their preferred method of delivery.<br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Blights, Herbalist<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 2, Matter 2, Medicine 2, Science 2, Occult or Crafting 1<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Consumption and survival without magic of an extremely toxic mix of nightshade and Ape<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">ir</span>on. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This mixture, coupled with the reshaping of the vessel of their soul, primes the Herbalist's body to react to their infusions.</span> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">this seems a tad over deadly, I would either allow magic to be used or choose something less lethal.</span><br /> <b>Organization</b>: Pre-Great Refusal: A council overseen by the strongest legacy member. After Great Refusal: Master-Student chains<br /> <b>Theory</b>: Certain <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">m</span>aterials, when consumed or with exposure, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">a</span>ffect the body and mind. The <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Seekers of the Lotus</span> brew potions that elevate these effects to a wondrous degree.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>: Life<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">mundane chemical or alchemical ingredients</span> +1; <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">supernatural alchemical ingredients</span> +2; consumption of a prepared draught +1 (+2 if made with supernatural ingredients)<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: tending to a garden; studying a chemical formula; self-experimentation; spending at least a scene preparing a concoction<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">First: Taste the Root</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The Herbalist can spend a scene to prepare a concoction to open up their inner eye to the secrets of the alchemical universe, after which the Herbalist can determine the alchemical properties of plant and mineral with naught but a simple examination. The effects of the concoction last for the lower of the Herbalist's Life or Matter dots on the Advanced Duration chart, and the examination requires an instant action and tasting or otherwise handling the examined substance.<br /> This insight allows the Herbalist to replicate the feats of Mortal Alchemists, the Herbalist treats the lower of their Life or Matter dots as dots in any specialized form of Alchemy available to Mortals such as the Ascending One's Elixir Endowment or the Magnitude trait of the Alchemists described in <i>Promethean: the Created </i>2e. If the Herbalist already has such a Merit, use the Merit's value if higher and refund the experience per Sanctity of Merits if lower.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Second: Internal Alchemy</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 2, Matter 2, Medicine 3<br /> The Herbalists consume and use toxic materials on a daily basis <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">and this Attainment grants the Herbalist resistance</span> to <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">the</span> negative conditions caused by their creations<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">:</span> they are immune to bashing damage caused by handling <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">or consuming caustic or</span> toxic materials, and reduce lethal damage by their <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Matter</span> dots. The <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Herbalist</span> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">can </span>also <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">attempt to immediately flush their system of toxins, spending an Instant action to roll immediately to resist the toxin's effects, they </span>add <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">their</span> Life dots to <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">this roll</span>.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This Attainment negates any backlash or physiological drawback to consuming a potion derived from Mortal Alchemy, but not any mystical backlash or drawback.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Third: The Bitter Draught</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 3, Science 3, Crafts 2 or Occult 2<br /> The Herbalist may spend a scene <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">and a point of Mana</span> preparing a concoction. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">When</span> consumed by <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">the</span> Herbalist the potion <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">grants</span> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">1 + Life dots/2</span> ranks in each of the following:<ul><li>Breathing: <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Each rank halves</span> the amount of oxygen <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">the Herbalist</span> needs to function normally.</li> <li>Heartbeat: <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Each rank slows</span> the <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Herbalist's</span> heartbeat, <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">doubling</span> the interval at which a toxin affects her.</li> <li>Metabolism: <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Each rank regulates the Herbalist's</span> metabolism allow<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">ing</span> her to subsist on half as much food, and doubl<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">ing</span> the amount of time between checks for deprivation or fatigue.</li> <li>Reflexes: <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Each rank </span>add<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">s</span> +1 to the <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Herbalist</span>\u2019s Initiative.<br /> Scent: The <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Herbalist</span> can change <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">her</span> scent to any that her body could naturally produce, eliminating (or increasing) body odors, controlling pheromone release.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Healing: Each rank halves the healing time for bashing and lethal damage.</span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The effects of this potion last for an amount of time equal to the Herbalist's Life dots on the Advanced Duration chart.</span><br /> If the potion is <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">consumed by anyone other than the Herbalist that created it, it instead</span> acts as a deadly poison, with strength equal to the effect's potency of (1 + lower of Life or Matter dots)/2 and a duration based on the Mage's Life dots on the Advanced Duration chart, rolling every Lethal healing interval.<br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This attainment functions as the spell </span><i>Body Control</i> with the Permanence Attainment and 2 reach towards lethal healing.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Matter 3<br /> The Herbalist spend<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">s a</span> scene and a point of Mana to prepar<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">e</span> a concoction <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">capable of transforming whoever drinks it.</span> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The herbalist chooses a number of effects from the below list (or other, similar effects, with Storyteller permission) equal to their dots in Life to affect the potion's imbiber, the imbiber may Withstand the transformation with Stamina if they are unwilling:</span><ul><li>Claws: The subject gains savage claws, granting her a +1 weapon bonus.</li> <li>Environmental Adaptation: Like creatures adapted for life deep underwater or inhospitable deserts, the subject gains the ability to survive pressure, extreme heat or cold (up to level 4 environments), and arid or moisture-heavy environments. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This effect may be chosen multiple times, each time choose a different environment.</span></li> <li>Gills/Lungs: The subject may breathe underwater (or in air, if normally aquatic) freely.</li> <li>Immunities: The <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">subject gains</span> resistance to toxins or poisonous materials, like a rat\u2019s ability to devour even rotten food unharmed or herbivores\u2019 ability to fully digest plant matter. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This effect may be chosen multiple times, each time choose a different immunity.</span></li> <li>Leaping: Gaining powerful legs like a frog\u2019s or kangaroo\u2019s, the target gains a bonus to jumping rolls, increasing the distance leaped by each success on the Athletics roll.</li> <li>Prehensile Tail: Gain a bonus to rolls related to balance or climbing equal to Potency.</li> <li>Scaly Armor/Thick Hide: The subject gains 2/1 armor (must be at least Size 2).</li> <li>Senses: The subject gains a new sense, such as echolocation, primitive infravision, or a keen sense for vibrations, granting a bonus to Perception rolls and the ability to perceive phenomena outside the human senses.<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"> This effect may be chosen multiple times, each time choose a different sense.</span></li> <li>Size: Each level of rank either adds or subtracts one from the subject\u2019s Size. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If reduced to</span> Size 0 <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">the subject can be made</span> roughly the size of a dime. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The subject can grow to a size of up to 1 + (the lower of the Herbalist's Life or Matter dots)/2 on the Advanced Scale chart.</span></li> <li>Tentacles: The subject may make grappling attempts against targets up to her Size in feet away.</li> <li>Venom: The subject gains fangs or small stingers (damage bonus 0) capable of injecting venom with a Toxicity equal to the Herbalist's Life dots. Must grapple first unless a second level of this<br /> adaptation is taken. If taken with Tentacles, the Venom may be delivered automatically by any successful move during a grapple.</li> <li>Wall-Crawling: The subject (which can be no larger than Size 7) gains the ability to climb on surfaces without equipment or even handholds, provided the surface can bear her weight.</li> </ul><br /> This transformation last a scene. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">The potion, if unconsumed, retains its efficacy for the Herbalist's Matter dots on the Advanced Duration chart.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fourth: The Putrid Serum</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 4, Medicine 4.<br /> The Herbalist spend<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">s a</span> scene <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">and a point of Mana to</span> prepar<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">e</span> a concoction <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">that enhances the Herbalist's physical attributes</span>. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">When creating the concoction the Herbalist assigns 1 + Life dots/2 potency to up to two physical Attributes, drinking this concoction increases the Herbalist's Attributes by the chose potency for an amount of time equal to the Herbalist's Life dots on the Advanced Duration chart and can increase the Attributes above the Herbalist's normal limit. Drinking a second concoction ends the effects of the first and applies the new Attribute bonuses, however the duration of the effect is measured from the creation of the concoction, not its consumption.<br /> If the potion is consumed by anyone other than the Herbalist that created it, it instead acts as a deadly poison, with strength equal to the effect's potency of (1 + lower of Life or Matter dots)/2 and a duration based on the Mage's Life dots on the Advanced Duration chart, rolling every Lethal healing interval.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This Attainment replicates the effects of <i>Honing the Form</i> with the Permanence Attainment, the ability to boost attributes above the normal maximum, and the ability to increase two attributes.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Matter 4<br /> The Herbalist <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">can spend a scene and a point of Mana to</span> create a similar<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">,</span> but more potent<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"> and shorter lasting</span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">,</span> concoction <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">than</span> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">the above</span>. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rather than a long lasting, but small, boost to their own Attributes, the Herbalist can instead make a </span><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">potion that increases a single physical Attribute of the imbiber by the Herbalist's Life dots for a single scene, this effect can take the imbiber above their normal Attribute maximum. The potion, if unconsumed, retains its efficacy for the Herbalist's Matter dots on the Advanced Duration chart. If the Herbalist imbibes the potion the effect fully stacks with the Attribute bonus from the primary Attainment, rather than overwriting it or stacking transiently. </span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Maybe add &quot;A subject can only safely drink one such potion, each additional potion counts as a toxin with toxicity equal to potency and an interval of 1 minute.&quot;</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This Attainment replicates the effects of <i>Honing the Form</i> with the Permanence Attainment and reach to change the primary factor to potency and the ability to boost attributes above the normal maximum.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fifth: The Final Transmutation</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Life 5, Matter 5 two dots in a third Skill among the optional prerequisite Skills<br /> The Herbalist makes on<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">e</span> final potion<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">, their Magnum Opus</span>. <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If anyone other than the Herbalist that brewed it consumes this potion they die immediately.</span> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">After consuming the potion t</span>he Master Herbalist becomes something more than they once were, and possibly something less: they are <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">a</span> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">P</span>erfected <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">living being</span>. The Herbalist gains the rote action quality on any non-spellcasting action whose unmodified dice pool is 8 or greater. However, for any action whose base dice pool is 3 or less their failures are automatically dramatic. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">This honestly feels a bit unimpressive to me, since it doesn't really play in to the way perfected materials work. I also missed a bit in <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> where it says an entire person can't be perfected, so I dunno if this attainment should be reworked (the Herbalist can use their own parts as Perfected living materials that grow back) or completely changed.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 05-19-2021, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T12:03:42-07:00","id":1449024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449011#post1449011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This honestly feels a bit unimpressive to me, since it doesn't really play in to the way perfected materials work. I also missed a bit in Signs of Sorcery where it says an entire person can't be perfected, so I dunno if this attainment should be reworked (the Herbalist can use their own parts as Perfected living materials that grow back) or completely changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I chose it because the text reads <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of Sorcery page 42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Supernal Evolution (Prime): The Beast transforms the mage into pure Mana, allowing her to achieve her<b> perfected state</b>, before returning her to flesh. Mark all the Mana currently in her pool with an X; until she\u2019s spent all the marked points the mage gains the rote action quality on any non-spellcasting action whose unmodified dice pool is 8 or greater. However, for any action whose base dice pool is 3 or less, her failures are automatically dramatic failures&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> That's almost the same effect as the rote quality all ascended Ochemata get.<br /> Well the perfected living material have a few properties, they are always living, and can never die, and they reduce rote casting times in Grimoires. Perfected bones are as hard as iron. Perfected materials rely on both the physical properties of a subject and on the symbolic properties. For example, Orichalcum never corroding is due the the supposed purity of gold, more than any any other particular property. Lunargent reflects things in Twilight, because silver is associated with light, and light reveals.<br /> A fully Perfected body possibly never dies, even if the mind and soul depart. A perfectly preserved and living body with no mind or soul sounds perfect for something to make it's home there. Since it's no longer symbolically the mages body, but a totally separate thing that the mages soul just happens to be in. In exchange the Mage always has the effects of every perfected material that their body is made of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-19-2021, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T12:39:30-07:00","id":1449028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449024#post1449024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I chose it because the text reads That's almost the same effect as the rote quality all ascended Ochemata get.<br /> Well the perfected living material have a few properties, they are always living, and can never die, and they reduce rote casting times in Grimoires. Perfected bones are as hard as iron. Perfected materials rely on both the physical properties of a subject and on the symbolic properties. For example, Orichalcum never corroding is due the the supposed purity of gold, more than any any other particular property. Lunargent reflects things in Twilight, because silver is associated with light, and light reveals.<br /> A fully Perfected body possibly never dies, even if the mind and soul depart. A perfectly preserved and living body with no mind or soul sounds perfect for something to make it's home there. Since it's no longer symbolically the mages body, but a totally separate thing that the mages soul just happens to be in. In exchange the Mage always has the effects of every perfected material that their body is made of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just think the Boon is underwhelming as a capstone Attainment, is all.<br /> <br /> A never dying body would definitely be weird, but not sure what the Herbalist would get out of it.<br /> <br /> Another thought would be the Herbalist turns their body into an Eidoform, a vessel into which they can safely relinquish spells for 5 Mana instead of a dot of Willpower, and they can hold up to the lower of their Matter of Life dots in total dots of spells this way.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> A brief lowdown on HtV2e and PtC2e Alchemy:<br /> <br /> <br /> Ascending Ones (<i>Hunter: the Vigil</i> 2e):<ul><li>Ascending Ones take the Elixir Merit (\u25cf-\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf), this represents not just knowledge of how to make an elixir but also the training to use one.</li> <li>Dicepool for using an elixir is Stamina + Elixir; some don't in the manuscript, using Stamina + Medicine or Stamina + Presence, but hopefully those are mistakes.</li> <li>Researching a new elixir is an extended action requiring 10 successes on an Intelligence + Medicine roll with each roll representing a week.</li> <li>They get one elixir recipe per dot in the Elixir Merit.</li> <li>They can carry Stamina + Elixir elixirs on them.</li> <li>Most have a Willpower cost.</li> <li>Elixirs are toxic to anyone without the Merit</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Alchemists (<i>Promethean: the Created </i>2e):<ul><li>Alchemists use the Magnitude trait (\u25cf-\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf), this affects the number of Distillations they know, the amount of Pyros they can store (Pyros stolen from Prometheans is exempt from this limit) and how much they can spend per turn, and the amount of Pyros they create per week.</li> <li>Alchemists create Distillations based on the Transmutations of Prometheans and use the rules for those abilities.</li> <li>It's not stated, but I think Alchemists use Magnitude instead of Azoth as part of their rolls to create the distillation and to determine any effects.</li> <li>The rules here are looser since they're primarily meant for antagonists.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T13:10:24-07:00","id":1449038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449028#post1449028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I just think the Boon is underwhelming as a capstone Attainment, is all.<br /> <br /> A never dying body would definitely be weird, but not sure what the Herbalist would get out of it.<br /> <br /> Another thought would be the Herbalist turns their body into an Eidoform, a vessel into which they can safely relinquish spells for 5 Mana instead of a dot of Willpower, and they can hold up to the lower of their Matter of Life dots in total dots of spells this way.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was just thinking of side effects to doing this. I think if I am interpreting Signs of Sorcery right, the Herbalist literally can't die, even after they have been torn to shreds, and the pain is so great they can't concentrate on a spell. On the plus side, the mage can probably heal from limb loss or complete body loss. Any missing limbs probably do become perfected living materials once separated. I personally would say the soul departs past a certain point but the mage might still be alive and aware. They might even acquire a new soul. Or if they don't they spend forever in a coma as their mind break down.<br /> While becoming a Eidoform is fitting, I question the usefulness of relinquishing spells are to gnosis 7 mage. (I haven't played so it might be more useful than it appears.) Maybe the answer is to combine all 3, or any dice pool higher than 5 receives the rote quality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449028#post1449028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A brief lowdown on HtV2e and PtC2e Alchemy:<br /> <br /> <br /> Ascending Ones (<i>Hunter: the Vigil</i> 2e):<ul><li>Ascending Ones take the Elixir Merit (\u25cf-\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf), this represents not just knowledge of how to make an elixir but also the training to use one.</li> <li>Dicepool for using an elixir is Stamina + Elixir; some don't in the manuscript, using Stamina + Medicine or Stamina + Presence, but hopefully those are mistakes.</li> <li>Researching a new elixir is an extended action requiring 10 successes on an Intelligence + Medicine roll with each roll representing a week.</li> <li>They get one elixir recipe per dot in the Elixir Merit.</li> <li>They can carry Stamina + Elixir elixirs on them.</li> <li>Most have a Willpower cost.</li> <li>Elixirs are toxic to anyone without the Merit</li> </ul>Alchemists (<i>Promethean: the Created </i>2e):<ul><li>Alchemists use the Magnitude trait (\u25cf-\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf), this affects the number of Distillations they know, the amount of Pyros they can store (Pyros stolen from Prometheans is exempt from this limit) and how much they can spend per turn, and the amount of Pyros they create per week.</li> <li>Alchemists create Distillations based on the Transmutations of Prometheans and use the rules for those abilities.</li> <li>It's not stated, but I think Alchemists use Magnitude instead of Azoth as part of their rolls to create the distillation and to determine any effects.</li> <li>The rules here are looser since they're primarily meant for antagonists.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks. When in doubt, use the more stable rules. 2e Ascending Ones are the best bet. Their Elixirs are closer to the legacy anyhow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-19-2021, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T18:54:01-07:00","id":1449073,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Well, I think this should be interesting. This is only the start, I'm curious to see how this first attainment is </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">received. I'm basing the rest off of the first attainment, so I would like to see if it works before I continue. Edit: Nobody said anything, so I'm going to assume everything is good. I posted the second attainment.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Edit: Well, it's been a few days. I have had much less time to work on these compared to last week. I will finish, no promises on when though. I will be revising some of this today. Edit: Well, life got in the way, (it always does), so I'm posting my reasons for what I did. I am keeping the first draft saved so I can bring this first rough draft back if I have to. When I was making this, I wanted the Garden to increase in strength every level, but in retrospect that just bloats the legacy, so I am going to shave off the non vital bits. Edit: that went better than expected, adding proper attainments to the first attainment. I have started changing rough draft 2 into rough draft 3, so if you want to comment on rough draft 2 look at </span>proindrakenzol's post. Edit: On to draft 3. It seems nobody had any objections to the rest of my ideas besides the Demesne, which I'm scrapping.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Tamers of Roots</b></span><br /> <br /> She always was one to hang out all day in the orchard. She always tried to see the best in everyone, even when times were hard. She's back now, with new job tending the botanical garden, be she still has the same old smile. Heard she broke up some dumb old fight in the garden, even got everyone involve to apologize to each other.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Gardens of the Sacred</b></span><br /> <br /> There are tales of mythical Gardens, whose fruit contained magical power. Immortality, Knowledge, Power. Why were those Gardens grown, and why were those fruits special? The trees they grew from were ordinary things, really. No, the power came from the Roots, hidden beneath the surface. You see they were said to grow in Heaven, in Eden, in the Sacred. Not here. Not within reach.<br /> Look around you. The World is Broken, Fallen. It used to not be like this, but now it's wounded, and perhaps it will never be what it once was. It is the Mundane, the Profane. The Sacred is left out of reach.<br /> That's the trick, the lie, that you will never see the Sacred, never be there. But it's a <b>Lie</b>. A Lie that has cracks in it, cracks caused by the Roots of those Gardens. All we need to do is widen them, let them grow through cracks, and we can break down the lie, and let the World heal, and grow anew.<br /> <br /> What are the Roots? The Roots are power, hidden beneath the Surface. Others call them Ley lines, cracks in the Lie, but they don't see the Life in them. They don't see how they push up into the world like new sprouts, How they can be tended and nursed to grow strong. They don't see how that sprout grows into a whole Garden, and how that Garden changes the world.<br /> <br /> Long ago, in a ancient part of the world, a seeker of truth found a hidden grotto. Who they were is long lost, only what they found remains. Inside the cave they found a beautiful Garden, with all the plants growing as though they had been cared for lovingly, but with no sign that anyone had ever set foot in this cave. Tired from their journey, they sat beneath a great tree, and soon, slept. They dreamed. Dreamt of Root pushing, digging into soil, into rock. They Dreamt of a Ivory tower falling, crashing and a Hungry Black Sea that swallowed everything in it's path. They dreamt of tending a garden as penance for some overwhelming crime, discovering the Garden was growing powerful, strong and Beautiful. And that it would outlast them. And they Finally dreamt of a faint presence asking if they would tend to the Garden in their stead. When they awoke, they felt the pulsing beat of power just beneath their feet. They felt the Roots pushing against...something. They resolved to tend to this Holy place, and know it's Truths.<br /> That was a Long Time Ago, and things have changed. The legacy has always been around in one form or another, never really coming into the spotlight. It found it's way into the groups that would become the Mysterium, tending to their stores of knowledge as well as the gardens. It was chiefly though of as a way to store knowledge through the generations, and simultaneously a way to make the defense of a Athaneum that much easier. That all changed when a young and hopeful member of the Silver Ladder was found worthy to be taught the secrets of the Legacy. From the moment she saw the the legacy, she knew it's potential. She dreamed of being able to shatter the barriers the Tyrants placed on the world, and bring real change, all without needing to fight. Her passion, her love of the world and of peace has been carried on through the legacy ever since. These days, the Legacy isn't as close to each other as they used to be. They spread out, all around the World. Where ever there are large concentrations of Roots, the Legacy thrives. The Legacy knows that the world is what you make of it, and want a world of harmony, of happiness and hope. Even within the Legacy, many doubt that the Legacy alone can shatter the Lie. The same still believe that they are making a difference, making the world a little less Fallen. The Legacy believes always trying for the best outcome. Even if everything seems hopeless, someone has to try for a better outcome, or it will never happen. Legacy is not naive, and they know that sometimes there are no right answers. The Legacy knows that actions have unforeseen consequences, and that resonance makes more resonance. They believe the conflict only makes more conflict, and to have a better world, you need to act better. The Legacy knows the Seers probably won't change, but they have to try. Even if they won't change, they might still be persuaded. They give everyone a chance, so the world might be that much better. There is a exception to this rule. Just one. Scelesti. The Legacy is vulnerable to the Abyss's touch, and any paradox condition the Flower Girl suffers usually is also suffered by their Garden. The reverse is also true. Paradox in the Garden goes deep, tainting Roots and spreading far outside the Garden. The legacy has been targeted by Scelesti for thousands of years, seeking to spread the Abyss's influence far into the Fallen. The Legacy has strong guidelines on risking Paradox, and on Containing it. One can imagine the response to finding out someone actually serves the Abyss.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Thyrsus, Silver Ladder, Mysterium,<br /> <b>Background</b>: Background of average member.<br /> <b>Appearances</b>: Many have green stained fingers, mainly thumbs, and many wear flowers in clothes and hair<br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Gardeners, Flower Girls/Boys, Hippies<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Life 1, Craft or Survival 3, Expression 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Gardening)<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Creation of a soul seed with a senior legacy member assistance, and planting and nurturing it for a full lunar cycle past its sprouting inside of the Node they wish to bond with.<br /> <b>Organization</b>: Small Cabals that have a few links to each other, every equinox the entire legacy meets to discuss any issues concerning the legacy and problems individual members might have.<br /> <b>Theory</b>: The Gardeners know that there are cracks in the lie, places where the Supernal meets the Fallen. The places can, with help, grow and with time may completely overwhelm shatter the lie.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>: Prime<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: Flowers appropriate to the spell+1; +2 if a supernatural flower; Inside the Garden +2; success of an expression roll relating to the spell +2; in order to help the subject grow +1<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: Tending to a garden; Creating a work of art; Removing Pollution; Resolving a Potentially Hostile Situation Non-Violently<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">First: The Garden</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation<br /> The Roots show themselves to those that would seek them. After a scene of meditation with her Soul Seed or Soul Plant, The Flower Girl senses Ley Lines and Nodes. If there are no Nodes or Ley Lines within sensory range, she know the direction to the nearest Node or Ley Line.<br /> <br /> Every initiate has a Garden, one they have tended to since it was but simple seed. After the first lunar cycle after sprouting, the soul plant rapidly grows into a young but mature specimen of its kind. This Soul Plant must grow from the Heart of the Node. This act binds the Node to the Flower Girl and her Legacy, transforming the Node into a Garden. The Flower Girl has a Connected Sympathetic Connection to the Garden and is always Attuned to the Garden. The area of the Garden is the area of the Node, with the Creators Prime dots acting as the number of ley lines flowing into the Node. The Flower Girl senses anything that would trigger her Peripheral Mage Sight as though she was standing at every point in her Garden. She also senses anything around plants from her Garden connected by a Ley Line. As a instant action the Flower Girl may split her senses between herself and her Garden, looking as though she was standing in any space within the garden. The Flower Girl has a 360-degree field of view. She may also change her view from any plant or their seeds from her Garden, as long as they are rooted in a Ley Line originating from her Garden. Mages may Attune as normal, but Sleepers that spend a lunar cycle in the Node become Attuned. Plants in the area automatically become Attuned. The resonance flowing out of the Node is influenced by by the Legacy, the Flower Girl\u2019s Nimbus, and her actions. This effect is limited to the effect as if the Flower Girl was always inside her Garden. Her long term Nimbus always effects the Garden.-<i>(Not constantly active, but no amount of Wisdom or Shadow Name will reduce the long term Nimbus' effects)</i><br /> <br /> List of Node effects:<br /> \u2022 Forces: By precisely aligning a stationary piece of technology that requires heat or electricity to function, the Attuned may use the Node to power it.<br /> \u2022 Life: The Attuned may harness the Node to bring any plant put there to any point it its life cycle, as long as that point would take a year or less. These changes require a day to complete and a successful Intelligence + Crafts or Intelligence + Survival roll.<br /> \u2022 Matter: Unless totally destroyed, stationary, inanimate objects built in alignment with local Resonance heal one point of Structure per day. Their permanent Structure may slowly wear down due to environmental conditions, but at half the usual rate.<br /> \u2022 Space: Those who are Attuned acquire a +2 bonus to tasks that require significant movement through space, including driving, running, and certain athletic feats.<br /> \u2022 Time: The Attuned benefit from a +2 bonus to Initiative.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plants that grow within the Garden and drink of its resonance grow strong, healthy, beautiful, and faster than normal. This effect is limited to effects a plant would experience if it was raised in perfect conditions.<br /> <br /> This Garden is the heart of the Legacy, the foundation point. If a Flower Girl\u2019s Garden is destroyed, the Legacy attainments ceases to function, although she is still a member of the Legacy. In the event of a Garden being completely destroyed, the Flower may create a new Soul Seed. This requires a seed of size 2 or below, and the expenditure of 1 mana and 1 willpower. A Flower Girl may also transfer the soul seed to another seed at any time for the same cost as making a new Soul Seed. The moment the Soul Seed is transferred, the Garden starts to slowly lose its magic with the attainments failing each week one by one starting with the highest attainment the Flower Girl has. No matter how long she may go without a Garden, a flower Girl always has this Attainment. When replanting, the garden takes one week to regain one level of the Legacy. The seed may only be Planted within the Heart of a Node.<br /> <br /> When the Flower Girl passes away, as all must in the end, part of her will remain in the Garden. This Echo is not a Ghost, and does not respond to Death. It tends to the garden in the Flower Girls absence, and defends it as she would. Build as a Ghost Mage (the non-lich kind) with the Garden as it's Anchor, and it can use Attainments as she would. Mages may use a Prime version of Goetic Evocation or the Echo Chamber merit to communicate with the Echo. Legacy members theorize that the Echo is a living Nimbus Knot, drawn from the Flower Girls Connection to her Garden. It may even be present before the Flower Girl's death.-(I am toying on when exactly a Echo would appear. It definitely doesn't need the final attainment but becomes much rarer the less Gnosis invested into the Legacy. This probably would make a fine mystery)<br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 2<br /> The Flower Girl hears the whisper of vine and bloom. After spending a scene meditating with her Soul Seed or Soul Plant, the Flower Girl may speak and hear any plant. this lasts for her Life dots of steps on the Advanced Duration chart. The words of plants are not verbal communications, requiring the Flower girl to feel or smell the scents plant gives off. Most plants have little understanding of human concepts, and are unconcerned with such things. What plants do know is what they feel, and they feel both the world above the ground and the world below the surface. Many plants are sensitive to the Roots, especially Plants growing in the Garden. Plants also understand the situation that they grow in remarkably well, and a Flower Girl may take the Informed(Gardening this Plant) condition after conversing with a plant. Many Plants can move, and may be persuaded to grow in a particular direction.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Second:</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Expression 3, Area of Expertise (Gardening)<br /> <br /> <br /> The stronger bond allows the Flower Girl to take some of the Power of her Garden with her on her travels. After spending a scene tending to her Garden, the Flower Girl carries part of the Node within herself, acting as if she was within the Nodes boundaries. This effect lasts for her Prime dot\u2019s steps on the advanced duration chart. She may share this Attunement with anyone she touches for a Mana, although doing only lasts a scene. Anyone she shares the Attunement with permanently becomes Attuned to the Garden\u2019s Node, but can only benefit while in the boundaries of the Garden.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 2<br /> &quot;The Flower Girl can detect all living things, or any category of living thing, nearby or that comes within range during the duration of the effect with an Instant Action and in an area equal to 1 + Life dots/2 on the Advanced Scale: Area chart and lasts for a number of turns equal to her Life dots. This effect is always active on her Garden, letting her know everything within or entering her garden at all times. This Attainment emulates the spell <i>Web of Life</i> with reach assigned to Advanced Scale and either Advanced Duration (for the Garden) or Instant Cast (when used outside the Garden).&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Third:</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 3, Craft or Survival 4<br /> When the Lie cracks, Truth bleeds through. The Garden glows with Truths. Without direction this creates a general aura of revelations similar to a long term Nimbus of such, generally related to the Resonance of the Garden. While in the garden, the Flower Girl may spend a scene tending to her Garden, this focuses the Truths into a message. The message can be any length, but the Flower Girl must know that it is true. This message can be felt by anyone who spends any time within or examining the Garden, unless the message would be false for them. For example, if a Flower Girl leaves a message saying &quot;I love you&quot;, only those she loves will get the message. Everyone who hears the Message knows it to be True in their Soul. This create a Lasting Inspired or Guilty conditions and if used in Social Maneuvering, this removes one Door or raises the impression level by a step per half the Flower Girl's dots in Prime plus one. The message lasts for the Flower Girl's dots in Prime steps on the advanced duration chart. The Flower Girl may change the message with another ritual. When outside the Garden, the Flower Girl may spend a point of Mana to cast Words of Truth with scale: area of effect and reach for instant and the reach to create the inspired or guilty conditions. This affects anyone with a composure of less than her dots in Prime.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 3<br /> Root and stem listen to the Flower Girl, following her Awakened Will. While inside her Garden, and spending a scene tending to her Garden, the Flower Girl can command plants around her to move. Plants in the area can be moved however the Flower Girl desires, in an area with lots of plants the Flower Girl can impose a penalty to speed and rolls relying on movement equal to the Flower Girl's dots in Life. The Flower Girl can also direct large plants, such as trees, to attack using Wits + 1+(Life/2) as the dicepool, damage dealt is bashing or lethal depending on the type of plant (vines would deal bashing, an oak would deal lethal, thorns maybe be complicated), and the weapon modifier is equal to the plant's size. The Flower Girl may instead have the Plant grapple a opponent, using Wits +1+(Life/2)+ Size - Defense. <i>(this dice pool probably needs work) </i>This effect lasts for the Flower Girl's dots in Life on the advance duration chart and is in advance scale: area of effect dots in Life. The Flower Girl may spend a Mana and a instant action to use this outside of the Garden, but it only lasts her dots in Life turns.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fourth:</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 4, Expression 4.<br /> The Flower Girl's connection is such that the Roots will bend to her Will. After a scene meditating in a Ley Line, the flower Girl may redirect ley lines within a area of her Life dots on the advance scale, reshaping Nodes and altering Resonance as a instant action. She may move ley lines, and therefore the Nodes created where ley lines cross, \u201cpinning\u201d a line to a point within the area of effect of the spell. She may also change the Resonance Keyword of a Node to whatever she wishes. This lasts for the Flower Girl's dots in Life on the advanced duration, before returning to normal.<br /> <br /> In addition, the Flower Girl may purchase the Hallow Merit for her Garden, the resulting Hallow spontaneously appears at the Heart of the Garden. -<i>Is this fine?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 4<br /> The Roots of the Garden drink deep from the resonance past the lie. Body control with advanced duration, and +2 reach toward lethal healing quicker, on both the Flower Girl and the Garden. Anything Attuned to the Garden benefits while in the Garden.<br /> <br /> In addition, supernatural plants can grow in the Garden as if they had the proper amount of what they need to exist. Many Flower Girls obtain Crypto-Flora, Goblin Fruit, and Mandrakes from other supernatural creatures. -<i>Small addition that amused me. </i><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fifth:</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 5, Life 5, Craft or Survival 5, Expression 5<br /> The Garden finally grows to its truest potential. Both the Garden and its Flower Girl are connected on such intimate level that is functionally no difference between the two. And from the union of Gnosis, Root, Soul, and Stem comes a living symbol of that connection. The Soul Plant becomes a Living Soul Stone. <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Soul Plant has a number of properties that separate it from a normal Soul Stone. It acts as a +3 yantra for it's Flower Girl. The Soul Plant makes no Demesne or A</span>nnullity. <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Soul Plant does not reduce the maximum Gnosis of the Flower Girl. The Soul Plant can only be dedicated if the Flower Girl has the Broad Dedication Merit. It is a normal Soul Stone in every other regard.<br /> <br /> Instead of a Demesne or Annullity, The Garden Perfects it's Node, and Extends it's effects onto Living Things. The Node effects becomes:</span><br /> <br /> \u2022 Forces: The Attuned need no rest, nor food. They always are full of energy. They ignore wound penalties.<br /> \u2022 Life: The Attuned can heal from any wound, given enough time, unless they outright die. Scars fade, Limbs regrow.<br /> \u2022 Matter: Unless totally destroyed, the Attuned gain a general armor equal to 1 +(Prime/2).<br /> \u2022 Space: Those who are Attuned know where everything is around them, they don't need to roll to find a path or trail. They add Prime dots to Roll requiring precise movement though space.<br /> \u2022 Time: The Attuned's memories become sharp and clear. They don't need to roll to remember. They add Prime dots to rolls to predict consequence and to rolls to understand the Consequences of their actions.<br /> <br /> From the Soul Plant comes special seeds. Every solar year, a number of seeds equal to the Flower Girl's dots in Life can be harvested. These seeds, when planted in a Ley Line that is connected to one of the ley lines from the original Garden, grows into a new Garden, with its own Node. New Ley Lines emerge from the new Node and the process continues. For the purposes of Attainments, these new Gardens are considered extensions of the original. The new Gardens only grow to an area as if they had added another Ley Line to the intersection. Many of these new Gardens attract caretakers, many of whom become Attuned Sleepwalkers over a extended period of time.-<i>(The seeds act as their own Ley Line, making a intersection if there was not one before, this only happens when the plant sprouts after being planted)</i><br /> <br /> If instead the seed is planted into the Flower Girl's Garden, it instead expands the radius of the Garden by one Ley Line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 06-02-2021, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-20T13:34:59-07:00","id":1449139,"title":"","content":"First draft of the Tamers of roots is finished, it needs a lot of work to perfect. The later attainments especially, because I ran out of ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T12:02:12-07:00","id":1449364,"title":"","content":"I feel the first Attainment is trying to do too much. Creating a Node is a Prime 5 effect or multiple geomantic effects. Creating an artificial soul stone is a pretty powerful effect, perhaps for the fourth or fifth Attainments. The Resonance should probably fit the mage rather than be fixed by the Legacy. Some additional commentary should probably be dedicated on how it mitigates Paradox for the caster, how individual pieces are connected to their Nimbus and if they can be used as Dedicated Tools. Finally, the incorporation of so many optional Arcana seems like spreading itself too wide, especially since the effects don't all follow a central theme (the effects for Space and Time seem to have no correlation to the growth and serenity themes).<br /> <br /> The first part of the secondary effect is a Prime 4 Patterning and therefore way too powerful to be implemented at this level. The optional effect might run into problems if the shaping does not respect the laws of physics, causing the garden to collapse once duration ends. In addition, there may simply not be enough organic matter for all the required fortifications.<br /> <br /> The third optional Attainment feels like its trying to do too much with too many Arcana.<br /> <br /> The fourth main Attainment replicates too many effects at once. Ephemeral Enchantment, Words of Truth, Stealing Fire, protection from Breaking Points (which seems unrelated to either Arcana) and granting rote quality (which should cost a mana and only affect a limited number of rolls). It needs to be distilled into one effect.<br /> <br /> The fourth optional Attainment probably is a Patterning of Prime and Life, therefore it requires advanced scale (to cover the entire garden) and advanced duration for optimal results, leaving it one Reach over the limit.<br /> <br /> Regarding the fifth Attainment, the spell Create Truth is being replicated. Normally it requires mana equal to 5 * Potency, which even truncated by Legacy mana rules means it should cost a mana and last up to a year. In addition, the spell is resisted by the dot rating of the Hallow, meaning it cannot have Prime dots in rating, even applying the pseudo dice for extra factors.<br /> <br /> The optional fifth Attainment can create a different garden via a permanent transform life and even give the plant a quick reproduction or growth cycle. However, the caretaker becoming a Sleepwalker is the result of Stealing Fire and giving them an Obsession is the result of Forge Purpose, which means the Attainment has 3 effects rather than one.<br /> <br /> Overall, they feel like the theme is being spread too thin between: one with nature, an honest place and a place that cultivates the self. Right now it would be a good idea to choose one to focus on entirely.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-24-2021, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T13:57:30-07:00","id":1449373,"title":"","content":"So I was editing the stuff on my own, and just happened to notice you commented. I changed a bunch of stuff just now, maybe it works slightly better and is similar to what you posted about. Maybe.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449364#post1449364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the first Attainment is trying to do too much. Creating a Node is a Prime 5 effect or multiple geomantic effects. Creating an artificial soul stone is a pretty powerful effect, perhaps for the fourth or fifth Attainments. The Resonance should probably fit the mage rather than be fixed by the Legacy. Some additional commentary should probably be dedicated on how it mitigates Paradox for the caster, how individual pieces are connected to their Nimbus and if they can be used as Dedicated Tools. Finally, the incorporation of so many optional Arcana seems like spreadong itself too wide, especially since the effects don't all follow a central theme (the effects for Space and Time seem to have no correlation to the growth and serenity themes).</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for commenting on this. This is pretty much exactly what I need to hear. I have been worried since I first made this that it might be too much. But nobody commented, so I proceeded anyway. I think I might move the Soul stone bit to the Final Attainment, with the main thing being the Legacy claiming a wild Node to make the Garden. I had planned on it being able to be dedicated with the signs of sorcery merits that change what you can dedicate, but never wrote that down. The extra charges of the node are all prime effects. It is still probably not a Prime 1 effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449364#post1449364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first part of the secondary effect is a Prime 4 Patterning and therefore way too powerful to be implemented at this level. The optional effect might run into problems if the shaping does not respect the laws of physics, causing the garden to collapse once duration ends. In addition, there may simply not be enough organic matter for all the required fortifications.</div> </div> </div> </div> The First part is Patterning? I thought it was like the nimbus tilt from signs of sorcery that makes a condition that carries the nimbus tilt on a person indefinitely. Creating a condition from appropriate conditions is Ruling, right?<br /> I never meant for physics to be broken with the optional effect. I may have accidently forgotten not worded it correctly? The effect is meant only have the plant grow in ways plants can Normally grow, just with the mage determining how it does it. the only physics breaking part is the enhanced speed, I think?<br /> That last bit actually is on purpose. The legacy is biased to Gardens with Lots of Plant Biomass. I will mention that if I bring back the merits.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449364#post1449364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third optional Attainment feels like its trying to do too much with too many Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div> In my defense, Nodes only need Prime to mess with charges. Since I had the Node set up to have multiple charges, a perfecting effect would enhance all the properties of Node. Still isn't Life, and still messed up the reach. I moved this part up a spot, and turned it into body control.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449364#post1449364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fourth main Attainment replicates too many effects at once. Ephemeral Enchantment, Words of Truth, Stealing Fire, protection from Breaking Points (which seems unrelated to either Arcana) and granting rote quality (which should cost a mana and only affect aimited number of rolls). It needs to be distilled into one effect.</div> </div> </div> </div> Definitely, that's why I removed it. I actually thought Prime Legacies could protect from Supernal caused Breaking Points. Is that not the case?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449364#post1449364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fourth optional Attainment probably is a Patterning of Prime and Life, therefore it requires advanced scale (to cover the entire garden) and advanced duration for optimal results, leaving it one Reach over the limit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Removed, because I think it didn't fit the legacy. Actually I wondered about the Practice. What Practice is merging into a object, and What Practice is merging two separate but Connected Sympathetically object?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449364#post1449364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the fifth Attainment, the spell Create Truth is being replicated. Normally it requires mana equal to 5 * Potency, which even truncated by Legacy mana rules means it should cost a mana and last up to a year. In addition, the spell is resisted by the dot rating of the Hallow, meaning it cannot have Prime dots in rating, even applying the pseudo dice for extra factors.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I realized I could do this with Weaving because I had a Node there. Now the Withstand part is interesting, I completely missed that. I bet even a Weaving would have the same Withstand. Going to math it out later.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449364#post1449364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The optional fifth Attainment can create a different garden via a permanent transform life and even give the plant a quick reproduction or growth cycle. However, the caretaker becoming a Sleepwalker is the result of Stealing Fire and giving them an Obsession is the result of Forge Purpose, which means the Attainment has 3 effects rather than one.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep, removed because it absolutely didn't work.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449364#post1449364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, they feel like the theme is being spread too thin between: one with nature, an honest place and a place that cultivates the self. Right now it would be a good idea to choose one to focus on entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I'm trying to fix that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449364#post1449364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hope that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-23-2021, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T12:56:05-07:00","id":1449689,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> Do you think the First Attainment would work better as a weird Tamers of Roots living souls stone with all the downsides including the reduction of maximum Gnosis, or as a Node the First Attainment binds to the Legacy Member acting as a pseudo Familiar. (My goal for the first Attainment to have a Connected sympathetic connection to their Garden or their Soul Plant that actually benefits them while in the Garden.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T15:28:29-07:00","id":1449712,"title":"","content":"Another option is to make it an extension of their senses. They have a Connected sympathy to the garden and are able to perceive things via Peripheral Mage Sight happening near it (like a soul stone). With an action, they can swap their senses to anywhere near the garden. <br /> <br /> They could also do this on a plant taken from it, provided it lies in the same ley line as the garden.<br /> <br /> However, the big question is theme are you going for ? Using a single phrase, with no pauses or commas, how would you describe this Legacy ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T17:01:55-07:00","id":1449731,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m at work so rushed reply.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449712#post1449712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option is to make it an extension of their senses. They have a Connected sympathy to the garden and are able to perceive things via Peripheral Mage Sight happening near it (like a soul stone). With an action, they can swap their senses to anywhere near the garden.<br /> <br /> They could also do this on a plant taken from it, provided it lies in the same ley line as the garden.<br /> <br /> However, the big question is theme are you going for ? Using a single phrase, with no pauses or commas, how would you describe this Legacy ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I used \u201cgardeners of the sacred\u201d but I guess that is not very clear. Maybe \u201cNurture the World you want\u201d. If I was allowed commas and periods and song lyrics , \u201c this is the world we live in, these are the hands we give her. Let\u2019s get and let\u2019s start trying to make it a place worth living in\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T17:44:53-07:00","id":1449735,"title":"","content":"What I am not clear about is: what are the Roots ? Tamer Legacies relate the physical phenomenon they tame to a metaphysical concept, seeing them as one and the same. The Tamers of Fire see their element as passion given form and power. The Tamers of Rivers see them as being change made manifest, the Tamers of Wind see gales and gusts as knowledge and so on. But what are the Roots ? What do they symbolically represent and how are they being tamed, harnessed ? <br /> <br /> Even though you mentioned the themes of the Roses of Eden are not what you are looking for, there exists a 2ed conversion whose Attainments seem to capture the feel of what you are looking for:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1180101#post1180101\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1180101#post1180101\"> Even more Legacies, updated to 2E - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1180101#post1180101\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1180101#post1180101 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm using this thread as both a homebrew hub, venue for receiving criticisms, and way to receive suggestions for conversions should anyone reading this be </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T21:37:55-07:00","id":1449755,"title":"","content":"Wow today has been eventful. I\u2019m just home from work, and a flat tire, and a major car wreck (I wasn\u2019t involved, but I\u2019m pretty someone didn\u2019t make it). Standard disclaimer about tiredness aside, I will try to answer this in full. Maybe it will even make sense when I try to read this in the morning.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449735#post1449735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I am not clear about is: what are the Roots ? Tamer Legacies relate the physical phenomenon they tame to a metaphysical concept, seeing them as one and the same. The Tamers of Fire see their element as passion given form and power. The Tamers of Rivers see them as being change made manifest, the Tamers of Wind see gales and gusts as knowledge and so on. But what are the Roots ? What do they symbolically represent and how are they being tamed, harnessed ?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Roots are Ley Lines and Nodes, being the roots of Magic. Magic is a Living thing, and is often compared to a tree, specifically a Tree of Knowledge. Ley Lines look like the Roots of tree, with Nodes being the source or the stem rising out into the fallen world. Fallen plants are basically the same thing, drinking in unseen nutrients and water. In the metaphor, the ground the tree sits on is the Lie, and the legacy may be able to destroy the Lie by covering the world in Gardens, but that is a extremely distant pipe dream, and may not even work.<br /> The legacy works by investing a part of themselves into a crack in the lie, widen it through their Attainments, and draw on that power for further Attainments. Since I\u2019m working with plant metaphors, a garden results from the excess ley energy from the Node, making the area even more sacred. Eventually both the Supernal and the Fallen world around the crack in the Lie are filled with plants, whose roots further widen it. Of course the Mage is tied to the land now, and must tend to it lest others destroy what they have made. Hmm maybe I should have done a King and his Land are One as the summarization. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449735#post1449735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though you mentioned the themes of the Roses of Eden are not what you are looking for, there exists a 2ed conversion whose Attainments seem to capture the feel of what you are looking for:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1180101#post1180101\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...01#post1180101</a></div> </div> </div> </div> The Roses of Eden are almost the same thing as this legacy, because they are Tamers Of Thornless Roses or Tamers of Flowers. The thing is, their symbolism and point is kind of weird, being caught up in their new garden of Eden metaphor, and managing to still cover lot of related concepts slightly. They also get weird with path symbolism, and other things. I think the big difference is that the Roses focus on Gardens as People, building cults and becoming perfect pacifistic plant people, becoming the thornless Roses of Eden. Meanwhile the Tamers of Roots focus on Gardens as a Place in the World, building a Place of Power and becoming Rooted. That in my mind is a big enough difference to separate the two. After all, the Silver Ladder and the Free Council are similar, they both focus on being rebels, and sleepers, but I don\u2019t think anyone is seriously suggesting that there is no need for the Silver Ladder because the Free Council exists... in real life anyway. Maybe you disagree on the two legacies being distinct. Which is fine, I probably will slowly continue to rewrite the Tamers of Roots for a little more.<br /> <br /> With all of that said, yes there are similarities. Both legacies draw from some of the same metaphors. Both even use plants, in different ways. Which means that the Attainments are going to overlap somewhat as well. That being said, maybe I should focus on making Yantras to further separate the Prime parts, and maybe focus on more plant manipulation as the life part. By no means is this legacy finished, I just rather suddenly have much less time to work on it.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a pretty good conversion though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T10:56:49-07:00","id":1449823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449712#post1449712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option is to make it an extension of their senses. They have a Connected sympathy to the garden and are able to perceive things via Peripheral Mage Sight happening near it (like a soul stone). With an action, they can swap their senses to anywhere near the garden.<br /> <br /> They could also do this on a plant taken from it, provided it lies in the same ley line as the garden.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that last line, probably going to include it. I wanted the Garden to spread, but never could really get it to feel right. It also plays into living magic which is nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T20:15:21-07:00","id":1449912,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of bringing back the Safe Place and Sanctum merits. As KaiserAfini pointed out, if this is just from the plants, then there will be dead zones where that effect is not active. Now that\u2019s not necessarily a bad thing, it emphasizes seeding the area with new life. None the less, I wonder if I could have the resonance have a effect, something like a resonance auto immune response. I think the Initiative bonus should be active anywhere inside of the Garden but maybe the traps wouldn\u2019t be. I actually thought invaders would get a Initiative penalty in the Garden, but it seems that that\u2019s not the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:03:25-07:00","id":1449923,"title":"","content":"The more I think about it, the more I see the Roots as being linked to the <a href=\"https://mushi-shi.fandom.com/wiki/The_River_of_Light\" target=\"_blank\">River of Light from Mushishi</a><br /> <br /> The river would be the roots and the beings that dwell within, those that are closer to the origin of life than sentient beings, are the sap that can be used to cultivate the future. The Gardeners are those adept at perceiving the sap, redirecting its flow by moving the roots and drawing the beings within to the surface. Perhaps exploring that could provide inspiration on how to go about cultivating it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:07:55-07:00","id":1449925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449923#post1449923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I think about it, the more I see the Roots as being linked to the <a href=\"https://mushi-shi.fandom.com/wiki/The_River_of_Light\" target=\"_blank\">River of Light from Mushishi</a><br /> <br /> The river would be the roots and the beings that dwell within, those that are closer to the origin of life than sentient beings, are the sap that can be used to cultivate the future. The Gardeners are those adept at perceiving the sap, redirecting its flow by moving the roots and drawing the beings within to the surface. Perhaps exploring that could provide inspiration on how to go about cultivating it.</div> </div> </div> </div> The what now? I\u2019m going to have to look at this in depth. I have never seen or heard of this series. Is it good? Edit: Wow, that is uncanny. That\u2019s almost exactly how I imagined the Roots. The only difference seems to be the presence of the Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-28-2021, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:22:14-07:00","id":1449933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449925#post1449925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The what now? I\u2019m going to have to look at this in depth. I have never seen or heard of this series. Is it good? Edit: Wow, that is uncanny. That\u2019s almost exactly how I imagined the Roots. The only difference seems to be the presence of the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mushishi is something pretty different. Its quiet and creative, emotional and with a tranquil flow. Its an amazing series to wind down to. While the lore that is relevant to the Legacy might be limited, its so solidly written that I find it difficult not to recommend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-27T21:25:07-07:00","id":1449934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449933#post1449933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mushishi is something pretty different. Its quiet and creative, emotional and with a tranquil flow. Its an amazing series to wind down to. While the lore that is relevant to the Legacy might be limited, its so solidly written that I find it difficult not to recommend.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will add it to the list then. I should warn my backlog of stuff to watch is rather large, as I focus a bit heavily on video games. I will get to it sometime, but that time probably isn\u2019t soon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T12:20:20-07:00","id":1450035,"title":"","content":"First try on the redone soul plant. I had a idea, I'm not sure if it is a attainment, but that the connection between a Tamer and her Roots will last until both are destroyed. Essentially, I was thinking that the Garden would be &quot;haunted&quot; by a nimbus knot or evocation that had access to the attainments of the legacy in the event of the mages death. The knot could gain Mana through gardening in order to use the Mana costing Attainments and take care of the Garden like the Flower Girl would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T14:44:06-07:00","id":1450075,"title":"","content":"Alright I think rough draft version two is ready. Any thoughts, comments, concerns, and/or criticisms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T16:01:57-07:00","id":1450093,"title":"","content":"<s>Muhahaha, time to rain on your parade again!</s><br /> <br /> Oh, another neat Legacy idea to offer constructive criticism on!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1449073#post1449073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Parentage</b>: Thyrsus, Silver Ladder, Mysterium,<br /> <b>Background</b>: Background of average member.<br /> <b>Appearances</b>: Many have green stained fingers, mainly thumbs, and many wear flowers in clothes and hair<br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Gardeners, Flower Girls/Boys, Hippies</div> </div> </div> </div>I am now picturing Perfuma from <i>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Life 1, Craft 3, Expression 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Gardening)<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Creation of a soul seed with a senior legacy member assistance, and planting and nurturing it for a full lunar cycle past it\u2019s sprouting<br /> <b>Organization</b>: Small Cabals that have a few links to each other, every equinox the entire legacy meets to discuss any issues concerning the legacy and problems individual members might have<br /> <b>Theory</b>: The Gardeners know that there are cracks in the lie, places where the Supernal meets the Fallen. The places can, with help, grow and with time may completely overwhelm shatter the lie. </div> </div> </div>I feel like gardening would be more Survival than Crafts, personally, but I do like Expression for things like arrangement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>: Prime<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: Flowers appropriate to the spell+1; +2 if a supernatural flower; Inside the Garden +2; success of an expression roll relating to the spell +2; in order to help the subject grow +1<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: Tending to a garden; Creating a work of art; Removing Pollution; Resolving a Potentially Hostile Situation Non-Violently </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">First: The Garden</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation.<br /> Every initiate has a Garden, one they have tended to since it was but simple seed. After the first lunar cycle after sprouting, the soul plant rapidly grows into a young but mature specimen of its kind. This Soul Plant must grow from the Heart of the Node. This act connects binds the Node to the Flower Girl and her Legacy, transforming the Node into a Garden. The Flower Girl has a Connected Sympathetic Connection to the Garden. The area of the Garden is the area of the Node, with the Creators Prime dots acting as the number of ley lines flowing into the node. The Flower Girl senses anything that would trigger her Peripheral Mage Sight as though she was standing at every point in her Garden. She also senses anything around plants from her Garden connected by a Ley Line. As a instant action the Flower Girl may split her senses between herself and her Garden, looking as though she was standing in any space within the garden. The Flower Girl has a 360-degree field of view. She may also change her view from any plant or their seeds from her Garden, as long as they are rooted in a Ley Line originating from her Garden. The Soul Plant only grows from Nodes charged with the Life Arcanum. Mages may Attune as normal, but Sleepers that spend a lunar cycle in the Node become Attuned. Plants in the area automatically become Attuned. The resonance flowing out of the Node is determined by by the legacy, the Flower Girl\u2019s Nimbus, and the actions of those within the Garden, usually Growth, Peace, Plant, Truth, or Wisdom.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Life: The Attuned may harness the Node to bring any plant put there to any point it its life cycle, as long as that point would take a year or less. These changes require a day to complete and a successful Intelligence + Crafts or Intelligence + Survival roll.<br /> <br /> Plants that grow within the Garden and drink of it\u2019s resonance grow strong and healthy and beautiful, and faster than normal. This effect is limited to effects a plant would experience if it was raised in perfect conditions.<br /> <br /> This Garden is the heart of the Legacy, the foundation point. If a Flower Girl\u2019s Garden is destroyed, the Legacy attainments ceases to function, although she is still a member of the Legacy. In the event of a Garden being completely destroyed, the Flower may create a new Soul Seed. This requires a seed of size 2 or below, and the expenditure of 1 mana and 1 willpower. A Flower Girl may also transfer the soul seed to another seed at any time for the same cost as making a new Soul Seed. The moment the Soul Seed is transferred, the Garden starts to slowly lose its magic with the attainments failing each week one by one starting with the highest attainment the Flower Girl has. When replanting, the garden takes one week to regain one level of the Legacy. The seed may only be Planted within the Heart of a Life Node.<br /> <br /> A living soul stone. I wanted to start with this because I felt the idea had interesting potential. I wanted it to generate a Node instead of a Demesne, because I felt a &quot;free&quot; soul stone might be a bit too much, and it would tie into ley lines and the other roots. As for why the Node gains more charges, well I felt the Node should scale like a plant grows, starting a seed, then getting stronger. Maybe I should just have this as a Life only Node, but expand what the Life charge does. or maybe I should leave it as is.<br /> Of the 5 effects I feel the time and space and forces effects are not in theme. Matter is an exception because if it applies to plants you can grow extremely durable plants, which I feel is in theme. If I remove all but life, I feel like the life node should be improved as the legacy continues. I would like this legacy to be able to grow Gardens in extreme locations. </div> </div> </div>Creating a Node here is way too much, even changing the resonance is beyond the power of the first Legacy Attainment. Putting a way to <i>find</i> a place to grow the Garden here makes more sense, imo, <i>Sacred Geometry</i> with Advanced Duration. Also, it allows the Flower Girl to choose the type of Node they want, rather than being forced into just Life (this will make the next Attainment better, too).<br /> <br /> For the Life effect I think maybe <i>Speak with Plants</i> would be pretty cool and thematic.<br /> <br /> Attuning themself to the Node makes sense here, as well (obviously), and I feel like giving the Flower Girl a Connected Sympathy to, and the ability to cast Remotely on, their Garden makes perfect sense, it's a double-edged sword.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Second:</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Expression 3, Area of Expertise (Gardening)<br /> <br /> <br /> The stronger bond allows the Flower Girl to take some of the Power of her Garden with her on her travels. After spending a scene tending to her Garden, the Flower Girl carries part of the Node within herself, acting as if she was within the Nodes boundaries. This effect lasts for her Prime dot\u2019s steps on the advanced duration chart. She may share this Attunement with anyone she touches for a Mana, although doing only lasts a scene. Anyone she shares the Attunement with permanently becomes Attuned to the Garden\u2019s Node, but can only benefit while in the boundaries of the Garden.<br /> <br /> I wanted the legacy to have use outside the garden, but I also wanted the garden to act as the legacies home ground, where they are their strongest. The Yantras probably cover that aspect of the Legacy. I also wanted the mage to see their though soul stone like a Prime Soul Windows and the Garden like a Familiar. In retrospect this is probably not a good idea, it allows the legacy to leave their Garden and defend it from a distance.<br /> <br /> The next part is a Prime Ruling with advance duration to carry the effects of the node when outside the area of the node. This might be very underwhelming with only the Life charge.<br /> <br /> I wanted the garden to be obviously magical, and have a effect on those within it. I also thought the legacy should have some way to see resonance. </div> </div> </div>I think carrying the Resonance is a neat Attainment, and it pushes the Gardener to find or create the best Garden they can.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Optional</b>: Life 2<br /> Root and stem listen to the Flower Girl, following her Awakened Will. While inside of the Garden, the Flower Girl can meditate in order to shape grass, bush and tree. After spending a scene meditating in her Garden, a Flower Girl may spend an instant action in which she touches the plant subject, and she determines the way it grows for her Life dots on the advanced duration chart. She may combine this Attainment with the Life effect of the Node to grow the subject any shape the plant could potentially grow in a year. She may spend a mana to rapidly grow the subject with a turn instead of a day when combining with the Node effect.<br /> <br /> In addition, the Garden animates to defend itself, and it's Flower Girl. The Garden becomes a Safe Place and a Sanctum to it's Flower Girl with a rating equal to her dots in Life. This comes in the form of intuitive knowledge of her Garden like she would know herself. If the Flower Girl is in a region where there are no plants, and that is still in her Garden, then she only benefits from the Initiative bonus from the Safe Place Merit. When she is within touching distance of plants, the Flower Girl benefits from the bonus spell control slots from the Sanctum Merit as the plants draw the spells into the Roots. The Flower Girl may instead of Lethal Damage chose to impart a penalty to a roll as the plants of the Garden interfere with the Intruder. this penalty is equal to the amount of Lethal damage they would normally take. If a Intruder is not within a distance that the plants of the Garden can't grow into within a year, then they do not receive any direct consequences for entering the Garden. The Flower Girl may reflexively spend a Mana to refresh the Safe Place Merit during a Invasion.<br /> <br /> Living Shaping-Normal Shaping requires a reach for solid objects, because it's not in the nature of solids to readily change shape like liquids and gas. I felt that a plant shaping spell would require a reach to just have the plant quickly be the shape you want. It would start by having the grow into that pattern. Plants do move, just at a nearly imperceptible rate. I then remembered that the Life node effect allowed you to quickly grow things up to a year. I figured I could substitute that for the reach need to grow plants immediately. Again I wanted the effect to be stronger in the Garden, and I figured the most common use would be to make a Safe Place merit. I probably should remove that. </div> </div> </div><i>Accelerate Growth</i> is a Patterning effect, I realize that you're harnessing the hypothetical Life node, but still. I also don't think the Merit is really appropriate at this level and the independent animation would be a Weaving (Life 3) effect.<br /> <br /> I'd go with something a little simpler, <i>Web of Life</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Flower Girl can detect all living things, or any category of living thing, nearby or that comes within range during the duration of the effect with an Instant Action and in an area equal to 1 + Life dots/2 on the Advanced Scale: Area chart and lasts for a number of turns equal to her Life dots. This effect is always active on her Garden, letting her know everything within or entering her garden at all times. This Attainment emulates the spell <i>Web of Life</i> with reach assigned to Advanced Scale and either Advanced Duration (for the Garden) or Instant Cast (when used outside the Garden).&quot;<br /> <br /> It's thematic, you're detecting living things, and it lets you monitor your Garden from afar (which can help you defend it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Third:</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 3, Craft 4<br /> <br /> When the Lie cracks, Truth bleeds through. The Flower Girl may spend a point of Mana to cast Words of Truth with scale: area of effect and reach for instant and the reach to create the inspired or guilty conditions.<br /> <br /> I always wanted a Prime weaving to let a node become a nimbus. At the same time I wanted the legacy to have a social aspect. Keeping the Words of Truth. </div> </div> </div>I would do a similar thing here as for my suggestion on the Second Alternate: give this a permanent effect for the Garden (anyone going through the Garden has whatever Truth the Flower Girl wants revealed to them, so Advanced Duration and the Condition, can be a different Truth each time it's refreshed by changing the Garden), and an out of Garden effect (Instant and the Condition). Don't forget that it's Withstood by Composure and has Potency equal to the Flower Girl's Prime dots.<br /> <br /> The issue here is that it's a little unclear whether the Condition is tied to the duration of the spell, I lean towards &quot;it's not&quot; since it's written as a Lasting effect, but that's not 100%.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Optional</b>: Life 3<br /> <br /> The Bond between the Flower Girl and her garden grows deeper, the Flower Girl may spend a Scene tending to her Garden gain the senses of any plant in her Garden and within her Life dots of Advanced Scale: Area of Effect. This effect lasts for her life steps on the Advanced Duration chart. These plants cannot see, exactly, but they can feel, and sense the resonance of anything they touch. Animals usually have the resonance of themselves, while Mortals have the resonance of the strongest emotion or action they have recently performed. Mages have their nimbus revealed as well as their resonance. The Flower Girl is considered touching the Plants for the Purposes of her Spells and Attainments.<br /> <br /> A Life Prime combined Unveiling with reach toward advanced scale: AoE and Advanced duration and a reach to be considered touch every plant the spell effects. </div> </div> </div>This would be covered by the <i>Web of Life</i> suggestion.<br /> <br /> Instead I'd recommend putting your plant control here, when used outside the Garden it would have reach for Instant Cast and Advanced Scale (for Area), for the Garden it'd be an Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale.<br /> <br /> The spell would look like:<br /> <br /> <b>Plant Bending</b> (Life 2)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Composure (Plants usually have zero composure)<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Survival, Intimidation, Expression<br /> Plants in the area can be moved however the Mage desires, in an area with lots of plants the Mage can impose a penalty to speed and rolls relying on movement equal to the spell's potency. The Mage can also direct large plants, such as trees, to attack using Wits + Spell Potency as the dicepool, damage dealt is bashing or lethal depending on the type of plant (vines would deal bashing, an oak would deal lethal), and the weapon modifier is equal to the plant's size.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fourth:</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 4, Expression 4.<br /> The Garden\u2019s Roots destroys more of the Lie. The Garden's Node becomes a Hallow of a rating equal to the Flower Girl's dots in Prime.<br /> <br /> Actually not a Prime Making but a Prime Weaving with the 2 reach for Lasting or Indefinite.<br /> <br /> Dice modifiers are boring, even if they fit rather well. Drawing rote quality from nimbus tilts is interesting in a short term manner, but not really a good option for a Legacy. </div> </div> </div>This is definitely a Prime Making effect. <i>Geomancy</i> with Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale is more appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Optional</b>: Life 4<br /> The Roots of the Garden drink deep from the resonance past the lie. Body control with advanced duration, and +2 reach toward lethal healing quicker, on both the Flower Girl and the Garden.<br /> <br /> I wanted the Node to scale at some point, because node effects are very limited. I am switching to body control, because that replicates pretty much everything I wanted the node to do. It's probably not as ridiculous as every node effect scaling, but it should be nice.<br /> <br /> I want a legacy that turns a mages body into her nimbus, soul stones, and dedicated magical tools because that's cool. This isn't the legacy for it though. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fifth:</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 5, Life 4, Craft 5, Expression 5<br /> The Garden finally grows to it's truest potential. Both the Garden and it's Flower Girl are connected on such intimate level that is functionally no difference between the two. And from the union of Gnosis, Root, Soul, and Stem comes a living symbol of that connection. The Soul Plant becomes a Living Soul Stone. <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Soul Plant has a number of properties that separate it from a normal Soul Stone. The Soul Plant cannot be used to create Demesnes or Annulities. The Soul Plant does not reduce the maximum Gnosis of the Flower Girl. the Soul Plant is always counted as having 1 more Gnosis than The Flower Girl that created it. The Soul Plant is always dedicated to the Flower Girl as if under the effect the P</span>rofligate Dedication and Broad Dedication merits and does not count toward those Merit's maximums. The Soul Plant is very difficult to destroy, acting a both a Perfected Living Creature and gaining the Stalwart Soul Merit with a rating equal to the Flower Girls dots in Prime that stack with the regular merit. Even if every living cell of the plant is destroyed, the Roots will simply regrow the Soul Plant within one lunar cycle.<br /> <br /> When the Flower Girl passes away, as all must in the end, part of her will remain in the Garden. This Echo is not a Ghost, and does not respond to Death. It tends to the garden in the Flower girls absence, and defends it as she would. It has a mana pool equal to the Flower Girl at the moment of death, and can use Attainments as she would. Mages may use a Prime version of Goetic Evocation or the Echo Chamber merit to communicate with the Echo. Legacy members theorize that the Echo is a living Nimbus Knot, drawn from the Flower Girls Connection to her Garden. It may even be present before the Flower Girl's death. </div> </div> </div>I'd just make it a Soul Stone that doesn't reduce your Gnosis, but otherwise have all the same effects.<br /> <br /> I do like the Echo, but I'd still use the rules for a Ghost Mage (even though it's not a Ghost) with the Garden as the Anchor, with the exception of still allowing it to use Legacy Attainments that affect the Garden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Optional</b>: Life 5.<br /> From the Soul Plant comes special seeds. Every solar year, a number of seeds equal to the Flower Girl's dots in prime can be harvested. These seeds, when planted in a ley line that is connected to one of the ley lines from the original Garden, grows into a new Garden, with it's own Node. New Ley Lines emerge from the new Node and the process continues. For the purposes of Attainments, these new Gardens are considered extensions of the original. The new Gardens only grow to an area as if they had added another Ley Line to the intersection. Many of these new Gardens attract caretakers, many of whom become Attuned Sleepwalkers over a extended period of time.<br /> <br /> I wanted some way to have supernatural plants grow in the garden, then spread outward from it. I don't think I did a good job. </div> </div> </div>I actually like it and think it's fine.<br /> <br /> Just an fyi, since you made this mistake a lot: &quot;it<b>'s</b>&quot; is a contraction for &quot;it is&quot;, &quot;it<b>s</b>&quot; (no apostrophe) is the possessive form of the word &quot;it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T17:27:01-07:00","id":1450104,"title":"","content":"Short on time, may go over it in more detail, but the thing that stands out to me:<br /> <br /> Ley Lines don't come from Nodes, they're intersections between them; which Gross Arcanum a Node is aligned with is specifically a thematic function of the Resonances that intersect there. If the bases for Gardens work differently, that's probably worth fleshing out as a specific Mystery rather than treating it as a given part of the way the world works that the Legacy reflects upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T21:31:00-07:00","id":1450131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><s>Muhahaha, time to rain on your parade again!</s></div> </div> </div> </div> Fool! I love the rain.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, another neat Legacy idea to offer constructive criticism on!</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you for dropping by! Glad you like it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am now picturing Perfuma from <i>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> That show is on the List! Along with Steven Universe and Owl House....I need more free time.<br /> *quickly scans bio without looking at spoilers* Yes, that's the legacy personified. I actually based the legacy's social theme on Grace from El Goonish Shive, specifically the first, third, and fourth panels of this <a href=\"https://www.egscomics.com/comic/2012-02-07\" target=\"_blank\">strip</a>. Read a few comics before for context.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like gardening would be more Survival than Crafts, personally, but I do like Expression for things like arrangement.</div> </div> </div> </div> *Sighs* I asked in the general ask a simple question thread what skills would be appropriate to gardening, and I got back Crafts, Expression, and maybe Survival. I will change it if you think it fits better. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating a Node here is way too much, even changing the resonance is beyond the power of the first Legacy Attainment. Putting a way to <i>find</i> a place to grow the Garden here makes more sense, imo, <i>Sacred Geometry</i> with Advanced Duration. Also, it allows the Flower Girl to choose the type of Node they want, rather than being forced into just Life (this will make the next Attainment better, too).</div> </div> </div> </div> I considered letting the legacy pick any node, but I had set up the second optional Attainment by then so it had to be Life. I do know I want the Node to effect the plants in the Garden somehow. Maybe I just leave the line about their growing conditions?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Life effect I think maybe <i>Speak with Plants</i> would be pretty cool and thematic.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh yeah, this should be here at some point.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Attuning themself to the Node makes sense here, as well (obviously), and I feel like giving the Flower Girl a Connected Sympathy to, and the ability to cast Remotely on, their Garden makes perfect sense, it's a double-edged sword.</div> </div> </div> </div> I just wasn't sure if making the Garden would take up the whole Attainment or if there would be room of other Attainment effects. I think I will add your suggestions. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think carrying the Resonance is a neat Attainment, and it pushes the Gardener to find or create the best Garden they can.</div> </div> </div> </div> My only problem with it is that node effects are really minor, and either really specific or way too broad. It's why I wanted the Life one, it's in theme and I could use it to cheat certain Attainments.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Accelerate Growth</i> is a Patterning effect, I realize that you're harnessing the hypothetical Life node, but still. I also don't think the Merit is really appropriate at this level and the independent animation would be a Weaving (Life 3) effect.</div> </div> </div> </div> I had to use the Node effect somewhere. I will grant you the independence of the Attainment probably shouldn't be here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with something a little simpler, <i>Web of Life</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Flower Girl can detect all living things, or any category of living thing, nearby or that comes within range during the duration of the effect with an Instant Action and in an area equal to 1 + Life dots/2 on the Advanced Scale: Area chart and lasts for a number of turns equal to her Life dots. This effect is always active on her Garden, letting her know everything within or entering her garden at all times. This Attainment emulates the spell <i>Web of Life</i> with reach assigned to Advanced Scale and either Advanced Duration (for the Garden) or Instant Cast (when used outside the Garden).&quot;<br /> <br /> It's thematic, you're detecting living things, and it lets you monitor your Garden from afar (which can help you defend it).</div> </div> </div> </div> ...Alright I can work with this. I basically use this later on with a bit of Prime splashed on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would do a similar thing here as for my suggestion on the Second Alternate: give this a permanent effect for the Garden (anyone going through the Garden has whatever Truth the Flower Girl wants revealed to them, so Advanced Duration and the Condition, can be a different Truth each time it's refreshed by changing the Garden), and an out of Garden effect (Instant and the Condition). Don't forget that it's Withstood by Composure and has Potency equal to the Flower Girl's Prime dots.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh right, Withstand. Got to write that down. I really like the Garden version.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue here is that it's a little unclear whether the Condition is tied to the duration of the spell, I lean towards &quot;it's not&quot; since it's written as a Lasting effect, but that's not 100%.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have the power to say, at least for the legacy, this is always Lasting. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be covered by the <i>Web of Life</i> suggestion.<br /> <br /> Instead I'd recommend putting your plant control here, when used outside the Garden it would have reach for Instant Cast and Advanced Scale (for Area), for the Garden it'd be an Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok. That would work. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spell would look like:<br /> <br /> <b>Plant Bending</b> (Life 2)<br /> Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Composure (Plants usually have zero composure)<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Survival, Intimidation, Expression<br /> Plants in the area can be moved however the Mage desires, in an area with lots of plants the Mage can impose a penalty to speed and rolls relying on movement equal to the spell's potency. The Mage can also direct large plants, such as trees, to attack using Wits + Spell Potency as the dicepool, damage dealt is bashing or lethal depending on the type of plant (vines would deal bashing, an oak would deal lethal), and the weapon modifier is equal to the plant's size.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mind throwing this onto the Creative Thaumaturgy thread? This fulfills my desire to see grass grow to tangle someone's shoes. I would add on vines or trees being able to grapple or otherwise immobilize. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is definitely a Prime Making effect. <i>Geomancy</i> with Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale is more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div> I knew this one would come up. I am going to have to disagree. It's not Making because it is attached to a Node, not being generated from thin air. It might not be Weaving, but I don't feel it's Making either. As for Geomancy being more appropriate... well maybe. It definitely fits somewhere in the Legacy. I wanted a Hallow because that's as close as the Fallen World normally comes to Lie being shattered. I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just make it a Soul Stone that doesn't reduce your Gnosis, but otherwise have all the same effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>...But...but...a nearly unkillable weed. I wanted to see what would happen if someone used kudzu as their Soul Plant.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the Echo, but I'd still use the rules for a Ghost Mage (even though it's not a Ghost) with the Garden as the Anchor, with the exception of still allowing it to use Legacy Attainments that affect the Garden.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually typed then deleted &quot;make like Ghost Mage, except may use Legacy Attainments&quot;, because I couldn't find the Ghost Mage rules in 2e. I actually wasn't entirely sure I didn't Imagine them up. I also was in a rush to finish before I went to work, so if the rules are some place obvious, that is why. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually like it and think it's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, that was leftover commentary from my first iteration of the idea. It was a bit of a mess then, I think it is better now, thanks to your suggestion. I am happy you like it though. Maybe I should mark development commentary with a color or something? Does anyone know how to color text?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450093#post1450093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just an fyi, since you made this mistake a lot: &quot;it<b>'s</b>&quot; is a contraction for &quot;it is&quot;, &quot;it<b>s</b>&quot; (no apostrophe) is the possessive form of the word &quot;it&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> ... It just wouldn't be one of my creations without grammar mistakes. I will fix it, it's just not high on my priorities right now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-28T21:53:56-07:00","id":1450134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450104#post1450104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short on time, may go over it in more detail, but the thing that stands out to me:<br /> <br /> Ley Lines don't come from Nodes, they're intersections between them; which Gross Arcanum a Node is aligned with is specifically a thematic function of the Resonances that intersect there. If the bases for Gardens work differently, that's probably worth fleshing out as a specific Mystery rather than treating it as a given part of the way the world works that the Legacy reflects upon.</div> </div> </div> </div> By all means, comment as you like. I do value your comments, because they are very insightful. I may not always use them, but I do try to follow through on them.<br /> <br /> What the Gardens actually are has had a bit of a troubled development. At first they were a piece of the mage that pushed at one of the cracks in the Lie, represented by the Soul Plant. Currently, they are the product the interaction of Node, Gnosis, Life, and the overall Legacy, which is somewhat alive(not aware though). If I change how they work tomorrow, they will probably be something a bit different. One thing I think still applies is that the Node sticks around even if the original Ley Lines move around or vanish, it\u2019s sustained by the Legacy and its own Roots. I think that qualifies as a Mystery? You know, I probably should make a rumors and mysteries section after I finish the mechanics and lore.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T09:27:27-07:00","id":1450318,"title":"","content":"So I\u2019m going over each of the attainments to see if I have any issues with them, and the Final Attainment caught my eye. In particular, what would happen if I allow Demesnes to be created. Seeing as it\u2019s a legacy Attainment, it should be free from Paradox, and Sleepers can\u2019t shut it down by looking at it. But would it grant unlimited reach? And the area it effects, should it be Soul Stone standard, or should it cover the Garden? That\u2019s a big area difference, but it is the Final Attainment, and it\u2019s as much the Garden\u2019s and Roots\u2019 Soul Stone as the Flower Girl\u2019s. If it\u2019s not enough, should it instead make something like a positive Annuity in the Garden\u2019s area, or boost the Node\u2019s effect to ridiculous levels? Anyone have any thoughts about this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T13:43:58-07:00","id":1450349,"title":"","content":"I think rough draft 2.5 is ready, I took most of proindrakenzol's suggestions and made a few changes. Again, thoughts, comments, concerns, and/or criticisms are all welcome. Really, anything is helpful.<br /> <br /> Edit: Whoops, forgot to write &quot;The Flower Girl may change the message with another ritual.&quot; in the Third Attainment. Fixed now. I apologize if this inconveniences you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-30-2021, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T18:24:39-07:00","id":1450379,"title":"","content":"The main danger of a non-dispellable Demesne is that its a nightmare for Sleepers. Quiescence makes it so they forget, but such overt exposure to the Supernal things within make it so they are at a constant risk of Breaking Points, still generating Paradox for all overt magic within, eroding summons and more. All the while they are slowly going insane from the revelations and cummulative memory holes and rewrites from it all taking their toll. <br /> <br /> A possible final Attainment is to mix elements of Create Truth with Contagion, with advanced duration. This highly contagious but ultimately harmless disease makes anyone infected into a living Hallow, with the chosen Resonances (peace, tranquility, introspection, proactiveness, altruism, etc). That means you are not only actively spreading positive change, but you are also making mana more abundant and giving the Supernal a stronger perch upon the world, thus cultivating the sacred. Figuring out the spell factors is the main challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T19:26:55-07:00","id":1450387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450379#post1450379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main danger of a non-dispellable Demesne is that its a nightmare for Sleepers. Quiescence makes it so they forget, but such overt exposure to the Supernal things within make it so they are at a constant risk of Breaking Points, still generating Paradox for all overt magic within, eroding summons and more. All the while they are slowly going insane from the revelations and cummulative memory holes and rewrites from it all taking their toll.</div> </div> </div> </div> So even a Legacy's protection from the Lie is not enough to stop the carving light of Demesne. Yeah, guess a Demesne isn\u2019t a option then. Wouldn\u2019t fit.<br /> <br /> Side note: do cryptids cause breaking points in sleepers? I can\u2019t remember.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450379#post1450379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A possible final Attainment is to mix elements of Create Truth with Contagion, with advanced duration. This highly contagious but ultimately harmless disease makes anyone infected into a living Hallow, with the chosen Resonances (peace, tranquility, introspection, proactiveness, altruism, etc). That means you are not only actively spreading positive change, but you are also making mana more abundant and giving the Supernal a stronger perch upon the world, thus cultivating the sacred. Figuring out the spell factors is the main challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div> That works? I guess there is no reason for it not to. If at all possible I would like the Legacy to have a distinct place of power and plant aesthetic. A disease has the spreading of the Final attainments, but it has no root, no base. A disease might have a patient zero, but it does come from then, they are just the first infected. The whole of the legacy is symbolically rooted. I just don\u2019t think this fits. It\u2019s a good idea, though and I\u2019m going to keep it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T01:29:02-07:00","id":1450414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450387#post1450387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So even a Legacy's protection from the Lie is not enough to stop the carving light of Demesne. Yeah, guess a Demesne isn\u2019t a option then. Wouldn\u2019t fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Legacy's Attainments are the mage affecting the world without reaching into the Supernal, which is why they're unaffected by Paradox, are immune to Dissonance, and doesn't cause Quiescence. As such, Legacy Attainments should probably not involve the Supernal directly. Alternatively, if you were to write a Legacy that more actively interacts with the Supernal (which doesn't seem to be relevant to this Legacy, though), it might have special rules that specify how and why it's subject to the Lie. Like some sort of inverse parallell to Abyssal Legacies that causes Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Side note: do cryptids cause breaking points in sleepers? I can\u2019t remember. </div> </div> </div>Anything supernatural generally causes breaking points until they've normalised it. Applies equally to Sleepers and Sleepwalkers (although Sleepwalkers with Supernatural Merits may have a higher tolerance due to exposure to their own stuff).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T05:45:13-07:00","id":1450440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450414#post1450414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Legacy's Attainments are the mage affecting the world without reaching into the Supernal, which is why they're unaffected by Paradox, are immune to Dissonance, and doesn't cause Quiescence. As such, Legacy Attainments should probably not involve the Supernal directly. Alternatively, if you were to write a Legacy that more actively interacts with the Supernal (which doesn't seem to be relevant to this Legacy, though), it might have special rules that specify how and why it's subject to the Lie. Like some sort of inverse parallell to Abyssal Legacies that causes Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. This is a good argument, and very interesting. Unfortunately I\u2019m back to the drawing board now. On Legacy Attainments that would directly involve the Supernal, that would only be Summoning Legacies and maybe something that opens a Demesne or someone else like that, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450414#post1450414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything supernatural generally causes breaking points until they've normalised it. Applies equally to Sleepers and Sleepwalkers (although Sleepwalkers with Supernatural Merits may have a higher tolerance due to exposure to their own stuff).</div> </div> </div> </div> General Supernal stuff causes breaking points, even to Sleepwalkers? I thought that Sleepwalkers would be immune to breaking points caused by general supernatural shenanigans, seeing as it\u2019s rather heavily implied that that is caused by the abyssal shard in them. I seem to remember that the shard gets burned out with the Sleepwalker Merit, or with Supernatural Merits? That\u2019s good to know, since i MIGHT be running a game in semi near future. (I am waiting on a hardcover rule book, and my group can\u2019t seem to make any timeframe past a month work.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-31T09:24:47-07:00","id":1450460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450440#post1450440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">General Supernal stuff causes breaking points, even to Sleepwalkers? I thought that Sleepwalkers would be immune to breaking points caused by general supernatural shenanigans, seeing as it\u2019s rather heavily implied that that is caused by the abyssal shard in them. I seem to remember that the shard gets burned out with the Sleepwalker Merit, or with Supernatural Merits? That\u2019s good to know, since i MIGHT be running a game in semi near future. (I am waiting on a hardcover rule book, and my group can\u2019t seem to make any timeframe past a month work.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Abyssal shard is what causes Supernal and Abyssal magic to always cause breaking points in Sleepers. Sleepwalkers (whether they have the Sleepwalker Merit or a Supernatural Merit) does indeed lose that part. However, they still take any regular breaking points just like Sleepers, and since the supernatural in CofD tends to be fucking scary and traumatic, that tends to cause breaking points no matter if they're a Sleeper or Sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> Mage 2e core just tends to phrase it quite badly, very often implying that Sleepwalkers don't suffer breaking points from witnessing traumatic stuff, as well as stating Legacy Attainments don't cause breaking points when it really should specify that they don't cause <i>automatic</i> breaking points due to the Sleeping Curse. Well, except for the Integrity sidebar in the text about Sleepers where the book goes to the opposite extreme and clearly states that both Sleepers and Sleepwalkers (specifically including Proximi) <i>always</i> suffer breaking points from witnessing magic. Gotta suck for a Proximus to suffer breaking points whenever they cast their Blessings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T10:55:36-07:00","id":1450608,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> I had an idea that uses a principle very similar to your idea. What if instead of Contagion, we use Transform Life's ability to pass changes onto decedents, and Living Vessel form Signs of Sorcery. That would make Imbued Plants that eventually make more imbued Plants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T20:50:38-07:00","id":1450659,"title":"","content":"In the case of Contagion, I used the term disease as an easy parallel to the idea. It could also be presented as symbiotic beings, a connection to the Garden that allows people to cultivate both their lives and the Supernal, like a mana seed in symbiosis with the subject.<br /> <br /> Regarding the imbuement idea, Living Vessel requires the subject to be under its effects during the entire imbuement process, a trivial matter for masters of Prime and Life. Arguably, it can be cast without an Attainment, since imbuement is a focused effort.<br /> <br /> There is also the matter of spell control, which means each imbued plant could cost a willpower dot.<br /> <br /> Examining the mainstream theories of imbuement, passing the spell on genetically seems dubious. By the Xoristos theory, each instance requires the mage to imbue the Imago of the original spell into the item. By the Memias theory, the imbued item Imago of that spell must be imprinted in order for its continual activations to be used. Both hypothesis seem to imply a sustained effort by a being with Gnosis is indispensable, akin to custom made orders. More information can be found on page 68 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> and I believe its the reason that spell does not have such a Reach option.<br /> <br /> Another option is to transform the subjects into beings halfway between platonic ideals and living beings. This could allows them to ignore the need for food and sleep, not be hindered by wound penalties or even have greater proficiency in their rolls. The Smelting Aura from Feng Shen Ji and how it creates the idyllic vistas of the Phantom Island could provide inspiration for this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-01-2021, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-01T22:31:51-07:00","id":1450664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450659#post1450659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of Contagion, I used the term disease as an easy parallel to the idea. It could also be presented as symbiotic beings, a connection to the Garden that allows people to cultivate both their lives and the Supernal, like a mana seed in symbiosis with the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, the symbiosis angle occurred to me this morning. It\u2019s very good. Very, very good. I think it fits, but I keep getting a weird feeling about it. I think I figured out why it bothered me so. It\u2019s similar to the Roses of Eden. I have tried to make the Tamers and the Roses very distinct in mechanics. The Final Attainments are the culmination of the Legacy\u2019s philosophy. The Roses lift the people up to the Legacy\u2019s idea of perfect, The Tamer work on a area, trying to lift up the entire world one piece at time. The effect on sleepers is desired, but it\u2019s in a abstract way. It\u2019s not personal for the Tamers like it is the Roses.The Attainment is the perfect blend of both. It\u2019s not personal to the mage, but it is very personal to the subject. It makes them better, but also drives them to change the world around them. And they do. They really do. So now I\u2019m torn...but I think this is enough to work with. I think understand more now. I think I will use this.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450659#post1450659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the imbuement idea, Living Vessel requires the subject to be under its effects during the entire imbuement process, a trivial matter for masters of Prime and Life. Arguably, it can be cast without an Attainment, since imbuement is a focused effort.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I thought it had to be on as long as you wanted the Imbued thing to last...which is rather silly now that I think about it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450659#post1450659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the matter of spell control, which means each imbued plant could cost a willpower dot.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, it would wouldn\u2019t it. Probably not good.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450659#post1450659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Examining the mainstream theories of imbuement, passing the spell on genetically seems dubious. By the Xoristos theory, each instance requires the mage to imbue the Imago of the original spell into the item. By the Memias theory, the imbued item Imago of that spell must be imprinted in order for its continual activations to be used. Both hypothesis seem to imply a sustained effort by a being with Gnosis is indispensable, akin to custom made orders. More information can be found on page 68 of <i>Signs of Sorcery</i> and I believe its the reason that spell does not have such a Reach option.</div> </div> </div> </div> What if all it\u2019s Supernal symbolism was copied exactly? Basically cloning it? You know, besides location. Still your point is more then taken. Oh well, it was a idea.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450659#post1450659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option is to transform the subjects into beings halfway between platonic ideals and living beings. This could allows them to ignore the need for food and sleep, not be hindered by wound penalties or even have greater proficiency in their rolls. The Smelting Aura from Feng Shen Ji and how it creates the idyllic vistas of the Phantom Island could provide inspiration for this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div> hmm another good one. This seems like it\u2019s perfecting the Node effects on a living being. This is like the Forces effects on a Living being. It\u2019s also it\u2019s own Life spell, but I need to do something with the Attuned Node effects. I will work on it...Wait isn\u2019t that Hone the Perfected Form? The description, not the effects?<br /> <br /> Edit: The List grows. My family apparently has a Netflix account, so I was planning on she-ra when that gets transferred over. I don\u2019t suppose Mushishi is on there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 06-02-2021, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T13:19:28-07:00","id":1450726,"title":"","content":"Nearly done. Still working on Lore, but I figured it mostly done. I decided not to go with KaiserAfini's symbiotic suggestion. That was a hard call, and I'm still not sure it was the right one. This probably the Last rough draft, and will move into Finalization soon. (Why do I always finish on days I work?) Anyways, thoughts, comments, criticisms, and concerns are all welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T13:32:20-07:00","id":1450727,"title":"","content":"Would you repost the current draft for ease of reference?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-02T13:44:05-07:00","id":1450729,"title":"","content":"Sure<br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Tamers of Roots</b></span><br /> <br /> She always was one to hang out all day in the orchard. She always tried to see the best in everyone, even when times were hard. She's back now, with new job tending the botanical garden, but she still has the same old smile. Heard she broke up some dumb old fight in the garden, even got everyone involve to apologize to each other.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Gardens of the Sacred</b></span><br /> <br /> There are tales of mythical Gardens, whose fruit contained magical power. Immortality, Knowledge, Power. Why were those Gardens grown, and why were those fruits special? The trees they grew from were ordinary things, really. No, the power came from the Roots, hidden beneath the surface. You see they were said to grow in Heaven, in Eden, in the Sacred. Not here. Not within reach.<br /> Look around you. The World is Broken, Fallen. It used to not be like this, but now it's wounded, and perhaps it will never be what it once was. It is the Mundane, the Profane. The Sacred is left out of reach.<br /> That's the trick, the lie, that you will never see the Sacred, never be there. But it's a <b>Lie</b>. A Lie that has cracks in it, cracks caused by the Roots of those Gardens. All we need to do is widen them, let them grow through cracks, and we can break down the lie, and let the World heal, and grow anew.<br /> <br /> What are the Roots? The Roots are power, hidden beneath the Surface. Others call them Ley lines, cracks in the Lie, but they don't see the Life in them. They don't see how they push up into the world like new sprouts, How they can be tended and nursed to grow strong. They don't see how that sprout grows into a whole Garden, and how that Garden changes the world.<br /> <br /> Long ago, in a ancient part of the world, a seeker of truth found a hidden grotto. Who they were is long lost, only what they found remains. Inside the cave they found a beautiful Garden, with all the plants growing as though they had been cared for lovingly, but with no sign that anyone had ever set foot in this cave. Tired from their journey, they sat beneath a great tree, and soon, slept. They dreamed. Dreamt of Root pushing, digging into soil, into rock. They Dreamt of a Ivory tower falling, crashing and a Hungry Black Sea that swallowed everything in it's path. They dreamt of tending a garden as penance for some overwhelming crime, discovering the Garden was growing powerful, strong and Beautiful. And that it would outlast them. And they Finally dreamt of a faint presence asking if they would tend to the Garden in their stead. When they awoke, they felt the pulsing beat of power just beneath their feet. They felt the Roots pushing against...something. They resolved to tend to this Holy place, and know it's Truths.<br /> That was a Long Time Ago, and things have changed. The legacy has always been around in one form or another, never really coming into the spotlight. It found it's way into the groups that would become the Mysterium, tending to their stores of knowledge as well as the gardens. It was chiefly though of as a way to store knowledge through the generations, and simultaneously a way to make the defense of a Athaneum that much easier. That all changed when a young and hopeful member of the Silver Ladder was found worthy to be taught the secrets of the Legacy. From the moment she saw the the legacy, she knew it's potential. She dreamed of being able to shatter the barriers the Tyrants placed on the world, and bring real change, all without needing to fight. Her passion, her love of the world and of peace has been carried on through the legacy ever since. These days, the Legacy isn't as close to each other as they used to be. They spread out, all around the World. Where ever there are large concentrations of Roots, the Legacy thrives. The Legacy knows that the world is what you make of it, and want a world of harmony, of happiness and hope. Even within the Legacy, many doubt that the Legacy alone can shatter the Lie. The same still believe that they are making a difference, making the world a little less Fallen. The Legacy believes always trying for the best outcome. Even if everything seems hopeless, someone has to try for a better outcome, or it will never happen. Legacy is not naive, and they know that sometimes there are no right answers. The Legacy knows that actions have unforeseen consequences, and that resonance makes more resonance. They believe the conflict only makes more conflict, and to have a better world, you need to act better. The Legacy knows the Seers probably won't change, but they have to try. Even if they won't change, they might still be persuaded. They give everyone a chance, so the world might be that much better. There is a exception to this rule. Just one. Scelesti. The Legacy is vulnerable to the Abyss's touch, and any paradox condition the Flower Girl suffers usually is also suffered by their Garden. The reverse is also true. Paradox in the Garden goes deep, tainting Roots and spreading far outside the Garden. The legacy has been targeted by Scelesti for thousands of years, seeking to spread the Abyss's influence far into the Fallen. The Legacy has strong guidelines on risking Paradox, and on Containing it. One can imagine the response to finding out someone actually serves the Abyss.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Origins</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Parentage</b>: Thyrsus, Silver Ladder, Mysterium,<br /> <b>Background</b>: Many come to the Legacy from Botanical or Idealistic places.<br /> <b>Appearances</b>: Many have green stained fingers, mainly thumbs, and many wear flowers in clothes and hair<br /> <b>Nickname: </b>Gardeners, Flower Girls/Boys, Hippies<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Life 1, Craft or Survival 3, Expression 2, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Gardening)<br /> <b>Initiation</b>: Creation of a soul seed with a senior legacy member assistance, and planting and nurturing it for a full lunar cycle past its sprouting inside of the Node they wish to bond with.<br /> <b>Organization</b>: Small Cabals that have a few links to each other, every equinox the entire legacy meets to discuss any issues concerning the legacy and problems individual members might have.<br /> <b>Theory</b>: The Gardeners know that there are cracks in the lie, places where the Supernal meets the Fallen. The places can, with help, grow and with time may completely overwhelm shatter the lie.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>: Prime<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: Flowers appropriate to the spell (+1, +2 if supernatural); the Garden (+2); success on an Expression roll relating to the spell (+2); Imago causes or assists growth (+1)<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: Tending to a garden; Creating a work of art; Removing Pollution; Resolving a Potentially Hostile Situation Non-Violently<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">First: The Garden</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation<br /> The Roots show themselves to those that would seek them. After a scene of meditation with her Soul Seed or Soul Plant, The Flower Girl senses Ley Lines and Nodes. If there are no Nodes or Ley Lines within sensory range, she know the direction to the nearest Node or Ley Line. This knowledge lasts for the Flower Girl's dots on the Advanced Duration chart.<br /> <br /> Every initiate has a Garden, one they have tended to since it was but simple seed. After the first lunar cycle after sprouting, the soul plant rapidly grows into a young but mature specimen of its kind. This Soul Plant must grow from the Heart of the Node. This act binds the Node to the Flower Girl and her Legacy, transforming the Node into a Garden. The Flower Girl has a Connected Sympathetic Connection to the Garden and is always Attuned to the Garden. The area of the Garden is the area of the Node. The Flower Girl senses anything that would trigger her Peripheral Mage Sight as though she were standing at every point in her Garden. As a instant action the Flower Girl may split her senses between herself and her Garden, looking as though she were standing in any space within the garden and has a 360-degree field of view. The resonance flowing out of the Node is influenced by by the Legacy, the Flower Girl\u2019s Nimbus, and her actions. This effect is limited to the effect as if the Flower Girl was always inside her Garden.<br /> <br /> Attuning to the Node requires either casting the spell <i>Sacred Geometry</i> or successfully Meditating while under the guidance of someone with <i>Sacred Geometry </i>active or already attuned to the Node. Attuning to the Garden's Node grants the Attuned the benefits, and detriments, of the Flower Girl's Nimbus tilt for as long as they are in the area of the Garden. Additionally Sleepers substitute the Flower Girl's dots in Prime for the normal bonus provided by Meditation. Many Attuned Sleepers purchase the Fitful Slumber Merit after a few encounters with the Supernal.<br /> <br /> List of Node effects:<br /> \u2022 Forces: By precisely aligning a stationary piece of technology that requires heat or electricity to function, the Attuned may use the Node to power it.<br /> \u2022 Life: The Attuned may harness the Node to bring any plant put there to any point it its life cycle, as long as that point would take a year or less. These changes require a day to complete and a successful Intelligence + Crafts or Intelligence + Survival roll.<br /> \u2022 Matter: Unless totally destroyed, stationary, inanimate objects built in alignment with local Resonance heal one point of Structure per day. Their permanent Structure may slowly wear down due to environmental conditions, but at half the usual rate.<br /> \u2022 Space: Those who are Attuned acquire a +2 bonus to tasks that require significant movement through space, including driving, running, and certain athletic feats.<br /> \u2022 Time: The Attuned benefit from a +2 bonus to Initiative.<br /> <br /> <br /> Plants that grow within the Garden and drink of its resonance grow strong, healthy, beautiful, and faster than normal. This effect is limited to effects a plant would experience if it was raised in perfect conditions.<br /> <br /> In the event of a Garden being completely destroyed, the Flower may create a new Soul Seed. This requires a seed of size 2 or below, and the expenditure of 1 mana and 1 willpower. A Flower Girl may also transfer the soul seed to another seed at any time for the same cost as making a new Soul Seed. The moment the Soul Seed is transferred, the Garden starts to slowly lose its magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 2<br /> The Flower Girl hears the whisper of vine and bloom. After spending a scene meditating with her Soul Seed or Soul Plant, the Flower Girl may speak and hear any plant. This lasts for her Life dots of steps on the Advanced Duration chart. The words of plants are not verbal communications, requiring the Flower girl to feel or smell the scents plant gives off. Most plants have little understanding of human concepts, and are unconcerned with such things. What plants do know is what they feel, and they feel both the world above the ground and the world below the surface. Many plants are sensitive to the Roots, especially Plants growing in the Garden. Plants also understand the situation that they grow in remarkably well, and a Flower Girl may take the Informed(Gardening this Plant) condition after conversing with a plant. Many Plants can move, and may be persuaded to grow in a particular direction.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Second: Forget Me Not</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Expression 3, Area of Expertise (Gardening)<br /> <br /> <br /> The stronger bond allows the Flower Girl to take some of the Power of her Garden with her on her travels. After spending a scene tending to her Garden, the Flower Girl carries part of the Node within herself, acting as if she was within the Nodes boundaries. This effect lasts for her Prime dot\u2019s steps on the advanced duration chart. She may share this Attunement with any subject she touches for a Mana, although doing only lasts a scene. When used in the Garden, the subject becomes Attuned until the Gardener revokes the Attunement.<br /> <br /> In addition, the Attuned may reflexively invoke the Flower Girl's nimbus tilt on themselves while in the Garden at the cost of one point of Willpower. The Flower Girl may instead pay one point of Mana to invoke on herself. All merits that effect the Nimbus apply.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 2<br /> The Flower Girl can detect all living things, or any category of living thing, nearby or that comes within range during the duration of the effect. Activating this effect takes a Instant Action, covers an area equal to 1 + Life dots/2 on the Advanced Scale: Area chart and lasts for a number of turns equal to her Life dots. This effect is always active on her Garden, letting her know every with living thing within or entering her garden at all times. This Attainment emulates the spell <i>Web of Life</i> with reach assigned to Advanced Scale and either Advanced Duration (for the Garden) or Instant Cast (when used outside the Garden).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Third:</span> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Red</span> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Chrysanthemum</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 3, Craft or Survival 4<br /> When the Lie cracks, Truth bleeds through. The Garden glows with Truths. Without direction this creates a general aura of revelations similar to a long term Nimbus, generally related to the Resonance of the Garden. While in the garden, the Flower Girl may spend a scene tending to her Garden, this focuses the Truths into a message. The message can be any length, but the Flower Girl must know that it is true. This message can be felt by anyone who spends any time within or examining the Garden, unless the message would be false for them. For example, if a Flower Girl leaves a message saying &quot;I love you&quot;, only those she loves will get the message. Everyone who discerns the Message knows it to be True in their Soul. This create a Lasting Inspired or Guilty conditions and if used in Social Maneuvering, this removes one Door or raises the impression level by a step per half the Flower Girl's dots in Prime plus one. The message lasts for the Flower Girl's dots in Prime steps on the advanced duration chart. The Flower Girl may change the message with another ritual. When outside the Garden, the Flower Girl may spend a point of Mana to cast Words of Truth with scale: area of effect and reach for instant and the reach to create the inspired or guilty conditions. This affects anyone with a composure of less than her dots in Prime.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 3<br /> Root and stem listen to the Flower Girl, following her Awakened Will. After spending a scene tending to her Garden, the Flower Girl can command the plants within to move. Plants in the area can be moved however the Flower Girl desires, in an area with lots of plants the Flower Girl can impose a penalty to speed and rolls relying on movement equal to the Flower Girl's dots in Life. The Flower Girl can also direct large plants, such as trees, to attack using Wits + 1+(Life/2) as the dicepool, damage dealt is bashing or lethal depending on the type of plant (vines would deal bashing, an oak would deal lethal, thorns maybe be complicated), and the weapon modifier is equal to the plant's size. The Flower Girl may instead have the Plant grapple a opponent, using Wits +1+(Life/2)+ Size - Defense. This effect lasts for the Flower Girl's dots in Life on the advance duration chart and is in advance scale: area of effect dots in Life. The Flower Girl may spend a Mana and a instant action to use this outside of the Garden, but it only lasts her dots in Life turns.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fourth: Coriander</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 4, Expression 4.<br /> The Flower Girl's connection is such that the Roots will bend to her Will. After a scene meditating in a Ley Line, the flower Girl may redirect ley lines within an area of her Life dots on the advance scale: area chart, reshaping Nodes and altering Resonance as a instant action. She may move ley lines, and therefore the Nodes created where ley lines cross, \u201cpinning\u201d a line to a point within the area of effect of the spell. She may also change the Resonance Keyword of a Node to whatever she wishes. This lasts for the Flower Girl's dots in Life on the advanced duration chart, when the duration expires the ley lines are free to drift and the resonance to shift, but will only do so if external conditions would cause a natural change.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Optional</b>: Life 4<br /> The Roots of the Garden drink deep from resonance untainted by the Lie. The Flower Girl, the Garden itself, and all living beings within the Garden and attuned to the Node, gain all of the following effects with potency equal to half the Flower Girl's Life dots plus one:<ul><li>Halve the amount of oxygen or carbon dioxide needed per potency.</li> <li>Double the interval at which toxins affect them per potency.</li> <li>Subsist on half as much sustenance per potency.</li> <li>Double the interval between deprivation and exhaustion checks per potency.</li> <li>+1 to Initiative per potency.</li> <li>Halve the healing time of both Bashing and Lethal damage per point of potency.</li> </ul>In addition, supernatural plants can grow in the Garden as if they were in their native environment. Many Flower Girls obtain crypto-flora, goblin fruit, mandrakes, and other strange plants from other Supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fifth: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Heliotrope</span></span></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 5, Life 5, Craft or Survival 5, Expression 5<br /> The Garden finally grows to its truest potential. Both the Garden and its Flower Girl are connected on such intimate level that there is functionally no difference between the two. And from the union of Gnosis, Root, Soul, and Stem comes a living symbol of that connection: the Soul Plant becomes a Living Soul Stone. <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Soul Plant has a number of properties that separate it from a normal Soul Stone. </span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">It acts as a +3 yantra for its Flower Girl. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Soul Plant makes no Demesne or A</span>nnullity.</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Soul Plant does not reduce the maximum Gnosis of the Flower Girl. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Soul Plant can only be dedicated if the Flower Girl has the Broad Dedication Merit. </span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">It is a normal Soul Stone in every other regard.</span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Instead of a Demesne or Annullity, The Garden Perfects it's Node, and Extends it's effects onto Living Things. The Node effects becomes:</span><br /> <br /> \u2022 Forces: The Attuned need no rest, nor food. They always are full of energy. They ignore wound penalties.<br /> \u2022 Life: The Attuned can heal from any wound, given enough time, unless they outright die. Scars fade, Limbs regrow.<br /> \u2022 Matter: Unless totally destroyed, the Attuned gain a general armor equal to 1 +(Prime/2).<br /> \u2022 Space: Those who are Attuned know where everything is around them, they don't need to roll to find a path or trail. They add Prime dots to Roll requiring precise movement though space.<br /> \u2022 Time: The Attuned's memories become sharp and clear. They don't need to roll to remember. They add Prime dots to rolls to predict consequence and to rolls to understand the Consequences of their actions.<br /> <br /> From the Soul Plant comes special seeds. Every solar year, a number of seeds equal to the Flower Girl's dots in Life can be harvested. These seeds, when planted in a Ley Line that is connected to one of the ley lines from the original Garden, grows into a new Garden, with its own Node. New Ley Lines emerge from the new Node and the process continues. For the purposes of Attainments, these new Gardens are considered extensions of the original, with exeption of creating more seeds. The new Gardens only grow to an area as if they had added another Ley Line to the intersection. Many of these new Gardens attract caretakers, many of whom become Attuned Sleepwalkers over a extended period of time. The seeds act as their own Ley Line, making a intersection if there was not one before, this only happens when the plant sprouts after being planted.<br /> <br /> If instead the seed is planted into the Flower Girl's Garden, it instead expands the radius of the Garden by one Ley Line.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Mysteries and Story Seeds</b></span><br /> <br /> This section is entirely optional, use or don't use at your pleasure. These are merely ideas that have collected over the course of making the Legacy, some are good, some are funny, and some maybe might make a nice story.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Echoes in Rain</b><br /> Sometimes, when a Flower Girl pass away, something is left to tend to her Garden. It is a remembrance, a shape left in her absence. An Echo. It's not a ghost, and Death has no power over it. It tends the Garden in her stead, as she would herself. What the Echo is actually is and what causes the Echo to arrive is relatively unknown, even to the Masters of the Legacy. The Echoes generally don't like to be examined closely, and tend to vanish into the Garden. Some learned Sages compare the Echo with Nimbus Knots, and the pieces of Memory and Understanding left in a Soul Stone. What is known is that Echoes appear most often if there is no one to take care of the Garden. Second most common is a Flower Girl dying inside her Garden. There are rumors of other ways, many plausible but unconfirmed. Sometimes, even in the mostly likely circumstances, no Echo appears. Perhaps most interestingly, those Flower Girls who leave Echoes almost never leave ghosts behind without interference. Sometimes, the Echoes recognize someone. A angry Echo stops it's attack because the woman it pursues reminds it of a small child she knew a long time ago. A cabal mate has one last conversation with the departed, and gets to say goodbye. The strangest of these occurrences happen centuries after the death of the Flower Girl, to people who have never been in the Garden before. At least one member of the Legacy claims to have spoken with the Echo of their past life.<br /> <br /> Running the Echoes<br /> Make as a non lich Ghost Mage with rank equal to half of the originating Flower Girl's Gnosis at the moment of death. It's only anchor is the Garden, and it can use Attainments as it's Flower Girl would. The majority of a Echo's memories will be of the Garden, and it will retain only a few fragments of it's Flower Girl's personality. It's not her, but its born of her and is like her in many ways. It mostly tends to the Garden as she would. A Echo may not remember why she attacks any who bear a certain rune carved on their right hand, but she will with just as much fury as her Flower Girl who died to them. Many defensive Echoes seek to repeal, not kill. Prime Mage Sight reveals it, and Mages may use a Prime version of Goetic Evocation or the Echo Chamber merit to communicate with the Echo.<br /> <br /> <b>Entangled Roots</b><br /> Many cabals of Flower Girls tend to Plant their Gardens on top of each other, effectively sharing the same Garden. There are no confirmed benefits to doing so, but many rumors of generating or awakening a Hallow, or other such things. One extremely persistent one it that two or more Tamers who are deeply love each other that plant their Garden together in the same space find their Love growing stronger and potent. Many dismiss this rumor as either enhanced sympathies of Legacy members, or as a side effect of spending so much time together. Then in 1954, a young couple came forward. They were both Tamers of Roots, and had met each other through the Tamers. One was Obrimos, the other Thyrsus. And they were Entangled. They believed that it was the Planting and tending the Same Garden that strengthened their bond so. Many have tried to obtain similar results, and failed.<br /> <br /> Tripping though the Tangled Roots<br /> Use the effects of a Entangled Metamorphic Awakening, ignoring the restriction on being of the same Path. If you don't like that, require it be two or more members of the same Path. It can be caused by any version of Love. Friendship or Familial should both count. Even so, this should probably be very rare.<br /> <br /> <b>Of Roots and Roses</b><br /> The Tamers of Roots has always had a complex relationship with the Roses of Eden. One that <i>totally</i> doesn\u2019t resemble a relationship straight out of a anime, why would you ever think that. The Roses of Eden tend to see the Tamers as locked in Atlantan tradition, unable to see how it binds them, and prevents their goal. The Tamers of Roots tend to see the Roses as being obsessed with rejecting Atlantis, and missing the point of the Garden of Eden metaphor. Many cabals engage in a kind of weird rivalry, where both try to out do the other in their respective goals. This never escalates to anything more then passive aggressive comments and maybe pointedly ignoring the other. Both legacies overlap somewhat in the pool of potential recruits, and thus have plenty of minor reasons to generate minor friction. A really easy way to annoy members of both legacies is to compare them to the other.<br /> <br /> Both Legacies are so non aggressive that this probably is the normal maximum their dislike can go, and in all likelihood they do like each other, just having constant silly fights. Inter Legacy friendships are not uncommon, and all but the most fanatical would come to the other Legacy\u2019s aid. Please play for laughs. Another way to go is a exasperated parent, and their rebellious child. Neither will back down, both have a point, and at the end of the day, both love each other dearly.<br /> <br /> <b>The Blighted Fields</b><br /> Sometimes even the Gardeners fall for the Abyss's flirtations. It's not common occurrence, with only handful of recorded incidents in the Legacies long history. Every one has been caught from changes in their Garden, and deviation from containing Paradox. Of course these days, with the Legacy spreading further and further out, it might not be so difficult for someone to slip though the cracks...<br /> <br /> More common is the occurrence that Garden is corrupted from without. Nasnasi may &quot;ground&quot; her stored Paradox into the Garden, infecting it with Abyssal anti-symbols. This is usually creates what is referred to as a Abyssal Blight. The Blight is an Abyssal cancer, warping both Plants and the Roots of the Garden into unrecognizable forms. At the infections peak, the tainted resonance spreads to other Nodes and Gardens, warping them as well. Many Gardens begin to swell, pushing their boundaries over the course of a few days to cover vast stretchers of land. These can overtake cities, swelling further from dissonance and Abyssal Resonance. If left unchecked, the Garden could potentially swallow whole nations, maybe even the world. Inside the Blighted Garden, everything becomes sick, becomes perverted. Twistedly, the Garden still represents everything it is supposed to be. Life flourishes, and grows. Revelations comes to those who seek it. Everything is in harmony, in tune. But they dance to the Abyss's tune. The entire Garden becomes one big Abyssal Environment. Not every Blight is the same. One Blight combines Life with other Life, merging and mutating everything in new Abyssal shapes. People become trees, tree grow mouths and eyes, all in a horrific parody of normal Life. Another causes resonance to break down the natural order, creating zones of bent Node effects. The most horrific break down the Supernal itself inside the Garden, causing spells and yantras to fail. Use any Abyssal Environmental Tilt, and watch movies like Annihilation or read about Warhammer's Nurgle for inspiration. The Colour out of Space is a good anti-life version. Use with care, Blighted Gardens are a big deal, and very dangerous. Sometimes with the Garden's Flower Girl, the Infection can be fought off. A Flower Girl while in her Garden may draw the Paradox into herself, creating a Abyssal Condition. Infections gain additional successes over time, ramping up to the Blight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 06-07-2021, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T16:11:34-07:00","id":1450992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450729#post1450729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum</b>: Prime<br /> <b>Yantras</b>: Flowers appropriate to the spell+1; +2 if a supernatural flower; Inside the Garden +2; success of an expression roll relating to the spell +2; in order to help the subject grow +1<br /> <b>Oblations</b>: Tending to a garden; Creating a work of art; Removing Pollution; Resolving a Potentially Hostile Situation Non-Violently</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd change up the formatting a little:<br /> <br /> Flowers appropriate to the spell (+1, +2 if supernatural); the Garden (+2); success on an Expression roll relating to the spell (+2); Imago causes or assists growth (+1).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">First: The Garden</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Initiation<br /> The Roots show themselves to those that would seek them. After a scene of meditation with her Soul Seed or Soul Plant, The Flower Girl senses Ley Lines and Nodes. If there are no Nodes or Ley Lines within sensory range, she know the direction to the nearest Node or Ley Line. </div> </div> </div>This is a little ambiguous as to how long the Ley Line and Node detection lasts, should probably mention it's Advanced Duration, or make it an Instant Action to activate and only last a few seconds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> with the Creators Prime dots acting as the number of ley lines flowing into the Node. </div> </div> </div>*Creator's<br /> <br /> Also, the number of Ley Lines shouldn't be dependent on the Gardener's Prime dots, that requires Prime 3's <i>Geomancy</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Flower Girl senses anything that would trigger her Peripheral Mage Sight as though she <s>was</s> <b>were</b> standing at every point in her Garden. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She also senses anything around plants from her Garden connected by a Ley Line. </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not sure what this is supposed to mean, but I think it's redundant with the previous sentence and should be removed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a<b>n</b> instant action the Flower Girl may split her senses between herself and her Garden, looking as though she <s>was</s> <b>were</b> standing in any space within the garden<s>. The Flower Girl</s> <b>and</b> has a 360-degree field of view. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She may also change her view from any plant or their seeds from her Garden, as long as they are rooted in a Ley Line originating from her Garden. </div> </div> </div>I'd remove this, it's pushing beyond the boundaries of a 1-dot effect by a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages may Attune as normal, but Sleepers that spend a lunar cycle in the Node become Attuned. Plants in the area automatically become Attuned. The resonance flowing out of the Node is influenced by by the Legacy, the Flower Girl\u2019s Nimbus, and her actions. This effect is limited to the effect as if the Flower Girl was always inside her Garden. </div> </div> </div>I'd remove this entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Her long term Nimbus always <s>e</s><b>a</b>ffects the Garden.-<i>(Not constantly active, but no amount of Wisdom or Shadow Name will reduce the long term Nimbus' effects)</i> </div> </div> </div>I'd remove this, it has connected Sympathy with the Gardener, that accounts for everything already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plants that grow within the Garden and drink of its resonance grow strong, healthy, beautiful, and faster than normal. This effect is limited to effects a plant would experience if it <s>was</s> <b>were</b> raised in perfect conditions. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This Garden is the heart of the Legacy, the foundation point. If a Flower Girl\u2019s Garden is destroyed, the Legacy attainments ceases to function, although she is still a member of the Legacy. </div> </div> </div>This is extraneous, all the effects tied to the Garden will cease, and the first effect, seeing Ley Lines and Nodes, is there to help establish the Garden, losing it without a Garden renders it pointless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the event of a Garden being completely destroyed, the Flower may create a new Soul Seed. This requires a seed of size 2 or below, and the expenditure of 1 mana and 1 willpower. A Flower Girl may also transfer the soul seed to another seed at any time for the same cost as making a new Soul Seed. The moment the Soul Seed is transferred, the Garden starts to slowly lose its magic </div> </div> </div>I'd end the sentence here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> with the attainments failing each week one by one starting with the highest attainment the Flower Girl has. No matter how long she may go without a Garden, a flower Girl always has this Attainment. When replanting, the garden takes one week to regain one level of the Legacy. The seed may only be Planted within the Heart of a Node.<br /> <br /> When the Flower Girl passes away, as all must in the end, part of her will remain in the Garden. This Echo is not a Ghost, and does not respond to Death. It tends to the garden in the Flower Girls absence, and defends it as she would. Build as a Ghost Mage (the non-lich kind) with the Garden as it's Anchor, and it can use Attainments as she would. Mages may use a Prime version of Goetic Evocation or the Echo Chamber merit to communicate with the Echo. Legacy members theorize that the Echo is a living Nimbus Knot, drawn from the Flower Girls Connection to her Garden. It may even be present before the Flower Girl's death.-(I am toying on when exactly a Echo would appear. It definitely doesn't need the final attainment but becomes much rarer the less Gnosis invested into the Legacy. This probably would make a fine mystery) </div> </div> </div>This should not appear until the final Attainment, this is a potent form of immortality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Second:</span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 2, Expression 3, Area of Expertise (Gardening)<br /> <br /> <br /> The stronger bond allows the Flower Girl to take some of the Power of her Garden with her on her travels. After spending a scene tending to her Garden, the Flower Girl carries part of the Node within herself, acting as if she was within the Nodes boundaries. This effect lasts for her Prime dot\u2019s steps on the advanced duration chart. She may share this Attunement with any<s>one</s> <b>subject</b> she touches for a Mana, although doing only lasts a scene. </div> </div> </div>Change &quot;anyone&quot; to &quot;any subject&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyone she shares the Attunement with permanently becomes Attuned to the Garden\u2019s Node, but can only benefit while in the boundaries of the Garden. </div> </div> </div>I'd change this to &quot;when used in the Garden, the subject becomes Attuned until the Gardener revokes the Attunement.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Optional </div> </div> </div></b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> : Life 2<br /> &quot;The Flower Girl can detect all living things, or any category of living thing, nearby or that comes within range during the duration of the effect<b>.</b> <s>with</s><b>Activating this effect takes</b> an Instant Action<b>,</b><s> and in</s> <b>covers</b> an area equal to 1 + Life dots/2 on the Advanced Scale: Area chart<b>,</b> and lasts for a number of turns equal to her Life dots. This effect is always active on her Garden, letting her know every<s>thing</s> <b>living thing</b> within or entering her garden at all times. This Attainment emulates the spell <i>Web of Life</i> with reach assigned to Advanced Scale and either Advanced Duration (for the Garden) or Instant Cast (when used outside the Garden).[s]&quot; </div> </div> </div>You should also remove the quotation marks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third: </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 3, Craft or Survival 4<br /> When the Lie cracks, Truth bleeds through. The Garden glows with Truths. Without direction this creates a general aura of revelations similar to a long term Nimbus<s> of such</s>, generally related to the Resonance of the Garden. While in the garden, the Flower Girl may spend a scene tending to her Garden, this focuses the Truths into a message. The message can be any length, but the Flower Girl must know that it is true. This message can be felt by anyone who spends any time within or examining the Garden, unless the message would be false for them. For example, if a Flower Girl leaves a message saying &quot;I love you&quot;, only those she loves will get the message. Everyone who <s>hears</s> <b>discerns</b> the Message knows it to be True in their Soul. This create a Lasting Inspired or Guilty condition<s>s</s> and if used in Social Maneuvering, this removes one Door or raises the impression level by a step per half the Flower Girl's dots in Prime plus one. The message lasts for the Flower Girl's dots in Prime steps on the advanced duration chart. The Flower Girl may change the message with another ritual. When outside the Garden, the Flower Girl may spend a point of Mana to cast Words of Truth with scale: area of effect and reach for instant and the reach to create the inspired or guilty conditions. This affects anyone with a composure of less than her dots in Prime. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Optional</b>: Life 3<br /> Root and stem listen to the Flower Girl, following her Awakened Will. <s>While inside her Garden, and</s><b>After</b> spending a scene tending to her Garden, the Flower Girl can command <b>the</b> plants <s>around her</s> <b>within</b> to move. Plants in the area can be moved however the Flower Girl desires, in an area with lots of plants the Flower Girl can impose a penalty to speed and rolls relying on movement equal to the Flower Girl's dots in Life. The Flower Girl can also direct large plants, such as trees, to attack using Wits + 1+(Life/2) as the dicepool, damage dealt is bashing or lethal depending on the type of plant (vines would deal bashing, an oak would deal lethal, thorns maybe be complicated), and the weapon modifier is equal to the plant's size. The Flower Girl may instead have the Plant grapple a opponent, using Wits +1+(Life/2)+ Size - Defense. <i>(this dice pool probably needs work) </i>This effect lasts for the Flower Girl's dots in Life on the advance duration chart and is in advance scale: area of effect dots in Life. The Flower Girl may spend a Mana and a<b>n</b> instant action to use this outside of the Garden, but it only lasts her dots in Life turns. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fourth:</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 4, Expression 4.<br /> The Flower Girl's connection is such that the Roots will bend to her Will. After a scene meditating in a Ley Line, the flower Girl may redirect ley lines within a<b>n</b> area of her Life dots on the advance scale<b>: area chart</b>, reshaping Nodes and altering Resonance as a instant action. She may move ley lines, and therefore the Nodes created where ley lines cross, \u201cpinning\u201d a line to a point within the area of effect of the spell. She may also change the Resonance Keyword of a Node to whatever she wishes. This lasts for the Flower Girl's dots in Life on the advanced duration <b>chart</b>; <s>before returning to normal</s> <b>when the duration expires the ley lines are free to drift and the resonance to shift, but will only do so if external conditions would cause a natural change</b>. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition, the Flower Girl may purchase the Hallow Merit for her Garden, the resulting Hallow spontaneously appears at the Heart of the Garden. -<i>Is this fine?</i> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, the Flower Girl can relocate her Garden to a Node with a Hallow, and if you want them to be able to raise a Hallow then you can give that to them as their 5th Attainment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Optional</b>: Life 4<br /> The Roots of the Garden drink deep from the resonance past the lie. Body control with advanced duration, and +2 reach toward lethal healing quicker, on both the Flower Girl and the Garden. Anything Attuned to the Garden benefits while in the Garden.<br /> <br /> In addition, supernatural plants can grow in the Garden as if they had the proper amount of what they need to exist. Many Flower Girls obtain Crypto-Flora, Goblin Fruit, and Mandrakes from other supernatural creatures. -<i>Small addition that amused me. </i> </div> </div> </div>I like the addition, but I'd spruce up the description a bit.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Roots of the Garden drink deep from resonance untainted by the Lie. The Flower Girl, the Garden itself, and all living beings within the Garden and attuned to the Node, gain all of the following effects with potency equal to half the Flower Girl's Life dots plus one:<ul><li>Halve the amount of oxygen or carbon dioxide needed per potency.</li> <li>Double the interval at which toxins affect them per potency.</li> <li>Subsist on half as much sustenance per potency.</li> <li>Double the interval between deprivation and exhaustion checks per potency.</li> <li>+1 to Initiative per potency.</li> <li>Halve the healing time of both Bashing and Lethal damage per point of potency.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> In addition, supernatural plants can grow in the Garden as if they were in their native environment. Many Flower Girls obtain crypto-flora, goblin fruit, mandrakes, and other strange plants from other Supernatural creatures.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">Fifth:</span><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Prime 5, Life 5, Craft or Survival 5, Expression 5<br /> The Garden finally grows to its truest potential. Both the Garden and its Flower Girl are connected on such intimate level that <b>there</b> is functionally no difference between the two. And from the union of Gnosis, Root, Soul, and Stem comes a living symbol of that connection<s>.</s><b>:</b> <s>T</s>the Soul Plant becomes a Living Soul Stone. The Soul Plant has a number of properties that separate it from a normal Soul Stone<s>.</s>:<ul><li>It acts as a +3 yantra for <s>it's</s><b>its</b> Flower Girl.</li> <li>The Soul Plant makes no Demesne or Annullity.</li> <li>The Soul Plant does not reduce the maximum Gnosis of the Flower Girl.</li> <li>The Soul Plant can only be dedicated if the Flower Girl has the Broad Dedication Merit.</li> <li>It is a normal Soul Stone in every other regard.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> Instead of a Demesne or Annullity, The Garden Perfects <s>it's</s><b>its</b> Node, and [s]E[/]extends <s>it's</s><b>its</b> effects onto Living Things. The Node effect<s>s</s> becomes:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Forces: The Attuned need no rest, nor food. They always are full of energy. They ignore wound penalties.<br /> \u2022 Life: The Attuned can heal from any wound, given enough time, unless they outright die. Scars fade, Limbs regrow.<br /> \u2022 Matter: Unless totally destroyed, the Attuned gain a general armor equal to <s>1 +(Prime/2)</s><b>the Flower Girl's Prime</b> <b>dots</b>.<br /> \u2022 Space: Those who are Attuned know where everything is around them, they don't need to roll to find a path or trail. They add <b>the Flower Girl's</b> Prime dots to [s]R[/]<b>r</b>oll<b>s</b> requiring precise movement though space.<br /> \u2022 Time: The Attuned's memories become sharp and clear. They don't need to roll to remember. They add<b> the Flower Girl's</b> Prime dots to rolls to predict consequence and to rolls to understand the Consequences of their actions.<br /> <br /> From the Soul Plant comes special seeds. Every solar year, a number of seeds equal to the Flower Girl's dots in Life can be harvested. These seeds, when planted in a Ley Line that is connected to one of the ley lines from the original Garden, grows into a new Garden, with its own Node. New Ley Lines emerge from the new Node and the process continues. For the purposes of Attainments, these new Gardens are considered extensions of the original. The new Gardens only grow to an area as if they had added another Ley Line to the intersection. Many of these new Gardens attract caretakers, many of whom become Attuned Sleepwalkers over a extended period of time.-<i>(The seeds act as their own Ley Line, making a intersection if there was not one before, this only happens when the plant sprouts after being planted)</i><br /> <br /> If instead the seed is planted into the Flower Girl's Garden, it instead expands the radius of the Garden by one Ley Line.<br /> <br /> Edit: No one had anything to say so I\u2019m leaving it as is for attainments. I rather enjoyed making this, but I think I need a break for a while. So naturally I came up with a new legacy right after I thought of this. Brain, why do you hate me?<br /> Later: I\u2019m feeling a bit burnt out, I wouldn\u2019t expect anything until Sunday </div> </div> </div>I think this is fine, though if you really want the Echo I'd put it as the 5th Alternate instead of the new seeds.<br /> I'd also specify that only the original garden grows the seeds, otherwise the entire world would be covered in Gardens within a few years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 06-04-2021, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T19:25:26-07:00","id":1451001,"title":"","content":"The lore looks pretty solid and interesting. Apart from that, I think proindrakenzol already addressed the typos and Attainments pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T20:50:14-07:00","id":1451009,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much for your response! I have a hard time catching my mistakes, and this helps tremendously.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450992#post1450992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This should not appear until the final Attainment, this is a potent form of immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is probably nitpicking, but the Echo isn\u2019t supposed to be immortality of any form, or at least not one that every other mage can\u2019t access. You see the Echo is based around the bit of you that gets left in your Soul Stones when you create them, except the Garden is the Soul Stone. The only difference is that the Echo can effect the Garden, and will tend to it like the Flower Girl would.It remembers pretty much nothing besides the Garden, it might have few bits of personality left, but that\u2019s hardly consistent. I tried to imply what it was by the Echo chamber merit. It\u2019s still probably too powerful.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450992#post1450992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is fine, though if you really want the Echo I'd put it as the 5th Alternate instead of the new seeds.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think I\u2019m just going to remove the Echo from the attainments altogether and make a section on Mysteries and Story Seeds surrounding the Legacy. I have a few other ideas that wouldn\u2019t be covered by attainments, and I think it would fit in there with them.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450992#post1450992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also specify that only the original garden grows the seeds, otherwise the entire world would be covered in Gardens within a few years.</div> </div> </div> </div> Whoops. Yeah that\u2019s not supposed to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T03:40:57-07:00","id":1451034,"title":"","content":"I can't believe I didn't think of this earlier:<br /> <br /> Attuning to the Garden's Node could cause the Gardener's Nimbus tilt. This scales with the Flower Girl's Gnosis, encourages them to &quot;grow&quot; their Nimbus in ways that influence behavior towards what they want, and give certain Merits (the Nimbus ones) more weight.<br /> <br /> Also, I like the Echo idea a lot, you should definitely include a &quot;hey, sometimes this happens if the Flower Girl dies in her Garden&quot; or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 06-05-2021, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T09:31:59-07:00","id":1451060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1451034#post1451034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't believe I didn't think of this earlier:<br /> <br /> Attubing to the Garden's Node could cause the Gardener's Nimbus tilt. This scales with the Flower Girl's Gnosis, encourages them to &quot;grow&quot; their Nimbus in ways that influence behavior towards what they want, and give certain Merits (the Nimbus ones) more weight.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can't believe *<b>I* </b>didn't think of that. I even had a idea about projecting the nimbus through the Garden and never even thought about the Attuned. It's so perfect. I think I would make a way to regain the Nimbus Tilt if a Attuned wanted, outside of the Flower girls direct control. Maybe a meditation roll inside the Garden? Even sleepers could do it. Is being Attuned enough to make them a Sleepwalker? It technically does grant them power, just only while in the Node or Garden.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1451034#post1451034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I like the Echo idea a lor, you should definitely include a &quot;hey, sometimes this happens if the Flower Girl dies in her Garden&quot; or something.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks, will do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T09:49:57-07:00","id":1451063,"title":"","content":"Becoming Attuned to a Node isn't enough to make someone a Sleepwalker: Sleepwalker status requires some sort of innate supernatural ability, and being under the effects of a Node aren't &quot;innate&quot;.<br /> <br /> But, yes, it would make sense for anyone (including Sleepers) to be able to Attune using a Meditation or gardening roll.<br /> <br /> [edit]I just want to say how much I really love this Legacy's themes, you did a really good job, TempleBuilder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 06-05-2021, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T10:11:43-07:00","id":1451064,"title":"","content":"In order to make them a Sleepwalker, you would need to cast Stealing Fire with indefinite duration. Another option is for the Garden to offer a chance to gain the Fitful Slumber merit by completing some kind of challenging quest or requirement, something that symbolically drives the person to cultivate themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-05-2021, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T11:01:09-07:00","id":1451067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1451063#post1451063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming Attuned to a Node isn't enough to make someone a Sleepwalker: Sleepwalker status requires some sort of innate supernatural ability, and being under the effects of a Node aren't &quot;innate&quot;.<br /> <br /> But, yes, it would make sense for anyone (including Sleepers) to be able to Attune using a Meditation or gardening roll.<br /> <br /> [edit]I just want to say how much I really love this Legacy's themes, you did a really good job, TempleBuilder.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you, that really means a lot to me. Thanks everyone for everything, you are the best. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1451064#post1451064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Another option is for the Garden to offer a chance to gain the Fitful Slumber merit by completing some kind of challenging quest or requirement, something that symbolically drives the person to cultivate themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div> Absolutely using this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T13:47:23-07:00","id":1451074,"title":"","content":"Final quality check:<br /> <br /> \u201cMages may Attune as normal, but Sleepers may make a meditation or gardening roll to Attune. Sleepers that successfully do this are granted a vision, a quest. Better themselves, and thus the world around them. Better the world, and thus better themselves. The quest is never easy, always requiring significant emotional investment, and confronting the worst in the world and in themselves and choosing to still try for a better outcome. Success for the quest relies on the Sleeper, no one can do the quest for them. The reward for all of this hardship is the Fitful Slumber Merit, which the Sleeper gains at the successful end of their quest. Failure removes the Attuned condition. Plants in the area automatically become Attuned.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIn addition, the Attuned may reflexively invoke the Flower Girl's nimbus tilt on themselves while in the Garden at the cost of one point of Willpower. The Flower Girl may instead pay one point of Mana to invoke on herself. All merits that effect the Nimbus apply.\u201c <br /> <br /> Are those good?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T14:04:33-07:00","id":1451075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1451074#post1451074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Final quality check:<br /> <br /> \u201cMages may Attune as normal, but Sleepers may make a meditation or gardening roll to Attune. Sleepers that successfully do this are granted a vision, a quest. Better themselves, and thus the world around them. Better the world, and thus better themselves. The quest is never easy, always requiring significant emotional investment, and confronting the worst in the world and in themselves and choosing to still try for a better outcome. Success for the quest relies on the Sleeper, no one can do the quest for them. The reward for all of this hardship is the Fitful Slumber Merit, which the Sleeper gains at the successful end of their quest. Failure removes the Attuned condition. Plants in the area automatically become Attuned.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIn addition, the Attuned may reflexively invoke the Flower Girl's nimbus tilt on themselves while in the Garden at the cost of one point of Willpower. The Flower Girl may instead pay one point of Mana to invoke on herself. All merits that effect the Nimbus apply.\u201c<br /> <br /> Are those good?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just go with:<br /> <br /> &quot;Attuning to the Node requires either casting the spell <i>Sacred Geometry</i> or successfully Meditating while under the guidance of someone with <i>Sacred Geometry </i>active or already attuned to the Node. Attuning to the Garden's Node grants the Attuned the benefits, and detriments, of the Flower Girl's Nimbus tilt for as long as they are in the area of the Garden. Additionally Sleepers substitute the Flower Girl's dots in Prime for the normal bonus provided by Meditation.&quot;<br /> <br /> This makes them more resistant to breaking points, which is the way Fitful Slumber is acquired.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-05T14:54:53-07:00","id":1451076,"title":"","content":"In which case, it might be a good idea 